INSERT INTO public.chef_kaggle_steps (recipe_id,position,instruction) VALUES
('20_Tips_to_Perfect_Macarons',1,'Place almond meal and powdered sugar in a food processor. Sift it and discard any big or remains that does not go thru. However, if you have a lot in the sifter - pulse some more and strain again. Tip - pulsing and staining will ensure you have a flour consistency. So do not skip this step.'),
('20_Tips_to_Perfect_Macarons',2,'Whip egg whites - Place the egg whites with cream of tartar in a grease-free bowl of a stand mixer with the whisk attachment. Start whisking on medium speed. (in the video I am using a hand mixer so you can see better but a stand mixer is ) Tip - the cream of tartar helps stabilize the egg whites. You can omit but it is especially helpful when making macarons in warm weather or humid places.'),
('20_Tips_to_Perfect_Macarons',3,'After a minute start adding the granulated sugar one spoon at a time.Tip - adding the sugar one spoon at a time will prevent the protein in the egg whites from breaking down. '),
('20_Tips_to_Perfect_Macarons',4,'Once all the sugar has been added - turn to medium-high and whip until stiff peaks. Add extract and food color - mix the color well.'),
('20_Tips_to_Perfect_Macarons',5,'Fold in - Next, fold the almond mixture into the whipped egg whites in three batches.'),
('20_Tips_to_Perfect_Macarons',6,'Macronage - once the almond mixture has been incorporated, we need to bring it to the right consistency. See video on how I do this. Use a spatula and spread the mixture around in the bowl - then bring it back to the center. Do it again and again until you have the right consistency. I usually have to do this about 4 to 5 times with each batch.'),
('20_Tips_to_Perfect_Macarons',7,'Consistency - you need, what is called a dropping consistency or a thick ''lava-like'' or ''cake batter'' consistency. This means when you hold a little batter on the spatula and it drops down like a ribbon that blends back into itself.Tip - getting the right consistency sometimes takes time. So, watch that part of a video carefully. '),
('20_Tips_to_Perfect_Macarons',8,'Pipe - Transfer batter into a piping bag with a large round tip (No.12). Pipe similar size macarons onto a parchment-lined baking tray using a template.Tip- templates ensure all shells are similar in size. This is helpful when we make the finished macarons. You can print free templates found on google or make your own with a cookie cutter. '),
('20_Tips_to_Perfect_Macarons',9,'Piping technique - The best way to pipe the macarons, hold the piping bag at 90%. Squeeze until you have a good mound then swirl the tip to one side. But don''t worry if you have a point,.When you tap the pan these usually settle down.'),
('20_Tips_to_Perfect_Macarons',10,'Tap baking pan - Tap the baking tray on the counter several times.Tip - Tapping helps so all the air pockets will rise to the top and release. That way you won''t have big holes in your macarons. I do three taps on each side as shown in the video.'),
('20_Tips_to_Perfect_Macarons',11,'Rest - Let the macarons sit in a cool dry place for about 30 to 50 minutes until it forms a skin on the top. If you touch the shell it should not stick to your finger. Tip -  In places, with high humidity, this can take up to 60 minutes. As long as it does not stick to your finger when you touch it - you are good to go.'),
('20_Tips_to_Perfect_Macarons',12,'While the macarons are drying - preheat the oven to 150 C / 300 F. Tip - I usually start my oven at about 20 minutes because that''s how long it takes in my home.'),
('20_Tips_to_Perfect_Macarons',13,'Bake the macarons for 12 to 15 minutes depending on your oven. (some ovens can take up to 18 minutes) The tops will look set but the bottom should not be wet. The top shell should be shiny and the bottom crusty (also called macaron feet).Tip - do not open the oven door for the first 10 minutes of baking. When you shake the pan they must look set. Remember they continue to bake with the residue heat on the baking tray. '),
('20_Tips_to_Perfect_Macarons',14,'Let the macarons rest in a cool dry place for about 15 to 20 minutes so the tops will get lightly crusted.'),
('20_Tips_to_Perfect_Macarons',15,'Cool on the baking tray for at least 10 minutes before you remove and transfer them to a cooling rack. Tip - trying to remove the macarons from the hot tray can cause the tops to separate from the bottom feet. Once you let them cool they will come off easily. So, be patient.'),
('20_Tips_to_Perfect_Macarons',16,'On a baking tray pair similar size macarons shells so you have similar size macarons'),
('20_Tips_to_Perfect_Macarons',17,'Add the filling in one piping bag and the buttercream in another bag. You can use a round piping tip but it''s not necessary.'),
('20_Tips_to_Perfect_Macarons',18,'Pipe a ring of buttercream on one macaron shell, then pipe the filling in the center of that buttercream ring. Place the second shell on top. Continue until you have filled all macarons.'),
('20_Tips_to_Perfect_Macarons',19,'Macarons must be stored in the refrigerator and are best eaten one or two days later. (if you can wait) '),
('20_Tips_to_Perfect_Macarons',20,'Enjoy!'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',1,'In a bowl, combine flour and salt – and set aside.'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',2,'In a measuring cup – measure the warm water, add olive oil, sugar, and yeast. Combine well.'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',3,'Add the yeast mixture to the flour mixture.'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',4,'Use a wooden spoon or spatula to combine it well making sure no dry flour is left on the bottom.'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',5,'This is a very wet dough, so don’t try touching it with your hand.'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',6,'Cover with a clean kitchen cloth or plastic wrap.'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',7,'Let on the countertop for an hour.'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',8,'Then, place in the fridge for 4 hours – up to 12 hours. I like to leave it overnight.'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',9,'Tip - Make sure the dough is well covered with plastic wrap so it does not dry out in the fridge.'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',10,'Preheat oven with pizza stone for at 200 C / 390 F for about 30 minutes.'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',11,'Remove the dough from the fridge.'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',12,'The dough will have become three times its size but still be very soft, sticky, and elastic with lots of air pockets.'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',13,'Dust your work surface generously with flour.'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',14,'Remove the dough on to the floured work surface. It is best to use a bench scraper or spatula.'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',15,'Divide the dough with a bench scraper. This dough makes three (for 3 x 12-inch thin-crust pizzas).'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',16,'Tip - Let the dough rest again for 10 to 15 minutes.'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',17,'Using a rolling pin, roll one piece of dough to about 12 inches (see video).'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',18,'Transfer pizza to a pizza pan or baking tray (or pizza peel). The video below uses a pizza pan.'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',19,'Tip - Place parchment paper on a pizza peel (parchment is less messy than cornmeal or flour).'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',20,'Tip - Let the base rest for 5 to 10 minutes - this will proof the base just a little which makes those edges puffy. (optional)'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',21,'Add all ingredients in a blender until smooth.'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',22,'Pour into a saucepan and cook on high for 2 minutes.'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',23,'You want the excess moisture to evaporate (see video).'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',24,'Let cool then use it on your favorite pizza.'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',25,'Tip - Brush the edges of the pizza with olive oil (this will give a nice golden crisp crust).'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',26,'Spread pizza sauce'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',27,'Sprinkle the parmesan, followed by the other cheeses ending with the mozzarella.'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',28,'Transfer the pizza to the preheated oven.'),
('3_Cheese_Pizza',29,'Bake for about 10 to 12 minutes until the edges are crisp and golden and the cheese is melted beautifully.'),
('3_Ingredients_Lemon_Ice_Cream_No_Churn',1,'Whip cream until almost stiff peaks.'),
('3_Ingredients_Lemon_Ice_Cream_No_Churn',2,'Add the condensed milk and mix a minute more to combine.'),
('3_Ingredients_Lemon_Ice_Cream_No_Churn',3,'Combine lemon curd well into the whipped cream mixture.'),
('3_Ingredients_Lemon_Ice_Cream_No_Churn',4,'I like to save a little of the whipped cream and fold it after I have combined the lemon curd. This creates a nice white and yellow swirl effect. '),
('3_Ingredients_Lemon_Ice_Cream_No_Churn',5,'Pour into an ice cream container and freeze for at least 4 hours or overnight.'),
('3_Ingredients_Lemon_Ice_Cream_No_Churn',6,'For the creamiest ice cream, thaw the container for at least 10 minutes before you attempt to scoop.'),
('3_Ingredients_Lemon_Ice_Cream_No_Churn',7,'Enjoy!'),
('4_Ways_to_Make_Homemade_Buttermilk',1,'Ensure the milk is at room temperature. If it’s cold it will not curdle, and it’s hot it will split.'),
('4_Ways_to_Make_Homemade_Buttermilk',2,'Add the lemon juice or vinegar. Stir and set aside for five minutes.'),
('4_Ways_to_Make_Homemade_Buttermilk',3,'After five minutes your buttermilk is ready. It will curdle and thicken more as it sits and that’s normal.'),
('4_Ways_to_Make_Homemade_Buttermilk',4,'Your buttermilk is now ready to use. This buttermilk will keep in the fridge for up to a week.'),
('4_Ways_to_Make_Homemade_Buttermilk',5,'Add a little milk to the yogurt and use a whisk to combine well.'),
('4_Ways_to_Make_Homemade_Buttermilk',6,'Then add the remaining milk and combine well. Leave to sit for 5 minutes.'),
('4_Ways_to_Make_Homemade_Buttermilk',7,'Your buttermilk is now ready to use. This buttermilk will keep in the fridge for up to a week.'),
('4_Ways_to_Make_Homemade_Buttermilk',8,'In a saucepan heat the milk until almost boiling. Let it cool to room temperature.'),
('4_Ways_to_Make_Homemade_Buttermilk',9,'Add the yogurt – use a whisk to ensure it''s well combined.'),
('4_Ways_to_Make_Homemade_Buttermilk',10,'Cover with a clean kitchen cloth and leave in a warm, dark place on the kitchen for 4 to 6 hours until thick and sour.'),
('4_Ways_to_Make_Homemade_Buttermilk',11,'Add more milk if the consistency is too thick. This buttermilk will keep for up to 2 weeks in the fridge.'),
('4_Ways_to_Make_Homemade_Buttermilk',12,'Place milk which is at room temperature (not cold) in a bowl.'),
('4_Ways_to_Make_Homemade_Buttermilk',13,'Add one packet yogurt starter and combine well with a whisk. (one sachet usually works for one-quart milk to make yogurt, buttermilk is thinner in consistency )'),
('4_Ways_to_Make_Homemade_Buttermilk',14,'Let sit for two minutes then stir well once again. Pour the cream into a mason jar.'),
('4_Ways_to_Make_Homemade_Buttermilk',15,'Cover with a lid and leave in a warm, dark place for up to 8 hours. Or until the milk is set and taste sour.'),
('4_Ways_to_Make_Homemade_Buttermilk',16,'Then place in the fridge for at least 3 hours before you use it. This buttermilk will keep for up to 3 weeks in the fridge.'),
('5_Spiced_Ginger_Tea_for_Cold_and_Sore_Throat',1,'Using a mortar and pestle again - coarsely grind the spices - set aside'),
('5_Spiced_Ginger_Tea_for_Cold_and_Sore_Throat',2,'Grate or smash the ginger in a mortar and pestle - set aside'),
('5_Spiced_Ginger_Tea_for_Cold_and_Sore_Throat',3,'Tip - I like using my mortar and pestle for this but since we are going to boil it, it does not matter whether you mince, grate, or chop it.'),
('5_Spiced_Ginger_Tea_for_Cold_and_Sore_Throat',4,'Add 4 cups of water in a saucepan.'),
('5_Spiced_Ginger_Tea_for_Cold_and_Sore_Throat',5,'Add the ginger and mixed spices in the saucepan.'),
('5_Spiced_Ginger_Tea_for_Cold_and_Sore_Throat',6,'Let come to a boil - once it comes to a boil - reduce heat'),
('5_Spiced_Ginger_Tea_for_Cold_and_Sore_Throat',7,'Simmer for 10 minutes until it is reduced to about 2 cups.'),
('5_Spiced_Ginger_Tea_for_Cold_and_Sore_Throat',8,'Use a mesh, sieve, or cheesecloth to strain into a jar or teapot.'),
('5_Spiced_Ginger_Tea_for_Cold_and_Sore_Throat',9,'This is the spice mixture and can be kept for about a week in the fridge.'),
('5_Spiced_Ginger_Tea_for_Cold_and_Sore_Throat',10,'Add ¼ cup of the spice mixture to your teacup'),
('5_Spiced_Ginger_Tea_for_Cold_and_Sore_Throat',11,'Top with 1 cup boiling hot water  (about 1:3 parts mix: water)'),
('5_Spiced_Ginger_Tea_for_Cold_and_Sore_Throat',12,'You can infuse with a tea bag (I drink it with as well as without tea bags)'),
('5_Spiced_Ginger_Tea_for_Cold_and_Sore_Throat',13,'Add 1 tbsp honey or more as you need.'),
('5_Spiced_Ginger_Tea_for_Cold_and_Sore_Throat',14,'Enjoy!'),
('Ahi_Tuna_Poke_Bowl',1,'Rice - Wash the rice in clean running water a couple of times until the water runs clear. Cook according to the package directions. And set aside.Pro tip - Generally, you would add 1 cup water and 1 cup rice in a pot. Let come to a boil. Then, turn the heat to a low simmer and cook for 15 minutes. Set aside until ready to serve.'),
('Ahi_Tuna_Poke_Bowl',2,'Ahi Tuna - Cut the tuna into small ½-inch cubes. And set aside.Pro tip - Ideally you want to make bite-size pieces of the tuna so you can pick it up with your chopsticks and eat. My kids are small so I make smaller pieces. '),
('Ahi_Tuna_Poke_Bowl',3,'Marinade - Combine all the marinade ingredients in a bowl. Then, add the chopped tuna, and combine well. Cover with plastic wrap and leave to marinate in the refrigerator for 2 hours. Two hours before serving, add the chilly flakes and sesame seeds.Pro tip - I like to add the chilly flakes and sesame seed shortly before serving. This way the chilly does not overpower in flavor and the sesame seeds don''t soak up the soy sauce. '),
('Ahi_Tuna_Poke_Bowl',4,'Sauce - Combine all the sauce ingredients in a bowl - mayo, rice vinegar, chili, and sesame oil.Pro tip - The color of your sauce will depend on the color of the sesame oil and the amount of chilly oil you use. '),
('Ahi_Tuna_Poke_Bowl',5,'Assemble - Fill a small bowl with steamed rice and invert it in the center of a bowl or plate. Surround it with all the remaining ingredients - tuna, cucumber, avocado, radishes, and lettuce or veggies. Top with some of the sauce. Pro tip - You can also serve this a la carte and let people make their own tuna poke bowl with the combination they like. '),
('Almond_Cream_Blackberry_Braided_Puff_Pastry',1,'Preheat the oven at 200 C/ 390 F.'),
('Almond_Cream_Blackberry_Braided_Puff_Pastry',2,'Almond cream filling - combine all ingredients in a bowl - set aside.'),
('Almond_Cream_Blackberry_Braided_Puff_Pastry',3,'Divide the puff pastry sheet into two. Roll each piece to a rectangle - 12 x 6-inches wide.'),
('Almond_Cream_Blackberry_Braided_Puff_Pastry',4,'Transfer to a parchment paper so it''s easier to move to the baking tray.'),
('Almond_Cream_Blackberry_Braided_Puff_Pastry',5,'Mark the pastry at 1 ½" from both edges lengthways (see vitrdeo).'),
('Almond_Cream_Blackberry_Braided_Puff_Pastry',6,'Cut off two corners (triangles) from the top and bottom - see video.'),
('Almond_Cream_Blackberry_Braided_Puff_Pastry',7,'Spread a generous amount of almond cream down the center (I prefer to use a piping bag).'),
('Almond_Cream_Blackberry_Braided_Puff_Pastry',8,'Then, spread a generous amount of jam over the almond cream mixture.'),
('Almond_Cream_Blackberry_Braided_Puff_Pastry',9,'Using a utility knife or pizza wheel, cut slanting strips along both sides of the pastry.');
INSERT INTO public.chef_kaggle_steps (recipe_id,position,instruction) VALUES
('Almond_Cream_Blackberry_Braided_Puff_Pastry',10,'Fold both ends at the top and bottom over the filling (this will prevent the filling from coming out when baking).'),
('Almond_Cream_Blackberry_Braided_Puff_Pastry',11,'Braid the pastry by crossing the strips over the filling overlapping each other (see video).'),
('Almond_Cream_Blackberry_Braided_Puff_Pastry',12,'When you reach the end, you can overlap any excess strips or cut them off.'),
('Almond_Cream_Blackberry_Braided_Puff_Pastry',13,'Pick the pastry with the parchment paper and transfer it to the baking tray.'),
('Almond_Cream_Blackberry_Braided_Puff_Pastry',14,'Brush the pastry with beaten egg.'),
('Almond_Cream_Blackberry_Braided_Puff_Pastry',15,'Bake in a preheated oven for 20 to 25 minutes, or until golden brown.'),
('Almond_Cream_Blackberry_Braided_Puff_Pastry',16,'Remove from the oven and let cool for at least 10 minutes - Do not try to transfer as the pastry may break and do not serve as the jam will be bubbling hot.'),
('Almond_Cream_Blackberry_Braided_Puff_Pastry',17,'Serve warm or room temperature.'),
('Almond_Crinkle_Cookies',1,'Preheat the oven to 170°C/ 340°F / Gas Mark 3'),
('Almond_Crinkle_Cookies',2,'Dry ingredients - combine flour, almond meal, baking powder, baking soda, and salt. Set aside. Pro tip- if you plan to sift add the almond meal after sifting or it won''t pass through the sifter. '),
('Almond_Crinkle_Cookies',3,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the paddle attachment, cream the butter and sugar until light and fluffy. '),
('Almond_Crinkle_Cookies',4,'Add the vanilla extract, followed by the flour mixture. It should make a soft dough but should be able to shape into balls. Pro tip - If necessary add a tablespoon or two of water if the dough is too dry. '),
('Almond_Crinkle_Cookies',5,'Using a spoon or cookie scoop, shape small golf size amounts of dough into balls.    Dip each ball in the powdered sugar. '),
('Almond_Crinkle_Cookies',6,'Place on a parchment-lined cookie tray leaving enough space for them to spread. (2 inches apart).'),
('Almond_Crinkle_Cookies',7,'Bake for 8 to 10 minutes on the center rack. Cool in the tray for five minutes then transfer to a cooling rack to cool further.Pro tip - depending on thickness they can take up to 12 minutes. The edges will start to color slightly.'),
('Almond_Crinkle_Cookies',8,'When cooled store in an airtight container for up to a week.'),
('Almond_Linzer_Cookies',1,'Dry ingredients - In a bowl combine flour, salt, cornflour, almond meal, and nutmeg together. Set aside'),
('Almond_Linzer_Cookies',2,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the paddle attachment, cream butter and sugar, until light and fluffy.'),
('Almond_Linzer_Cookies',3,'Add the egg followed by the vanilla and almond extract and flour mixture – combine well but don''t over mix'),
('Almond_Linzer_Cookies',4,'Divide dough into two discs and wrap in plastic wrap. Refrigerated for an hour or until firm enough to roll Pro tip - the dough is soft and needs to be refrigerated, so avoid adding more flour. '),
('Almond_Linzer_Cookies',5,'Preheat the oven at 170 C / 340 F'),
('Almond_Linzer_Cookies',6,'Roll the chilled cookie dough to about &frac18 inch in thickness on a lightly floured surface.Pro tip - it is best to roll these cookies thin or once you fill and sandwich them they will look bulky. I use a rolling pin with spacers so the dough is the same thickness all over.'),
('Almond_Linzer_Cookies',7,'Cut the cookiesFor the bottom cookies, cut out the disc using a Linzer cookie cutter without the center attachment. Alternatively, use a 3-inch round cookie cutterFor the top cookies, cut out the disc using the Linzer cooker cutter with the center attachment on.  Alternatively, use a 3-inch round cookie cutter combine with a 0.5 cookie cutter.'),
('Almond_Linzer_Cookies',8,'Bake - Place the cookies on a parchment-lined baking tray. Bake the cookies on the center rack for about 6 to 8 minutes.'),
('Almond_Linzer_Cookies',9,'Cool - Once baked cool on the cookie sheet for 10 mins then transfer them to a cooling rack to cool completely.'),
('Almond_Linzer_Cookies',10,'Sandwich the cookies - Place ½ tsp of jam or another filling of your choice on the bottom cookie. Dust the top cookies with powdered sugar then sandwich the two pieces togetherPro tip - It is better to dust the top cookies before you sandwich them to prevent sugar from getting into the filling. '),
('Aloo_Gobi___Sautéed_Cauliflower_and_Potatoes',1,'Using a sturdy chopping board and chefs knife cut potatoes into one-inch cubes. Separate the florets into similar size pieces as the potatoes. '),
('Aloo_Gobi___Sautéed_Cauliflower_and_Potatoes',2,'In a heavy bottom saute pan or skillet add oil on medium heat.  Saute the ginger and garlic for 30 seconds. '),
('Aloo_Gobi___Sautéed_Cauliflower_and_Potatoes',3,'Add onions and a pinch of salt. Saute until onions are translucent (about 2 minutes) '),
('Aloo_Gobi___Sautéed_Cauliflower_and_Potatoes',4,'Next, add the tomatoes, followed by the curry powder and garam masala. Combine well. '),
('Aloo_Gobi___Sautéed_Cauliflower_and_Potatoes',5,'Add 2 tbsp water and continue to cook on low for 3 to 5 minutes until you have a nice fragrant smell from the cooking spices. Tip - the water prevents the spices from burning. But, if you add too much it won''t cook the spices. '),
('Aloo_Gobi___Sautéed_Cauliflower_and_Potatoes',6,'Then, add the potatoes and cauliflower. Combine well. Season with salt and pepper. '),
('Aloo_Gobi___Sautéed_Cauliflower_and_Potatoes',7,'Cover and cook for about 10 minutes on medium-low heat - stirring often to ensure it does not stick to the bottom. Tip - vegetables will usually release enough liquid to cook but if necessary add ¼ to ½ cup to help cooking.'),
('Aloo_Gobi___Sautéed_Cauliflower_and_Potatoes',8,'When the cauliflower and potatoes are almost tender, cook open for another 10 minutes. Tip - We cook it open now so all the moisture will evaporate. Aloo gobi is usually a dry dish.  '),
('Aloo_Gobi___Sautéed_Cauliflower_and_Potatoes',9,'The potatoes and cauliflower should be cooked soft but still, hold their shape'),
('Aloo_Gobi___Sautéed_Cauliflower_and_Potatoes',10,'Finally, add the lemon juice and freshly chopped cilantro. Taste and adjust seasoning. '),
('Aloo_Gobi___Sautéed_Cauliflower_and_Potatoes',11,'Serve with roti on its own or as a side dish along with your main course. '),
('American_Buttercream_Frosting',1,'Use the bowl of a stand mixer with the paddle attachment. Combine the meringue powder, liquid creamer, and approximately two cups of powdered sugar. Pro tip - we make a meringue first this is what makes this buttercream different from other American buttercream recipes. '),
('American_Buttercream_Frosting',2,'Mix on medium-low for a minute - scraping the bowl as necessary. Add the vanilla extract and salt. Continue to mix for two to three minutes until you have a light and sticky consistency. Pro tip - It must look light and fluffy with a sticky appearance. This means the meringue powder has dissolved '),
('American_Buttercream_Frosting',3,'Next, gradually start adding the remaining powdered sugar. Continue to mix at medium speed. Pro tip - the mixture at the moment will be very dry and crumbly but continue to combine. You can add a tablespoon or more of cream but it is best to avoid at this point. '),
('American_Buttercream_Frosting',4,'Once all the sugar had been added and you have no dry powdered sugar, gradually start adding the butter one tablespoon at a time.   Pro tip - make sure that all the powdered sugar has been incorporated otherwise it will cause lumps in the butter. '),
('American_Buttercream_Frosting',5,'Once all the butter is in - run the mixer on high for about 3 to 5 minutes more. Whip until you have a light and fluffy, creamy velvety texture very similar to whipped cream.Pro tip - do not skip on the whipping as this is what will give us that whipped cream-like consistency. '),
('American_Buttercream_Frosting',6,'The buttercream consistency you get should be just right for piping swirls on cupcakes or decorating a buttercream cake. You can also use this buttercream for cakes that need to be covered with fondant. '),
('American_Buttercream_Frosting',7,'Stiff buttercream - If you find the buttercream is stiff, not peanut butter consistency when frosting or crumb coating - add a few tbsp of milk, cream, or even water to bring to the right consistency. Pro tip - Just like a meringue buttercream, it takes a while to incorporate the liquid but continue to mix well and it comes together beautifully. '),
('American_Buttercream_Frosting',8,'Colored buttercream - Food gel colors must be considered a liquid ingredient. If you plan to color your buttercream take that into account. I highly recommend you color the buttercream first then add more milk or cream to bring to consistency. '),
('American_Buttercream_Frosting',9,'Melt and cool the chocolate in a microwave or double boiler. Let cool to room temperature then carefully incorporate into the buttercream.  Pro tip- it is important that the chocolate is not warm when you add to the buttercream otherwise it will seize when combined with the cold buttercream. '),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',1,'Preheat the oven to 160 C / 320 F.'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',2,'Line your muffin pan with cupcake wrappers.'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',3,'Peel and core the apple then chop them finely'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',4,'Add 2 tbsp flour to the apples and set aside (this will prevent apples from sinking to the bottom of the cupcakes)'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',5,'Swift together – flour, baking powder, baking soda, salt, cinnamon & salt.'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',6,'Cream butter and sugar until light and fluffy.'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',7,'Add eggs one at a time.'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',8,'Followed by the vanilla extract'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',9,'Alternate the flour mixture and sour cream into the batter'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',10,'Scrape the bowl to ensure you have a smooth batter.'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',11,'Lastly, fold in the apples – do not over mix.'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',12,'Divide batter between the 12 cupcake wrappers'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',13,'Bake in a preheated oven at 160 C / 320 F for about 18 to 20 mins.'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',14,'Cool completely before you decorate.'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',15,'In a saucepan – add blueberries, sugar, salt and lemon juice.'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',16,'In a separate bowl – add cornstarch to 3 tbsp water (or use some of the blueberry juice) – set aside'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',17,'Place the saucepan on medium heat until all the sugar is dissolved.'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',18,'Add the cornstarch slurry – cook on low until thickened.'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',19,'You want the blueberry filling to be shiny and glossy not opaque.'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',20,'Cream together the butter and cream cheese.'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',21,'Add vanilla extract and salt'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',22,'Start adding powdered sugar one cup at a time.'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',23,'Mix well with each addition so you have a light and fluffy whipped cream-like consistency.'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',24,'Place the cream cheese frosting in a piping bag with a star tip.'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',25,'Once the cupcakes are cooled.'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',26,'Core out the center with an apple corer. (as shown in the video)'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',27,'Place a teaspoon of blueberry filling in the center.'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',28,'Pipe with cream cheese frosting (as shown in the video).'),
('Apple_Blueberry_Cupcakes_with_Cream_Cheese_Frosting',29,'Top with a fresh blueberry'),
('Apple_Honey_Tarte_Tatin',1,'Open the puff pastry and roll out to the size of your tart pan.  Use the tart pan as a guide and cut a disc'),
('Apple_Honey_Tarte_Tatin',2,'Place the pastry on a parchment paper and into the fridge to chill while you work on the apples.'),
('Apple_Honey_Tarte_Tatin',3,'Preheat the oven 200 C/ 400 F.'),
('Apple_Honey_Tarte_Tatin',4,'Peel, core, and cut the apples into 8 slices and add lemon juice to prevent them oxidizingTip - Cut each apple in half and then each half into two or three depending on the size of the apple'),
('Apple_Honey_Tarte_Tatin',5,'Spread the butter in the base of the oven-safe skillet. '),
('Apple_Honey_Tarte_Tatin',6,'Sprinkle the sugar, spice mix, and honey over the butter.'),
('Apple_Honey_Tarte_Tatin',7,'Arrange the apples over the mix.Tip-  Make sure to add more slices in between gaps as the apples will shrink as they cook.'),
('Apple_Honey_Tarte_Tatin',8,'Place pan on the stovetop on medium heat and cook for about 7 to 10 minutes. Shake the pan to ensure the butter and sugar combines and evenly caramelizes. '),
('Apple_Honey_Tarte_Tatin',9,'Using a tong, turn the apple slices over just flipping each one at about 6 minutes into cooking.'),
('Apple_Honey_Tarte_Tatin',10,'The apples will release their juices - then the juices will reduce and the sugar will start to caramelize.'),
('Apple_Honey_Tarte_Tatin',11,'As the color becomes a deep amber remove from heat and let cool for 5 minutes. Carefully rearrange the apples with a tong if necessary.'),
('Apple_Honey_Tarte_Tatin',12,'Carefully arrange the chilled puff pastry on the top of the apples tucking the sides in. Dock the puff pastry with the tings of a fork. '),
('Apple_Honey_Tarte_Tatin',13,'Place in the preheated oven and bake at 200 C/400 F for 10 minutes.'),
('Apple_Honey_Tarte_Tatin',14,'After 10 minutes - reduce the temperature to 180 C/360 F and bake further for 15 minutes.'),
('Apple_Honey_Tarte_Tatin',15,'When done the pastry will be a golden color and the sides will be bubbling with juices.'),
('Apple_Honey_Tarte_Tatin',16,'Remove from the oven and let sit on the countertop for at least 5 to 7 minutes.'),
('Apple_Honey_Tarte_Tatin',17,'Flip the pastry when the tart is still warm but not bubbling hot .Tip - The pan has very hot juices so please be very careful and use a gloved hand to do this quickly and without hesitation.'),
('Apple_Honey_Tarte_Tatin',18,'To do this safely - Chose the same size serving platter. Place it over the pan making sure to grip both the pan firmly. Then in one quick motion flip the tart onto the platter.Tip - the trick to any juices spilling out is to do it quickly. '),
('Apple_Honey_Tarte_Tatin',19,'Serve warm or room temperature just as is or with a dollop of ice cream on the sides.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',1,'Preheat oven to 190 C / 380 F.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',2,'Use an 8 x 8 square cake pan or a 7 x 9″ rectangle pan.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',3,'Chop butter into cubes.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',4,'In a food processor bowl – add flour, sugar, salt, vanilla, spice mix, and butter.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',5,'Pulse a few times – until crumbly. Not too much.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',6,'Pour into two separate bowls – one for the base and one for the top.');
INSERT INTO public.chef_kaggle_steps (recipe_id,position,instruction) VALUES
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',7,'I use a little extra for the base and less for the topping.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',8,'Keep the bowl for the crumble topping in the fridge to stay cold until ready to use.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',9,'Add the 2 tbsp of milk to the mixture for the base – mix to combine'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',10,'Then pour the mixture into the baking pan.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',11,'Use the back of a spoon to press it down firmly.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',12,'Bake in the preheated oven for 15 mins until lightly golden but not cooked thru.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',13,'Cool for 5 minutes.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',14,'Peel, core and chop the apple into small cubes'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',15,'Add the lemon juice and combine well – this will prevent discoloration.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',16,'Then add the sugar, honey, pumpkin spice, salt, nutmeg – mix well.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',17,'Lastly, add the flour and toss to combine.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',18,'Pour the apple pile filling over the baked base.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',19,'Spread evenly so every slice of crumble gets cherry filling in the middle.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',20,'Remove crumble topping from the fridge.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',21,'Evenly spread the topping all over the filling.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',22,'The more uneven the better it bakes.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',23,'Continue to bake in the oven for another 25 to 30 minutes or until lightly golden.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',24,'Cool completely.'),
('Apple_Pie_Crumble_Bars',25,'Once cooled cut into squares and serve.'),
('Apple_Pie_Hamantaschen_Cookies',1,'In a bowl, sift and combine together flour, cornstarch, baking powder, and salt.'),
('Apple_Pie_Hamantaschen_Cookies',2,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the paddle attachment, cream the butter and powdered sugar until light and creamy.Tip - do not cream too long, just until the sugar is melted, as we do not want to add too much air into our dough. '),
('Apple_Pie_Hamantaschen_Cookies',3,'Add the egg and egg yolk one at a time. Followed by the vanilla extract '),
('Apple_Pie_Hamantaschen_Cookies',4,'Next, add the flour mixture.  Combine well into a soft dough. Tip - you can combine the dry ingredients all at once.'),
('Apple_Pie_Hamantaschen_Cookies',5,'Divide the dough into two discs. Wrap well in plastic wrap and chill for at least 2 hours or until firm enough to roll.Tip - it is important to chill until the dough is firm enough to roll. Otherwise, it will be difficult to shape the cookies.'),
('Apple_Pie_Hamantaschen_Cookies',6,'Wash, core, peel and chop the apple into small pieces. Tip- since the filling is a small space on a 3-inch disc we want the pieces of apples to be small - I make mine less than ¼ inch pieces'),
('Apple_Pie_Hamantaschen_Cookies',7,'Add all filling ingredients in a heavy bottom saucepan. Heat on medium-low until the sugar melts and apples release their juices.'),
('Apple_Pie_Hamantaschen_Cookies',8,'The cornstarch will start to thicken the juices. Continue to cook on medium until almost all the juices are evaporated.Tip - it is important that all the juices have evaporated, otherwise you will have soggy cookies. The apples will continue to release some juices so take that into account.'),
('Apple_Pie_Hamantaschen_Cookies',9,'Take it off the heat. Let cool completely before filling in the cookies.Tip - it is important that the filling is cold, not hot when filling or it will warm the dough making it hard to shape. You can even put in the freeze for a quick chill. '),
('Apple_Pie_Hamantaschen_Cookies',10,'Roll the chilled cookie dough on a lightly floured surface to about &frac18 thickness.Tip -  You want the cookies thin enough so you can overlap the edges without cracking but thick enough so they won''t become too hard.'),
('Apple_Pie_Hamantaschen_Cookies',11,'Using a 3-inch or 3 ½ inch cookie cutter, cut as many discs as you can and place them on a baking tray.   Tip - Line the baking tray with parchment paper or silicone mat for easy clean-up. '),
('Apple_Pie_Hamantaschen_Cookies',12,'Add about a tablespoon of filling in the center. Tip -Do not add too much filling because the hot filling will force the cookies to open during baking. '),
('Apple_Pie_Hamantaschen_Cookies',13,'Dampen the disc edges very lightly with water or egg white Tip - you need just a dap of the water or egg whites otherwise it will be difficult to secure these folds'),
('Apple_Pie_Hamantaschen_Cookies',14,'Method one - Overlap the three corners as shown in the video. Fold the first two sides over at one end. Then overlap the third side under the first and under the second.Tip -At all times each side should be one under and one over the other. Sounds complicated but if you see the video it''s pretty simple.'),
('Apple_Pie_Hamantaschen_Cookies',15,'Method two - FInd the middle. Pinch two sides together, Bring the third side up and pinch to meet the other two sides. Tip - Press the folds gently, but firmly so they do not open during baking. '),
('Apple_Pie_Hamantaschen_Cookies',16,'Once all cookies are filled - chill them in the fridge while you preheat the oven.Tip - chilling the cookies will helps the cookies hold their shape better.'),
('Apple_Pie_Hamantaschen_Cookies',17,'Preheat the oven at  375 °F / 190 °C / Gas Mark 5'),
('Apple_Pie_Hamantaschen_Cookies',18,'Brush the cookies with egg wash. Bake for 10 to 12 minutes until the edges are lightly golden.'),
('Apple_Tart_with_Puff_Pastry',1,'Preheat the oven to 190 C/380 F.'),
('Apple_Tart_with_Puff_Pastry',2,'Open the chilled puff pastry and roll it the size of your tart pan.'),
('Apple_Tart_with_Puff_Pastry',3,'Line the tart pan with the pastry and cut off the excess. Press the side edges as we do not want flaky edges today. '),
('Apple_Tart_with_Puff_Pastry',4,'Score the pastry all over with the tings of a fork so it does not rise when cooking. Chill in the fridge while you prepare the apples.'),
('Apple_Tart_with_Puff_Pastry',5,'Peel, core, and slice the apples making 6 to 8 slices of each apple depending on the size of the apple.'),
('Apple_Tart_with_Puff_Pastry',6,'Add the lemon juice, brown sugar, cinnamon, salt, and vanilla.  Mix well to coat the apple slices.'),
('Apple_Tart_with_Puff_Pastry',7,'Arrange the apple slices on the pastry  Try to pack them well because they will shrink when cooking.'),
('Apple_Tart_with_Puff_Pastry',8,'Cut the butter into small cubes and sprinkle them on top. '),
('Apple_Tart_with_Puff_Pastry',9,'Place the pan on a baking tray to catch any spare juices.'),
('Apple_Tart_with_Puff_Pastry',10,'Bake for about 30 minutes. Until the pastry is golden with bubbling juices.'),
('Apple_Tart_with_Puff_Pastry',11,'Let rest for at least 10 minutes so the juices thicken. '),
('Apple_Tart_with_Puff_Pastry',12,'Cut a strip of puff pastry. Place on a parchment-lined baking trayTip - Make sure to use parchment paper as the juices will drip off the rimless tart.'),
('Apple_Tart_with_Puff_Pastry',13,'Using a ruler, score a line an inch-away from the edges of the pastry. This will then bake as the tart''s rim.'),
('Apple_Tart_with_Puff_Pastry',14,'Arrange the apples on the inside of the lines you just created. Try to pack them closely as they will shrink when cooking.'),
('Apple_Tart_with_Puff_Pastry',15,'Bake at 190 C/ 380 F for about 20 to 25 minutes. '),
('Apple_Tart_with_Puff_Pastry',16,'Cool for at least 10 minutes to help the juices settle. '),
('Apricot_Beef_with_Couscous',1,'Preheat oven to 150 C / 300 F.'),
('Apricot_Beef_with_Couscous',2,'Using a sturdy cutting board and chefs knife cut lamb into bitesize pieces not too small.'),
('Apricot_Beef_with_Couscous',3,'Season with salt and pepper. Coat well in flour and dust off excess. Set aside'),
('Apricot_Beef_with_Couscous',4,'Add 2 tbsp olive oil to a cast-iron skillet or heavy-bottom saute pan and brown the meat on all sides; 3 to 5 minutes. Do not crowd the pan. If necessary do this is batches. Remove and keep warm'),
('Apricot_Beef_with_Couscous',5,'To the same pan, add the remaining oil and saute onion, garlic, and ginger until onions are translucent'),
('Apricot_Beef_with_Couscous',6,'Add the bay leaves and cinnamon stick. Return the beef back to the pan.'),
('Apricot_Beef_with_Couscous',7,'Followed by the crushed tomatoes, apricot jam, and lemon juice. Add the parsley and water. Season with salt and pepper.'),
('Apricot_Beef_with_Couscous',8,'Bring to a boil. Cover the pan with a lid or aluminum foil. '),
('Apricot_Beef_with_Couscous',9,'Transfer to the oven. Cook for about 1 ½ to 2 hours or until the beef is fork-tender.'),
('Apricot_Beef_with_Couscous',10,'Always ensure you have enough water so the meat has enough moisture to cook. If necessary add ¼ to ½ cup more.Tip - This has a thick sauce so don''t add too much water either.'),
('Apricot_Beef_with_Couscous',11,'If you do not want to use the oven. Continue to cook in the Dutch oven on the stovetop stirring frequently until meat is cooked through and become fork-tender - about 1 to 1 ½ hour'),
('Apricot_Beef_with_Couscous',12,'Always ensure you have enough water so the meat has enough moisture to cook. If necessary add ¼ to ½ cup more.'),
('Apricot_Beef_with_Couscous',13,'Alternatively, transfer to a slow cooker or crockpot, and cook until the meat is fork-tenderTip- You can cook for 6 to 8 hours on low or for 3 to 4 hours on high. Personally, I like cooking on low so the meat is moist, juicy and fork-tender'),
('Apricot_Beef_with_Couscous',14,'Instead of using a Dutch oven, saute everything in the instant-pot '),
('Apricot_Beef_with_Couscous',15,'Close the lid and steam valve of the instant pot. Cook on high pressure for 30 minutes. When done - release pressure naturally for 10 minutes.'),
('Apricot_Beef_with_Couscous',16,'Place instant couscous in a bowl. stir in the olive oil well.'),
('Apricot_Beef_with_Couscous',17,'Pour boiling water over the couscous. Cover with a lid and let sit for 10 minutes.'),
('Apricot_Beef_with_Couscous',18,'After 10 minutes fluff with a fork. Add cranberries or pomegranate and parsley.'),
('Apricot_Beef_with_Couscous',19,'Enjoy'),
('Apricot_Creme_Brulee_Recipe',1,'Preheat the oven to 300°F/ 150°C / Gas Mark 2'),
('Apricot_Creme_Brulee_Recipe',2,'Place a paper hand towel in a roasting pan with 6 x 4 oz ramekins Pro tip - the paper hand towel will prevent the ramekins from moving around - Set aside.'),
('Apricot_Creme_Brulee_Recipe',3,'Blanch Apricot - Wash apricot and score the skin with a knife before you blanch them. Place them in a pot of hot water. Let them simmer in the hot water for 2 to 3 minutes. You will see the skin just starts to peel off.  Immediately place them in a bowl of cold water.'),
('Apricot_Creme_Brulee_Recipe',4,'When cool enough to touch, peel them. Cut the fruit in half, remove seed and pulse the in a food processor until smooth. Strain through a sieve and set aside. Use the amount required in your recipe.Pro tip - straining through a sieve will remove the fruit fiber which will give a smooth velvety texture to the custard mixture. '),
('Apricot_Creme_Brulee_Recipe',5,'In a heavy-bottom saucepan over medium heat, bring the cream, vanilla bean scraping and salt to an almont boil. Pro tip  - to use a vanilla bean, split the bean in half lengthways, scrape the insides with the back of a knife and add it to the pan along with the bean.'),
('Apricot_Creme_Brulee_Recipe',6,'In a separate bowl combine egg yolks and sugar. Add apricot puree and whisk until light and fluffy.'),
('Apricot_Creme_Brulee_Recipe',7,'Pour the hot cream mixture gradually into the egg mixture a few tablespoons at a time stirring continuously.  Strain thru a sieve to remove any curdled eggs Pro tip - this is called tempering the eggs. It is important to pour the milk gradually to prevent the eggs curdling. '),
('Apricot_Creme_Brulee_Recipe',8,'Divide the mixture equally between the prepared ramekins. Place the roasting pan on a larger baking tray.'),
('Apricot_Creme_Brulee_Recipe',9,'Pour enough water in the roasting pan to come to almost ½ way up outside the ramekinsPro tip - this is called baking in a water bath. The water outside will create steam and bake the custard without curdling. '),
('Apricot_Creme_Brulee_Recipe',10,'Bake in a preheated oven for 30 to 40 minutes. Once baked - remove from the oven, cover with plastic wrap. Chill in the fridge for at least 3 to 4 hours or overnight (up to 3 days) '),
('Apricot_Creme_Brulee_Recipe',11,'When ready to serve, sprinkle about 1 to 1 ½ teaspoon granulated sugar over each ramekin.Pro tip - this step must be done before serving, otherwise, the caramal will soften in the fridge due to condensation. '),
('Apricot_Creme_Brulee_Recipe',12,'Spread evenly by swirling the ramekin in your hand. Shake off any excess and clean the rim.Pro tip - wipe the rim of the ramekin with a paper towel to remove any sugar, otherwise, you will have brunt sugar on the edges which do not give a clean finish.  '),
('Apricot_Creme_Brulee_Recipe',13,'Carefully caramelize the sugar using a blowtorch. The sugar should turn amber and smooth but also hard which cracks like glass when eating.Pro tip - Pass the flame of the blowtorch over the sugar in a circular motion to get a more even caramel color.'),
('Apricot_Crumble_Squares',1,'Preheat oven to 375 °F 190 °C / Gas Mark 5'),
('Apricot_Crumble_Squares',2,'Use an 8 x 8 square cake pan or a 7 x 9" rectangle pan.  Line it with parchment paper and make sure you have an excess at the edges so you can pick it out of the pan. Pro tip - I find the square pan makes 16 even squares. But, you can use any pan similar in size. '),
('Apricot_Crumble_Squares',3,'In a food processor - add flour, sugar, salt, vanilla extract, spice mix, and cold cubed butter. Pulse a few times - until crumbly. Not too much.Pro tip - we want a crumble with some small pieces and some large pieces of butter. These will give us a good texture and mouthfeel.'),
('Apricot_Crumble_Squares',4,'Pour the crumble into two separate bowls - one for the base and one for the top. Pro tip -  I use a little extra for the base and less for the topping. This gives a bit more structure to the base so the squares will hold better '),
('Apricot_Crumble_Squares',5,'Top crumble  - Keep the bowl for the crumble topping in the fridge to stay cold.Pro tip - the butter in the crumble must be chilled well when added on the top, otherwise, it will melt instead of bake like a crumble. '),
('Apricot_Crumble_Squares',6,'Base crumble  -  Add the 2 tbsp of milk to the crumble for the base and combine well. Then pour the mixture into the baking pan. Use the back of a spoon to press it down firmly. Pro tip - the milk makes sure the base is pressed firmly and does not crumble when we cut the squares so don''t omit it. '),
('Apricot_Crumble_Squares',7,'Bake the base for 10 mins until lightly golden but not cooked thru. Cool for 5 minutes. Pro tip - we want the base to be partially cooked so it is firm as a base, this way it won''t soak up all the filling juices and crumble apart. '),
('Apricot_Crumble_Squares',8,'Fresh Apricots - wash the apricots, score a cross on the bottom skin, and blanch them in hot water for three minutes. Then drop them in cold water so the skin peels off easily. Remove skin, chop them into smaller pieces. Pro tip - if using canned or frozen peaches please read the notes above for details. '),
('Apricot_Crumble_Squares',9,'In a bowl combine together the sugar, lemon juice, vanilla extract, salt, and cornflour to the apricots. The cornflour will help thicken those juices nicely. Pro tip - Do not prepare the filling too early. The apricots will give out all the juices and the juices will make the base too wet and soggy.'),
('Apricot_Crumble_Squares',10,'Pour the filling over the base and spread evenly.  Generously sprinkle the crumble top mixture all over the apricot filling  (saved in the fridge). I use my fingers but a spoon works too. Pro tip - the top does not have to be even, in fact, the more uneven it is the better the baked crumble topping. '),
('Apricot_Crumble_Squares',11,'Continue to bake in the oven for another 25 to 40 minutes until lightly golden. When done cool in the pan for at least 10 minutes. Pro tip - If left in the pan for too long the sides may get stuck. Just take a knife and run through the edges. '),
('Apricot_Crumble_Squares',12,'Cut into 16 to 18 squares. I  get about 16 squares from the square pan and about 18 squares from the rectangular panPro tip - the top is quite crumbly so do the best you can when cutting. A sharp long knife does a better job than a short blade. '),
('Apricot_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',1,'Mark an X on the bottom of the apricots. Then, blanch them in hot water for 5 minutes. Peel and remove but do not discard the seeds/pits. Roughly chop the fruits and set them aside.Pro tip - Marking an X on the fruit helps to peel them easily as the skin shrinks when blanching. '),
('Apricot_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',2,'Place two small ceramic plates in the freezer so we can use these to test the jam later. Alternatively, you can use a candy thermometer to check the doneness of the jam. '),
('Apricot_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',3,'In a heavy bottom pan, combine the chopped apricots (and a few kernels), sugar, salt, and lemon juice. Also, add the star anise and cinnamon stick if using. Pro tip - If you are using fruits with skin on, let the fruits macerate in sugar and lemon juice for a few hours before cooking. This softens the skin considerably. ');
INSERT INTO public.chef_kaggle_steps (recipe_id,position,instruction) VALUES
('Apricot_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',4,'Cook on medium heat until the sugar is dissolved. Then, turn the heat up and let the mixture come to a boil. Let it boil for two minutes on medium-high. Pro tip - Boiling the jam is important as it releases pectin from the skin and seed in fruits. '),
('Apricot_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',5,'Then, turn the heat to medium-low. The jam should still be simmering but at a low simmer, not bubbling. Use a vegetable masher to mash the fruit – so you have a smoother jam-like consistency.Pro tip - Mashing the fruit is optional, as the fruit will break down into smaller chunks similar to preserve as it cooks. However, mashing will give smoother consistency like jam. '),
('Apricot_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',6,'Continue to simmer for about 20 to 30 minutes more stirring often so it does not stick to the bottom of the pan. The jam will continue to thicken as well as deepen in color as it cools.Pro tip - The cooking time will depend on the quantity of the jam as well as the heat applied to it. It''s ok to cook a little longer but there must be a simmer for the fruit to release pectin.'),
('Apricot_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',7,'Remove one of the ceramic plates from the freezer. Place a teaspoon of jam on the cold plate. Pro tip - The cold plate will help cool the jam almost instantly and give you a good indication if the jam is ready. '),
('Apricot_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',8,'Set aside for 2 to 3 minutes then test with your finger. Simply move/push the jam with your finger. If it wrinkles/crinkles it means the jam is ready. And if not, let the jam cook a couple of minutes more and test again.Pro tip - You may need to test the jam on a ceramic plate more than once or a couple of times depending on how early you start checking.'),
('Apricot_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',9,'Alternatively, you can use a candy thermometer - the jam should reach 105 C / 221 F.Pro tip - I find the thermometer to be the easiest and fail-proof method to check for doneness. '),
('Apricot_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',10,'Optional - Just when you are ready to take the jam off the heat add a teaspoon of butter and stir well. Butter helps dissolve foam that accumulates on top of the jam. Pro tip - You don''t need more than 1 teaspoon of butter to help with the foam. It will also give you that glossy shine.'),
('Apricot_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',11,'Pour the jam into warm sterilized jars leaving ¼ inch space from the top. Use a clean sterilized knife or spatula to move the jam a bit – this will remove any air pockets.'),
('Apricot_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',12,'Place a piece of wax paper on the top before you place the lid on tightly. Clean the rim of the jar with a clean paper towel. Top the lid. Alternatively, use the lid with screw-on rings that come with the canning jars.'),
('Apricot_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',13,'Sterilize 4 x 8 oz (250 g) jars by washing them in hot soapy water or cleaning them in the dishwasher with a gentle cycle. Then, place them in the oven for 20 minutes at a low 284 F / 140 CPro tip-  I find the dishwasher does a good job of cleaning and the oven dries any excess moisture in the bottles.'),
('Apricot_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',14,'Note - Leave them in the oven until you are ready to use them (you can turn the oven off). Don’t forget to wash and sterilize the bottle lids as well.'),
('Apricot_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',15,'Place a rack in the bottom of a large stockpot. Fill half the pot with water. Bring the water in the pot to a boil on high heat.'),
('Apricot_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',16,'Lower the jars over the rack leaving enough space between the jars.Pro tip - The level of water should be at least an inch above the top of the jars. So if necessary pour more boiling water.'),
('Apricot_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',17,'Bring the water to a boil again. Cover the pot and process/simmer for 15 minutes.'),
('Apricot_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',18,'Then, carefully remove the jars from the stockpot and place them on a kitchen towel to absorb any excess moisture. Cool completely. Pro tip - The hot jars are very delicate so make sure to use tongs when taking them out and place them on soft towels to prevent them from breaking. '),
('Apricot_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',19,'Press the top of the lid to ensure the seal is tight – the lid should not move at all. Store in a cool dry place.'),
('Apricot_Peach_Jam___No_Pectin___3_ingredients_',1,'Mark an X on the bottom of the apricots and peaches. Then, blanch them in hot water for 5 minutes. Peel and remove but do not discard the seeds/pits. Roughly chop the fruits and set them aside.Pro tip - Marking an X on the fruit helps to peel them easily as the skin shrinks when blanching.  '),
('Apricot_Peach_Jam___No_Pectin___3_ingredients_',2,'Place two small ceramic plates in the freezer so we can use these to test the jam later. Alternatively, you can use a candy thermometer to check the doneness of the jam. '),
('Apricot_Peach_Jam___No_Pectin___3_ingredients_',3,'In a heavy bottom pan, combine the chopped fruit (and a few kernels), sugar, salt, and lemon juice. Also, add the star anise and cinnamon stick if using Pro tip - If you are using fruits with skin on, let the fruits macerate in sugar and lemon juice for a few hours before cooking. This softens the skin considerably. '),
('Apricot_Peach_Jam___No_Pectin___3_ingredients_',4,'Cook on medium heat until the sugar is dissolved. Then, turn the heat up and let the mixture come to a boil. Let it boil for two minutes on medium-high. Pro tip - Boiling the jam is important as it releases pectin from the skin and seed in fruits. '),
('Apricot_Peach_Jam___No_Pectin___3_ingredients_',5,'Then, turn the heat to medium-low. The jam should still be simmering but at a low simmer, not bubbling.  Use a vegetable masher to mash the fruit – so you have a smoother jam-like consistency.Pro tip - Mashing the fruit is optional, as the fruit will break down into smaller chunks similar to preserve as it cooks. However, mashing will give smoother consistency like jam. '),
('Apricot_Peach_Jam___No_Pectin___3_ingredients_',6,'Continue to simmer for about 20 to 30 minutes more stirring often so it does not stick to the bottom of the pan. The jam will continue to thicken as well as deepen in color as it cools.Pro tip - The cooking time will depend on the quantity of the jam as well as the heat applied to it. It''s ok to cook a little longer but there must be a simmer for the fruit to release pectin.'),
('Apricot_Peach_Jam___No_Pectin___3_ingredients_',7,'Remove one of the ceramic plates from the freezer. Place a teaspoon of jam on the cold plate. Pro tip - The cold plate will help cool the jam almost instantly and give you a good indication if the jam is ready. '),
('Apricot_Peach_Jam___No_Pectin___3_ingredients_',8,'Set aside for 2 to 3 minutes then test with your finger. Simply move/push the jam with your finger. If it wrinkles/crinkles it means the jam is ready. And if not, let the jam cook a couple of minutes more and test again.Pro tip - You may need to test the jam on a ceramic plate more than once or a couple of times depending on how early you start checking.'),
('Apricot_Peach_Jam___No_Pectin___3_ingredients_',9,'Alternatively, you can use a candy thermometer - the jam should reach 105 C / 221 F.Pro tip - I find the thermometer to be the easiest and fail-proof method to check for doneness. '),
('Apricot_Peach_Jam___No_Pectin___3_ingredients_',10,'Optional - Just when you are ready to take the jam off the heat add a teaspoon of butter and stir well. Butter helps dissolve foam that accumulates on top of the jam. Pro tip - You don''t need more than 1 teaspoon of butter to help with the foam. It will also give you that glossy shine.'),
('Apricot_Peach_Jam___No_Pectin___3_ingredients_',11,'Pour the jam into warm sterilized jars leaving ¼ inch space from the top. Use a clean sterilized knife or spatula to move the jam a bit – this will remove any air pockets.'),
('Apricot_Peach_Jam___No_Pectin___3_ingredients_',12,'Place a piece of wax paper on the top before you place the lid on tightly. Clean the rim of the jar with a clean paper towel. Top the lid. Alternatively, use the lid with screw-on rings that come with the canning jars.'),
('Apricot_Peach_Jam___No_Pectin___3_ingredients_',13,'Sterilize 4 x 8 oz (250 g) jars by washing them in hot soapy water or cleaning them in the dishwasher with a gentle cycle. Then, place them in the oven for 20 minutes at a low 284 F / 140 CPro tip-  I find the dishwasher does a good job of cleaning and the oven dries any excess moisture in the bottles.'),
('Apricot_Peach_Jam___No_Pectin___3_ingredients_',14,'Note - Leave them in the oven until you are ready to use them (you can turn the oven off). Don’t forget to wash and sterilize the bottle lids as well.'),
('Apricot_Peach_Jam___No_Pectin___3_ingredients_',15,'Place a rack in the bottom of a large stockpot. Fill half the pot with water. Bring the water in the pot to a boil on high heat.'),
('Apricot_Peach_Jam___No_Pectin___3_ingredients_',16,'Lower the jars over the rack leaving enough space between the jars.Pro tip - The level of water should be at least an inch above the top of the jars. So if necessary pour more boiling water.'),
('Apricot_Peach_Jam___No_Pectin___3_ingredients_',17,'Bring the water to a boil again. Cover the pot and process/simmer for 15 minutes.'),
('Apricot_Peach_Jam___No_Pectin___3_ingredients_',18,'Then, carefully remove the jars from the stockpot and place them on a kitchen towel to absorb any excess moisture. Cool completely. Pro tip - The hot jars are very delicate so make sure to use tongs when taking them out and place them on soft towels to prevent them from breaking. '),
('Apricot_Peach_Jam___No_Pectin___3_ingredients_',19,'Press the top of the lid to ensure the seal is tight – the lid should not move at all. Store in a cool dry place.'),
('Artichoke_Kale_Quiche___Crustless',1,'Spray a 9-inch pie pan or quiche panwith cooking spray and sprinkle with breadcrumbs. Twirl the pan so the breadcrumbs are evenly distributed. Shake off any excess. Pro tip - similar to dusting a cake pan with flour, the breadcrumbs will prevent the quiche from sticking to the pan. '),
('Artichoke_Kale_Quiche___Crustless',2,'Prepare Kale - Wash the kale in a clean large pot of water. Stir it around to release the grit. Lift it out of the water. Drain water. Repeat the process one or two more times until you have no grit and the water is clean. Chopped the Kale small. '),
('Artichoke_Kale_Quiche___Crustless',3,'Chop artichokes into thin slices - set aside'),
('Artichoke_Kale_Quiche___Crustless',4,'In a skillet over medium heat saute onion and garlic in oil. Add the artichoke - saute a minute. Then add the kale - saute for 3 to 4 minutes until cooked. Season with salt and pepper to taste. Set aside to cool slightly. Pro tip - it is important to ensure all the liquid is evaporated otherwise the quiche won''t set. '),
('Artichoke_Kale_Quiche___Crustless',5,'In a mixing bowl combine the ricotta and milk until smooth. Add the flour, followed by the eggs. Season with salt and pepper.Pro tip - use a whisk and break the eggs apart making sure everything is well incorporated. '),
('Artichoke_Kale_Quiche___Crustless',6,'Preheat the oven at 350°F/177°C/Gas Mark 4. '),
('Artichoke_Kale_Quiche___Crustless',7,'Spread the cooked kale filling  in the bottom of the pie pan (coated with breadcrumbs) Top with grated cheddar cheese.'),
('Artichoke_Kale_Quiche___Crustless',8,'Pour the ricotta cheese mixture evenly over the greens. Use a fork to help the mixture sink into the greens. Sprinkle the breadcrumbs. Grate with fresh nutmeg  Pro tip - alternatively, you can add the egg mixture to the Swiss chard mixture then pour it all into the pie pan. '),
('Artichoke_Kale_Quiche___Crustless',9,'Bake in a preheated oven  for about 30 minutes. The top should look set - the middle with a slight jiggle which sets as it cools.'),
('Artichoke_Kale_Quiche___Crustless',10,'Let the quiche rest for at least 20 minutes before you cut. This will help cool and you will have pretty slices.'),
('Asian_Skewer_Chicken',1,'In a glass or stainless bowl ( do not use aluminum or other metal), add all the marinade ingredients along with the chicken.'),
('Asian_Skewer_Chicken',2,'Combine well - cover and leave to marinate for 15 mins on the counter up to 3 hours in the fridge.'),
('Asian_Skewer_Chicken',3,'Thaw chicken an hour before cooking.'),
('Asian_Skewer_Chicken',4,'Soak bamboo skewers in water for 30 minutes (this prevents them from burning).'),
('Asian_Skewer_Chicken',5,'Skewer the chicken and set aside.'),
('Asian_Skewer_Chicken',6,'Put the remaining marinade and ¼ cup water in a saucepan or frypan.'),
('Asian_Skewer_Chicken',7,'Cook the marinade for 2 to 3 minutes until thick like syrup - set aside.'),
('Asian_Skewer_Chicken',8,'Cook the chicken on a hot grill, turning once every 2 minutes until cooked on all sides. About 4 to 5 minutes per skewer.'),
('Asian_Skewer_Chicken',9,'In the last two minutes, brush the chicken with the sauce. This adds a nice glaze.'),
('Asian_Skewer_Chicken',10,'Serve over steamed rice or noodles with the remaining sauce.'),
('Avocado_Salad',1,'In a bowl or mason jar, combine the lemon juice, sugar, salt, and olive oil. Use a whisk to combine well. '),
('Avocado_Salad',2,'Dice the cucumbers, tomatoes, and onions. Chop the avocado just before you are about to make the salad. '),
('Avocado_Salad',3,'In a salad bowl, combine the chopped veggies, cucumber, tomatoes, avocado, onions, parsley, and olives.'),
('Avocado_Salad',4,'Pour over the salad dressing combine well. '),
('Avocado_and_egg_sandwich',1,'Cut the avocado in half, remove the seed, and put the flesh in a bowl'),
('Avocado_and_egg_sandwich',2,'Use a fork to mash the avocado. '),
('Avocado_and_egg_sandwich',3,'Add the lemon juice and combine well. '),
('Avocado_and_egg_sandwich',4,'Grate the boiled egg'),
('Avocado_and_egg_sandwich',5,'Add the sour cream and chopped cilantro. '),
('Avocado_and_egg_sandwich',6,'Seaslon with salt and pepper'),
('Avocado_and_egg_sandwich',7,'Spread it on a sandwich bread slice and top with another slice. Cut into half and serve. '),
('Avocado_and_egg_sandwich',8,'You can also spread this on a tortilla, roll it up, slice it in half and serve. '),
('BEST_Chocolate_Mud_Cake_Recipe',1,'Grease and line and 8-inch round baking pan/pans'),
('BEST_Chocolate_Mud_Cake_Recipe',2,'Preheat oven at 160 C / 320 F'),
('BEST_Chocolate_Mud_Cake_Recipe',3,'Sift together the flour, baking powder, baking soda, cocoa powder, and salt. '),
('BEST_Chocolate_Mud_Cake_Recipe',4,'Melt butter and chocolate in a microwave-safe bowl. '),
('BEST_Chocolate_Mud_Cake_Recipe',5,'Add the sugars and stir until almost melted'),
('BEST_Chocolate_Mud_Cake_Recipe',6,'Next, add the vanilla followed by the eggs one at a time. '),
('BEST_Chocolate_Mud_Cake_Recipe',7,'Then add the buttermilk - combine well. '),
('BEST_Chocolate_Mud_Cake_Recipe',8,'Lastly, add the flour and mix until you have a smooth batter. A whisk works well for this. '),
('BEST_Chocolate_Mud_Cake_Recipe',9,'Pour the batter into your baking pan. '),
('BEST_Chocolate_Mud_Cake_Recipe',10,'Bake in a preheated oven for about 60 to 70 minutes or until a toothpick inserted into the center comes out clean.'),
('BEST_Chocolate_Mud_Cake_Recipe',11,'Cool and decorate with your favorite frosting.'),
('BEST_Chocolate_Mud_Cake_Recipe',12,'Mix the caramel into the velvet American buttercream until well combined. '),
('BEST_Chocolate_Mud_Cake_Recipe',13,'Pour the melted still warm chocolate over the buttercream and leave it alone. '),
('BEST_Chocolate_Mud_Cake_Recipe',14,'After 10 minutes stir it vigorously. (read note above) '),
('BEST_Coconut_Cake_Recipe',1,'Preheat oven to 320°F / 165°C/ Gas Mark 3'),
('BEST_Coconut_Cake_Recipe',2,'Grease and line baking pans - I used one 8-inch round cake panBut you can use 2 x 8-inch round cake pan, or 1 x 9-inch round cake pan, one 8 x 8-inch square pan '),
('BEST_Coconut_Cake_Recipe',3,'In the bowl of the stand mixer with the paddle attachment measure all ingredients except the desiccated coconut.Pro tip - for a one-bowl recipe always make sure the butter, eggs, and milk are at room temperature. Otherwise, the batter will be lumpy'),
('BEST_Coconut_Cake_Recipe',4,'Now, add in the desiccated coconut and combine well. Pro tip - we add the desiccated coconut last because we do not want to crush it also it will absorb moisture instantly. '),
('BEST_Coconut_Cake_Recipe',5,'Pour batter into your prepared baking pan or pans. Sprinkle some shredded coconut or almonds on top. Pro tip - if you plan to use this in a layer cake then do not add coconut or almonds as it will make leveling it difficult later. '),
('BEST_Coconut_Cake_Recipe',6,'Bake in the center of the oven for about 30 to 40 minutes or until the skewer inserted in the center comes out clean.Pro tip - if you bake in two separate pans the baking time will be reduced to about 20 to 25 minutes. '),
('BEST_Coconut_Cake_Recipe',7,'Cool in the baking pan for 5 minutes. Invert and cool on a wire rack completely before you decoratePro tip - it is very important that the cakes are completely cooled before frosting. Otherwise, the frosting will melt on the warm cakes. '),
('BEST_Coconut_Cake_Recipe',8,'In a bowl of a stand mixer or hand mixer, cream butter and half the sugar until light and fluffy.'),
('BEST_Coconut_Cake_Recipe',9,'Add the extract, followed by the coconut cream a little at a time. Then add the powdered sugar until you reach a filling consistencyPro tip - A filling consistency is softer than peanut butter. '),
('BEST_Coconut_Cake_Recipe',10,'Add all ingredients in a bowl of a stand mixer. Mix until light and fluffy.Pro tip - this is a one-bowl buttercream recipe so you must ensure that the butter is at soft room temperature otherwise the frosting will be lumpy. '),
('BEST_Coconut_Cake_Recipe',11,'Prepare simple syrup - cool completely before using.Pro tip- Simple syrup is just sugar water that has been boiled and cooled. Used to keep cake layers moist.'),
('BEST_Coconut_Cake_Recipe',12,'Using a bread knife or cake leveler cut the domes off the cake layers. Split the cake into two horizontally.  Brush both layers with simple syrup.'),
('BEST_Coconut_Cake_Recipe',13,'Fill the cake - Pip a buttercream dam (edge) on the cake layer. Top with a big dollop of coconut filing – spread evenly but within the piped buttercream dam/edge.Pro tip - a buttercream dam prevents the soft filling from oozing out of the sides of the cake. '),
('BEST_Coconut_Cake_Recipe',14,'Place the second layer back on top. Sprinkle the cake with desiccated coconut or powdered sugar as I have done, OR Frost the outside generously with coconut buttercream.'),
('BEST_EVER_Chocolate_Fudge_Cupcakes_with_Chocolate_Fudge_Buttercream',1,'Preheat the oven to 160 C / 320 F.'),
('BEST_EVER_Chocolate_Fudge_Cupcakes_with_Chocolate_Fudge_Buttercream',2,'Sift flour with salt, baking powder, and baking soda. Set aside.'),
('BEST_EVER_Chocolate_Fudge_Cupcakes_with_Chocolate_Fudge_Buttercream',3,'Prepare baking cups or cupcake wrappers in a muffin tray.'),
('BEST_EVER_Chocolate_Fudge_Cupcakes_with_Chocolate_Fudge_Buttercream',4,'Melt chocolate in a microwave safe bowl or double boiler until melted - Set aside to cool.'),
('BEST_EVER_Chocolate_Fudge_Cupcakes_with_Chocolate_Fudge_Buttercream',5,'Cream Butter and Sugar until light and fluffy.');
INSERT INTO public.chef_kaggle_steps (recipe_id,position,instruction) VALUES
('BEST_EVER_Chocolate_Fudge_Cupcakes_with_Chocolate_Fudge_Buttercream',6,'Add eggs one at a time scraping the sides of the bowl often.'),
('BEST_EVER_Chocolate_Fudge_Cupcakes_with_Chocolate_Fudge_Buttercream',7,'Next sour cream and flour mixture in three batches.'),
('BEST_EVER_Chocolate_Fudge_Cupcakes_with_Chocolate_Fudge_Buttercream',8,'Add Vanilla followed by the melted and cooled chocolate.'),
('BEST_EVER_Chocolate_Fudge_Cupcakes_with_Chocolate_Fudge_Buttercream',9,'Use an ice cream scoop to distribute the batter evenly between 12 cupcakes wraps.'),
('BEST_EVER_Chocolate_Fudge_Cupcakes_with_Chocolate_Fudge_Buttercream',10,'Bake in a preheated oven for about 18 to 22 minutes or until the skewer inserted comes out clean.'),
('BEST_EVER_Chocolate_Fudge_Cupcakes_with_Chocolate_Fudge_Buttercream',11,'Chill Cupcake completely before you decorate.'),
('BEST_EVER_Chocolate_Fudge_Cupcakes_with_Chocolate_Fudge_Buttercream',12,'Melt chocolate in a microwave safe bowl or double boiler - Set aside to cool.'),
('BEST_EVER_Chocolate_Fudge_Cupcakes_with_Chocolate_Fudge_Buttercream',13,'Cream the butter, cream, and sugar until light and fluffy.'),
('BEST_EVER_Chocolate_Fudge_Cupcakes_with_Chocolate_Fudge_Buttercream',14,'Add Vanilla and cooled melted chocolate.'),
('BEST_EVER_Chocolate_Fudge_Cupcakes_with_Chocolate_Fudge_Buttercream',15,'Mix well to combine (if chocolate is not cooled it will seize in the buttercream).'),
('BEST_EVER_Chocolate_Fudge_Cupcakes_with_Chocolate_Fudge_Buttercream',16,'Place buttercream into a piping bag with your favorite piping tip and pipe a swirl.'),
('BEST_EVER_Chocolate_Fudge_Cupcakes_with_Chocolate_Fudge_Buttercream',17,'These cupcakes will stay at room temperature in good weather for up to 2 days.'),
('BEST_EVER_Chocolate_Fudge_Cupcakes_with_Chocolate_Fudge_Buttercream',18,'In the fridge for about 4 days if wrapped well.'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',1,'Preheat the oven to 160 C / 320 F.'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',2,'Prepare baking cups or cupcake wrappers in muffin pans.'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',3,'Sift together the flour, baking powder, baking soda, and salt'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',4,'Cream butter and sugar until light and fluffy.'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',5,'Add eggs one at a time scraping the sides of the bowl often.'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',6,'Followed by buttermilk and flour mixture'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',7,'Lastly, add in the Vanilla.'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',8,'Use an ice cream scoop to distribute the cupcakes evenly between 12 cupcakes wraps.'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',9,'Bake in a preheated oven for about 18 to 22 minutes or until the skewer inserted comes out clean.'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',10,'Let cupcakes cool completely but do not put them in the fridge.'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',11,'Place dulce de leche in a piping bag or ziplock bag.'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',12,'Make a small hole at the end of the bag.'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',13,'Using a melon baller make a hole in the center of the cupcake and fill the cavity with dulce de leche.'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',14,'Place cupcakes in the fridge to cool.'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',15,'Cream butter until light and fluffy.'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',16,'Add the powder sugar, continue to whip some more.'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',17,'Mix in the vanilla.'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',18,'Finally, fold the dulce de leche - Add half the dulce de leche and mix really well.'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',19,'When you add the other half, barely mix leaving streaks of the dark line in the frosting.'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',20,'Place buttercream into a piping bag with your favorite piping tip and pipe a swirl.'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',21,'Alternatively, use a spatula to create a dome on the cupcake.'),
('BEST_EVER_Dulce_De_Leche_Cupcakes_with_Dulce_De_Leche_Filling_and_Buttercream',22,'Enjoy!'),
('BEST_Ever_Pumpkin_Cream_Cake',1,'Preheat the oven at 325°F / 165°C / Gas Mark 3.'),
('BEST_Ever_Pumpkin_Cream_Cake',2,'Grease and line 3 x 7 inch round cakes or 2 x 8 inch round cake pans with parchment paper.'),
('BEST_Ever_Pumpkin_Cream_Cake',3,'Dry ingredients - Sift flour with baking powder, baking soda, pumpkin spice, nutmeg, and salt. Set aside.'),
('BEST_Ever_Pumpkin_Cream_Cake',4,'In the bowl of a stand mixer hand mixerwith the paddle attachment, cream butter and sugar until light and fluffy.Pro tip - We want to add some volume in the batter and the sugar completely dissolved so make sure to cream well.  '),
('BEST_Ever_Pumpkin_Cream_Cake',5,'Next, add eggs, one at a time. Followed by the pumpkin puree and vanilla extract.Pro tip - Ensure the eggs are at room temperature or the batter will curdle. If that happens, just add a tablespoon or two of flour and combine well. '),
('BEST_Ever_Pumpkin_Cream_Cake',6,'Then, add flour mixture and whipping cream alternating in three batches.Pro tip - Since whipping cream is thick the batter looks a bit stiffer than regular vanilla cake but the cream will melt in the oven so don''t add any more milk.'),
('BEST_Ever_Pumpkin_Cream_Cake',7,'Scrape the sides of the bowl, ensure you have a smooth batter. Then, divide the batter between the prepared baking pans.Pro tip - Use an offset spatula to spread the batter evenly in the pan so it bakes evenly. '),
('BEST_Ever_Pumpkin_Cream_Cake',8,'Bake for about 25 to 30 minutes until a skewer inserted in the center comes out clean.Pro tip - I like to use cake strips to ensure my layer cakes bake as flat as possible.'),
('BEST_Ever_Pumpkin_Cream_Cake',9,'Cool in the pan for 10 minutes. Then, invert on a cooling rack and cool completely. Always cool cakes completely before you decorate or store them away.Pro tip - Wrap in plastic wrap and place in the freezer for an hour. This will make fewer crumbs when torting and leveling the cake.'),
('BEST_Ever_Pumpkin_Cream_Cake',10,'In a stand mixer with a paddle the attachment, cream butter with salt for a minute. Then, gradually add the powdered sugar and vanilla extract'),
('BEST_Ever_Pumpkin_Cream_Cake',11,'Once all the powdered sugar is in, gradually add the whipping cream. Continue to whip until you have a light and fluffy whipped cream consistency (2 to 3 minutes).Pro tip - If you do not whip the consistency will be very soft. The whipping will add volume to the buttercream making it light and fluffy.'),
('BEST_Ever_Pumpkin_Cream_Cake',12,'Prepare simple syrup. Add sugar, water, and lemon juice to a saucepan over medium heat. Cook until sugar dissolves then boil two minutes more - cool completely before using.Pro tip - Simple syrup is used to keep cake layers moist.'),
('BEST_Ever_Pumpkin_Cream_Cake',13,'Using a bread knife or cake leveler, cut the domes off the cake layers. Then, cut each layer in half horizontally giving you a total of four layers. Brush each layer with the cooled simple syrup.'),
('BEST_Ever_Pumpkin_Cream_Cake',14,'Place a cake layer on the cake board or cake stand.pro tip - If you plan to move the cake again, it is best to use a cake circle under the cake, so you can pick the cake with its base and without any accidents.'),
('BEST_Ever_Pumpkin_Cream_Cake',15,'Filling - Top with a big dollop of the whipped cream buttercream – spread evenly with a straight-edged spatula. '),
('BEST_Ever_Pumpkin_Cream_Cake',16,'Top the second cake layer on top followed by more frosting until you have used up all the layers.Pro tip - It is best to lift individual cake layers on pieces of clean cardboard or cake lifter so you do not break them from table to cake.'),
('BEST_Ever_Pumpkin_Cream_Cake',17,'Place the cake in the fridge for 15 minutes so the layers hold together. Pro tip - Chilling the cake at this point will ensure the layers don''t move when you frost the outside. Though, if you leave the cake uncovered in the fridge for too long it can dry out. So, 10 minutes is all you need.'),
('BEST_Ever_Pumpkin_Cream_Cake',18,'Spread the remaining buttercream around and the top of the cake. Use a cake bench scraper to smooth the sides and an offset spatula for the top.'),
('BEST_Ever_Pumpkin_Cream_Cake',19,'Color ½ cup frosting with orange food color gel. Using a spatula place the orange frosting in little blobs all around the cake. Smooth with a bench scraper.Pro tip - You are looking for an almost smooth buttercream with a marbled effect. It''s easy to get carried away with this process but it''s best to not overdo this step.'),
('BEST_Ever_Pumpkin_Cream_Cake',20,'Finishing touches - I''ve used fondant pumpkins on this cake as shown in the video above. Alternatively, you can pipe remaining frosting on the top as well.'),
('BEST_Vanilla_Birthday_Cake_with_Vanilla_Buttercream',1,'Preheat the oven at 325 °F/ 165 °C/ Gas Mark 3.'),
('BEST_Vanilla_Birthday_Cake_with_Vanilla_Buttercream',2,'Grease and line 3×7 inch round cake pans or 2 x 8-inch round cake pans.'),
('BEST_Vanilla_Birthday_Cake_with_Vanilla_Buttercream',3,'In a bowl, combine the flour, baking powder, baking soda, and salt.'),
('BEST_Vanilla_Birthday_Cake_with_Vanilla_Buttercream',4,'In the bowl of a stand mixer, with the paddle attachment, cream butter and sugar until light and fluffy. Next, add the eggs, one at a time, followed by the vanilla extract.  '),
('BEST_Vanilla_Birthday_Cake_with_Vanilla_Buttercream',5,'Finally, add the flour and buttermilk in three batches. Scrape the sides and bottom to ensure you have a smooth batter.'),
('BEST_Vanilla_Birthday_Cake_with_Vanilla_Buttercream',6,'Divide the batter equally between the prepared baking pans. Pro tip - I like to use cake strips to ensure my layer cakes bake flat.'),
('BEST_Vanilla_Birthday_Cake_with_Vanilla_Buttercream',7,'Bake for 30 to 35 minutes or until a skewer inserted in the center comes clean.'),
('BEST_Vanilla_Birthday_Cake_with_Vanilla_Buttercream',8,'Cool in the baking pan for 5 minutes. Invert and cool on a cooling rack completely before you decorate.'),
('BEST_Vanilla_Birthday_Cake_with_Vanilla_Buttercream',9,'In the bowl of a stand mixer, with paddle attachment, cream butter and shortening for about 2 minutes, until light and fluffy.'),
('BEST_Vanilla_Birthday_Cake_with_Vanilla_Buttercream',10,'Next, add cornstarch to the hot water and add it to the creaming mixture. Pro tip - Add the water to the cornstarch at the time you want to add it in the butter. Otherwise, it will become lumpy. '),
('BEST_Vanilla_Birthday_Cake_with_Vanilla_Buttercream',11,'Continue to cream until it’s a smooth mixture again. Then, add vanilla extract and combine well.'),
('BEST_Vanilla_Birthday_Cake_with_Vanilla_Buttercream',12,'Finally, start adding the powdered sugar one cup at a time. Once all the sugar is in – whip the buttercream for a good three minutes until light and fluffy.Pro tip - It is important to whip so you have a whipped-cream like consistency. Otherwise, the buttercream will be too soft to spread. '),
('BEST_Vanilla_Birthday_Cake_with_Vanilla_Buttercream',13,'Prepare simple syrup – cool completely before using.Pro tip - Simple syrup is just sugar and water boiled for 3 minutes. It keeps the cake layers moist.'),
('BEST_Vanilla_Birthday_Cake_with_Vanilla_Buttercream',14,'Once cooled, cut the domes off the cake layers using a serrated knife. Brush each layer with the cooled, simple syrup.'),
('BEST_Vanilla_Birthday_Cake_with_Vanilla_Buttercream',15,'Place a cake layer on the cake board or cake stand.Pro tip - If you plan to move the cake again, it is best to use a cake circle under the cake, so you can pick the cake with its base and without any accidents.'),
('BEST_Vanilla_Birthday_Cake_with_Vanilla_Buttercream',16,'Top with a big dollop of buttercream – spread evenly using a straight-edge spatula.'),
('BEST_Vanilla_Birthday_Cake_with_Vanilla_Buttercream',17,'Then, top the second cake layer on top followed by buttercream and the last cake.Pro tip - It is best to lift individual cake layers on pieces of clean cardboard or cake lifter so you do not break them from table to cake.'),
('BEST_Vanilla_Birthday_Cake_with_Vanilla_Buttercream',18,'Place the cake in the fridge to chill for 10 to 15 minutes. Pro tip - Chilling the cake at this point will ensure the layers don''t move when you frost the outside. Though, if you leave the cake uncovered in the fridge for too long it can dry out. So, 10 minutes is all you need.'),
('BEST_Vanilla_Birthday_Cake_with_Vanilla_Buttercream',19,'Spread the remaining buttercream around and top of the cake.Pro tip - A straight-edge spatula fo the top, an off-set spatula and bench scraper for the sides work better.'),
('BEST_Vanilla_Birthday_Cake_with_Vanilla_Buttercream',20,'Place the remaining frosting in a piping bag with a star tip. Pipe swirls on top of the cake.'),
('BEST_Vanilla_Birthday_Cake_with_Vanilla_Buttercream',21,'Decorate with sprinkles or as desired.'),
('Baileys_Chocolate_Martini',1,'Smear the martini glasses with melted chocolate (optional).'),
('Baileys_Chocolate_Martini',2,'Place all the ingredients in a cocktail shaker with ice. Give it a good mix.'),
('Baileys_Chocolate_Martini',3,'Drain the ice, and pour into individual cocktail glasses.'),
('Baileys_Chocolate_Martini',4,'Enjoy!'),
('Baked_Cajun_Chicken_Thighs',1,'Preheat the oven at 200 C/ 390 F.'),
('Baked_Cajun_Chicken_Thighs',2,'Clean and pat dry the chicken pieces.'),
('Baked_Cajun_Chicken_Thighs',3,'Place the chicken pieces in a 9 x 13-inch baking dish.'),
('Baked_Cajun_Chicken_Thighs',4,'Season the chicken pieces with salt and pepper.'),
('Baked_Cajun_Chicken_Thighs',5,'In a separate bowl, combine Cajun spice and brown sugar'),
('Baked_Cajun_Chicken_Thighs',6,'Brush the chicken liberally with the lemon juice and olive oil '),
('Baked_Cajun_Chicken_Thighs',7,'Then sprinkle liberally with the cajun spice mix on both sides.'),
('Baked_Cajun_Chicken_Thighs',8,'Bake in the preheated oven for 25 to 35 minutes or until done.'),
('Baked_Cajun_Chicken_Thighs',9,'Tip - Chicken is done when the internal temperature of the chicken reaches 165 F.'),
('Baked_Chicken_Drumsticks',1,'Thaw the chicken at least an hour before baking. Pat dry with a clean paper towel.Tip - Frozen or wet chicken will result in too much liquid in the finished dish, plus the marinade won''t stick to it. '),
('Baked_Chicken_Drumsticks',2,'Preheat the oven at 420 F / 215 C for at least 10 minutes before you add the chicken in. '),
('Baked_Chicken_Drumsticks',3,'Next, combine all the marinade spices in a bowl. And set aside.'),
('Baked_Chicken_Drumsticks',4,'Then, add the oil to the chicken drumsticks and coat well. Sprinkle the spices all over the chicken. '),
('Baked_Chicken_Drumsticks',5,'Line a baking tray with aluminum foil for easy cleanup. Spray or brush the foil with oil.Tip - This chicken has wonderful pan juices, so make sure you have no holes in the foil. '),
('Baked_Chicken_Drumsticks',6,'Then, place the drumsticks on the baking tray. Do not crowd the pan. Tip - Alternatively, this marinated chicken can be kept in a bowl in the fridge for up to 12 hours. Thaw an hour before baking. '),
('Baked_Chicken_Drumsticks',7,'Bake the chicken for 40 to 45 minutes until the top is golden and the chicken is cooked through. When done, the internal temperature of the chicken should read 165 F. Tip - Chicken is done when you cut the inside and it is no longer pink and the juices will run clean.'),
('Baked_Chicken_Legs',1,'Thaw the chicken at least an hour before baking. Pat dry with a clean paper towel.Tip - Frozen or wet chicken will result in too much liquid in the finished dish, plus the marinade won''t stick to it. '),
('Baked_Chicken_Legs',2,'Preheat the oven at 420 F / 215 C for at least 10 minutes before you add the chicken in. '),
('Baked_Chicken_Legs',3,'Next, combine all the marinade ingredients in a bowl. And set aside.'),
('Baked_Chicken_Legs',4,'Line a baking tray with aluminum foil for easy cleanup. Spray or brush the foil with oil.Tip - This chicken has wonderful pan juices, so make sure you have no holes in the foil. ');
INSERT INTO public.chef_kaggle_steps (recipe_id,position,instruction) VALUES
('Baked_Chicken_Legs',5,'Then, place the chicken legs on the baking tray. Do not crowd the pan. Using a pastry brush, marinate the chicken on all sides.Tip - Alternatively, this marinated chicken can be kept in a bowl in the fridge for up to 12 hours. Thaw an hour before baking. '),
('Baked_Chicken_Legs',6,'Bake the chicken for 40 to 45 minutes until the top is golden and the chicken is cooked through. When done, the internal temperature of the chicken should read 165 F. Tip - Chicken is done when you cut the inside and it is no longer pink and the juices will run clean.'),
('Baked_Chicken_Potato_Casserole',1,'Preheat the oven at 325 °F / 165 °C / Gas Mark 3'),
('Baked_Chicken_Potato_Casserole',2,'Smear a 9 x 13 casserole or baking pan with olive oil. Alternatively, you can also use a cooking spray. Set aside. Pro tip - the oil will prevent the chicken and potatoes from sticking to the pan so make sure to be generous. '),
('Baked_Chicken_Potato_Casserole',3,'Thaw the chicken at least an hour before baking. Pat dry with a clean paper towel. Chop into 2-inch cubes - Set asidePro tip - Frozen or wet chicken will result in too much liquid in the finished dish'),
('Baked_Chicken_Potato_Casserole',4,'In a cup or bowl, combine milk and cream with onion powder, garlic powder, chicken bouillon, and cornstarch - set aside.Pro tip - you will need to stir the mixture again before adding it as the cornstarch will settle to the bottom. '),
('Baked_Chicken_Potato_Casserole',5,'Peel and chop potatoes into small 1-inch cubes. Set asidePro tip - if the potatoes are not small they will not cook at the same time as the chicken. '),
('Baked_Chicken_Potato_Casserole',6,'In the baking casserole add the chicken, potatoes, and chopped parsley. Season with salt and pepper and make sure it is well distributed in the pan. Pro tip - you can mix this directly in the baking casserole or use a separate mixing bowl. '),
('Baked_Chicken_Potato_Casserole',7,'Stir the milk and cream mixture one more time to mix the cornstarch again and evenly pour it all over the casserole.Pro tip - you can add flour instead of cornstarch which makes the gravy thicker. '),
('Baked_Chicken_Potato_Casserole',8,'Sprinkle with the three kinds of grated cheeses starting with Parmesan, Cheddar, and Mozarella. Top with more fresh herbs if desired. '),
('Baked_Chicken_Potato_Casserole',9,'Cover the casserole with foil and bake for an hour or until the potatoes are tender.   Pro tip - if the potatoes are cut small they will cook in an hour or they may take a few minutes longer. '),
('Baked_Chicken_Potato_Casserole',10,'Then remove the foil and bake further for 25 to 30 minutes until potatoes are fork-tender.Pro tip - cooking uncovered will evaporate excess moisture as well as give the cheese a lovely caramelized color on top. But, keep a close eye to not burn the cheese. '),
('Baked_Chicken_Potato_Casserole',11,'This is best served hot with a side salad or side-dish of sauteed veggies. '),
('Baked_Chicken_Potato_Casserole',12,'Leftovers can be reheated in the microwave, covered with a wet paper hand towel or kitchen cloth. Pro tip - The moisture in the paper towel helps hydrate the potatoes and chicken. '),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake',1,'Pre-heat the oven at 350°F / 177°C/ Gas Mark 3.'),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake',2,'Prepare pan - Wrap the outside of a 7inch springform pan in aluminum foil. We will also need a roasting rack larger than the springform pan. Pro tip - The aluminum foil will prevent water from entering the cheesecake while baking in a water bath.'),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake',3,'Melt chocolate - Break the chocolate into small pieces. Place in a microwave-safe bowl or double boiler. Melt at 50% power for one minute or more until melted. Set aside to cool slightly.Pro tip - It is important to do this now so the chocolate will cool otherwise the warm chocolate will seize into the batter. '),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake',4,'Crush the Graham cracker/biscuits in a food processor. Add sugar, and cocoa powder - combine well.  Then add the melted butter and stir to combine.Pro tip - You can also place them in a ziplock bag and use a rolling pin to crush them.'),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake',5,'Pour crumbs into the prepared springform pan. Use the back of your spoon or measuring cup to press the crumbs firmly to form a crust.Pro tip - Pressing down firmly will ensure a good base for the cheesecake and it won''t fall apart when you cut slices. '),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake',6,'Baked in the oven for 10 minutes. Once baked set aside to cool slightly. '),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake',7,'Reduce the oven temperature to  300°F / 150°C/ Gas Mark 2.'),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake',8,'In the bowl of a stand mixer, with the whisk paddle attachment, combine cream cheese and sour cream. Then, add the sugar. Followed by the cornflour and vanilla extract.Pro tip - The cream cheese must be at room temperature. Otherwise, the batter will be lumpy. If necessary, place a warm bowl on top of the cream cheese to help thaw faster. '),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake',9,'Add eggs one at a time making sure to incorporate each well.Pro tip - We want each egg to incorporate well but we do not want to incorporate too much air into the batter. Otherwise, the top will crack when baking. So, do not overmix. '),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake',10,'Finally, add in the melted chocolate and cooled coffee or espresso.Pro tip - If the chocolate is not cooled, it will seize when added to the batter and you will end up with small shards of chocolate in the batter. So, make sure the chocolate is room temperature.'),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake',11,'Double boiler - Pour the batter into the prepared springform pan over the baked crust. Place the springform pan in a deep baking pan or roasting rack.  Pour 2 cups of hot water into the roasting rack outside the springform pan. Pro tip - The water will create steam in the oven and prevent the custard-based cheesecake from drying out. '),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake',12,'Bake for 40 to 50 minutes until set. Remove from the oven and let cool for 30 minutes on the counter. Then, run a knife or spatula around the edge of the cake but do not remove it from the pan. Pro tip - As the cheesecake cools it will shrink slightly. Running the knife around will prevent any cracks on the top of the cheesecake. '),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake',13,'Cool for at least 4 hours or up to overnight in the fridge. Then, run a knife or spatula again and release it from the pan. Pro tip  - The cake must be cooled before you pour the chocolate glaze. Otherwise, the glaze will melt off the cake. '),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake',14,'Combine chocolate, cream, honey, and butter in a bowl. Melt in the microwave or double boiler'),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake',15,'Pour over the cheesecake and shake the pan to let it spread naturally toward the edges. Or, use an offset spatula to guide the glaze to drip over the edges. Chill the cheesecake for another hour at least so the glaze sets before you cut. '),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake',16,'Decorate with chocolate shavings or dust with cocoa powder.'),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake',17,'Enjoy!'),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Tart',1,'Pre-heat the oven at 350°F / 177°C/ Gas Mark 3.'),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Tart',2,'Melt chocolate - Break the chocolate into small pieces. Place in a microwave-safe bowl or double boiler. Melt at 50% power for one minute or more until melted. Set aside to cool slightly.Pro tip - It is important to do this now so the chocolate will cool otherwise the warm chocolate will seize into the batter. '),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Tart',3,'Crush the Graham cracker/biscuits in a food processor. Add sugar, and cocoa powder - combine well.  Then add the melted butter and stir to combine.Pro tip - You can also place them in a ziplock bag and use a rolling pin to crush them.'),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Tart',4,'Pour crumbs into a 9-inch tart pan. Use the back of your spoon or measuring cup to press the crumbs firmly to form a crust.Pro tip - Pressing down firmly will ensure a good base for the cheesecake and it won''t fall apart when you cut slices'),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Tart',5,'Chill in the fridge while you are preparing the batter.'),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Tart',6,'In the bowl of a stand mixer, with the whisk paddle attachment, combine cream cheese and sour cream. Then, add the sugar. Followed by the cornflour and vanilla extract.Pro tip - The cream cheese must be at room temperature. Otherwise, the batter will be lumpy. If necessary, place a warm bowl on top of the cream cheese to help thaw faster. '),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Tart',7,'Add eggs one at a time making sure to incorporate each well.Pro tip - We want each egg to incorporate well but we do not want to incorporate too much air into the batter. Otherwise, the top will crack when baking. So, do not overmix. '),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Tart',8,'Finally, add in the melted chocolate and cooled coffee or espresso.Pro tip - If the chocolate is not cooled, it will seize when added to the batter and you will end up with small shards of chocolate in the batter. So, make sure the chocolate is room temperature.'),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Tart',9,'Pour the batter into the prepared tart pan over the crust. Place the tart pan on a baking tray and place the baking tray in a roasting rack.  Pour 2 cups of hot water into the roasting rack, outside the baking tray (see video) Pro tip - The water will create steam in the oven and prevent the custard-based cheesecake from drying out. '),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Tart',10,'Baked on the center rack of the oven for about 30 to 35 minutes or until set but still slightly wobbly in the center. Cool for at least 2 hours before you add the topping.'),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Tart',11,'In the microwave-safe bowl or double boiler, combine the chocolate, cream, honey, and butter. Heat. until melted and smooth.  '),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Tart',12,'Pour over the cheesecake tart and shake the pan to let it spread naturally toward the edges. Pro tip - you can also use a spatula and create a swirl effect on the chocolate. Looks pretty!'),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Tart',13,'Chill the cheesecake for at least 4 hours, preferably overnight. Decorate with chocolate shavings or dust with some powdered sugar.'),
('Baked_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Tart',14,'Enjoy!'),
('Baked_Mango_Tart___Parisian_Flan',1,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the paddle attachment cream butter and sugar for just a minute until well combined. Add the vanilla extract, salt, and egg yolk. Combine well.Pro tip - we do not want to add too much air into our pastry so do not cream for too long.'),
('Baked_Mango_Tart___Parisian_Flan',2,'Add the flour and almond meal. Combine well but do not overmix. Pro tip - we do not want to activate any gluten so do not overmix. just combine until you have not dry flour. '),
('Baked_Mango_Tart___Parisian_Flan',3,'Make a disc and wrap it in plastic wrap. Chill the dough in the refrigerator for at least two hours, preferably overnight.Pro tip - this dough does need to chill until it is firm enough to roll otherwise it will be sticky when rolling needing excess flour which we want to avoid. '),
('Baked_Mango_Tart___Parisian_Flan',4,'When chilled roll on a lightly floured surface about 2 inches larger than the circumference of the tart pan or to about &frac18 inch thickness. '),
('Baked_Mango_Tart___Parisian_Flan',5,'Line the tart and trim excess dough at the edges. Use the trimming to patch any cracks or gaps that may be in the dough.Pro tip - this is a very forgiving dough so if you do break it, just patch it up with the trimmings.'),
('Baked_Mango_Tart___Parisian_Flan',6,'Chill for a minimum of 15 minutes.'),
('Baked_Mango_Tart___Parisian_Flan',7,'In a heavy-bottom saucepan, combine egg yolks and sugar. Add the cornstarch - combine well with a whisk'),
('Baked_Mango_Tart___Parisian_Flan',8,'Then, add the salt and vanilla extract. Followed by the cream and milk. Stirring constantly to avoid lumps. '),
('Baked_Mango_Tart___Parisian_Flan',9,'Place it on medium heat and stir continuously until thick and creamy.Pro tip - it is very important to keep the heat to medium-low and stir continously to prevent the milk scorching at the bottom. '),
('Baked_Mango_Tart___Parisian_Flan',10,'Add the mango puree - and combine well. Strain in a bowl through a sieve and cover with plastic wrap making sure the plastic touches the top surface of the cream.Pro tip - straining will remove any curdles eggs and give a smooth creamy texture. '),
('Baked_Mango_Tart___Parisian_Flan',11,'Let it cool to room temperature, then place in the fridge to chill.'),
('Baked_Mango_Tart___Parisian_Flan',12,'Preheat the oven at 375°F / 190°C/ Gas Mark 5'),
('Baked_Mango_Tart___Parisian_Flan',13,'Line the chilled dough with parchment paper. Pro tip – to ensure the parchment paper conforms to the shape of the pan – just crumple the paper into a ball with your hands. Open it up and the scrunched paper will behave itself.'),
('Baked_Mango_Tart___Parisian_Flan',14,'Fill the inside of the shell with pie weights (over the parchment paper). Bake for 15 minutes until the edges are lightly starting to brown. '),
('Baked_Mango_Tart___Parisian_Flan',15,' Reduce the oven temperature to 350 F /177 C/ Gas Mark 4'),
('Baked_Mango_Tart___Parisian_Flan',16,'Remove the pie weights and parchment paper. Then, fill the tart with pastry cream filling, using a spatula to smooth the top.'),
('Baked_Mango_Tart___Parisian_Flan',17,'Bake on the middle rack for 15 minutes. Then, cover the edges with a pie shield or aluminum foil to prevent the crust from getting too dark.Pro tip - While we want the blisters on the flan we also want to prevent the edges from getting burnt so make sure to cover the edges. '),
('Baked_Mango_Tart___Parisian_Flan',18,'Continue to bake for 10 to 15 minutes more until blistered on the top.'),
('Baked_Mango_Tart___Parisian_Flan',19,'Remove from the oven, and let cool. Then place in the refrigerator for at least 4 to 6 hours.'),
('Baked_Mango_Tart___Parisian_Flan',20,'This is a rich dessert and can be served on its own.'),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',1,'Preheat the oven at 190 C / 380 F.'),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',2,'Clean and wash the squash.'),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',3,'First cut a tiny slice off the bottom make sure each one stands on its own.'),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',4,'Then cut the top caps carefully such that they make lids.'),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',5,'Use a melon corer or teaspoon to remove the inside seeds carefully.'),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',6,'Place the squash pots in a baking tray.'),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',7,'Saute onions in cooking oil until translucent.'),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',8,'Add the ginger - saute another minute.'),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',9,'Then add the tomatoes and spices - cook for 2 minutes more.'),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',10,'Add ground meat and break the meat apart.'),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',11,'Cook on high so you dry out the juice.'),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',12,'Season with salt and pepper.'),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',13,'Lastly, add Lemon juice and parmesan.'),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',14,'Saute for two more minutes.'),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',15,'Check if the meat is done - taste and adjust seasoning. '),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',16,'Add fresh herbs and combine well.'),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',17,'Fill each squash with the meat using a small spoon.'),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',18,'Do not press too hard or when you cut the meat will look press like a cake.'),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',19,'Top each squash with a little bit of grated cheddar cheese.'),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',20,'Place the lids on lightly. '),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',21,'Add ¼ cup water to the baking pan outside the pots. This will help steam the pots.'),
('Baked_Meat_Stuffed_Squash_Pots_Recipe___Moroccan_Stuffed_Squash',22,'Place in a preheated oven. Bake uncovered for about 30 to 40 minutes.'),
('Baked_Potato_Chips',1,'Preheat the oven to 200 C/ 390 F.'),
('Baked_Potato_Chips',2,'Wash the potatoes well.'),
('Baked_Potato_Chips',3,'If you prefer, peel the potatoes ( I prefer to leave the potato skin on).'),
('Baked_Potato_Chips',4,'Slice them as thin as you can. The thinner the slices the crispier the chips.'),
('Baked_Potato_Chips',5,'Place them in a bowl.'),
('Baked_Potato_Chips',6,'Add olive oil, salt, pepper and any seasoning you want (such as rosemary, lemon, garlic, paprika).'),
('Baked_Potato_Chips',7,'Toss them around in the bowl. '),
('Baked_Potato_Chips',8,'Lightly spray two baking pans with cooking oil.'),
('Baked_Potato_Chips',9,'Line the potatoes in a single layer making sure they do not touch to prevent sticking.'),
('Baked_Potato_Chips',10,'Bake for about 15 to 20 minutes, turning them over ones at around 10 minutes.'),
('Baked_Potato_Chips',11,'If you have cut uneven slices (like me). Remove the ones that are done so they won''t burn.'),
('Baked_Potato_Chips',12,'Serve with a side of tomato sauce or accompanied with the main course. '),
('Baked_Potato_Wedges_aka_Oven_Fried_Potato_Wedges',1,'Preheat Oven at 210 C / 420 F.');
INSERT INTO public.chef_kaggle_steps (recipe_id,position,instruction) VALUES
('Baked_Potato_Wedges_aka_Oven_Fried_Potato_Wedges',2,'Peel and wash potatoes.'),
('Baked_Potato_Wedges_aka_Oven_Fried_Potato_Wedges',3,'Cut each potato cut in half. Then each half into three vertically.'),
('Baked_Potato_Wedges_aka_Oven_Fried_Potato_Wedges',4,'Keep in a bowl of water if not using them immediately to prevent oxidation.'),
('Baked_Potato_Wedges_aka_Oven_Fried_Potato_Wedges',5,'Drain the potatoes – leaving any excess moisture in there.'),
('Baked_Potato_Wedges_aka_Oven_Fried_Potato_Wedges',6,'Place potato wedges in a microwave-safe bowl. Heat in the microwave on high for 2 minutes. Toss them then cook 2 minutes more.'),
('Baked_Potato_Wedges_aka_Oven_Fried_Potato_Wedges',7,'Place potatoes in a pot of cold water and boil for approximately three minutes. They should be firm, not soft.'),
('Baked_Potato_Wedges_aka_Oven_Fried_Potato_Wedges',8,'Drain the potato wedges well on a paper towel – wipe excess moisture'),
('Baked_Potato_Wedges_aka_Oven_Fried_Potato_Wedges',9,'Season with oil, salt, pepper.'),
('Baked_Potato_Wedges_aka_Oven_Fried_Potato_Wedges',10,'Add and any seasoning you want -(such as paprika, garlic, rosemary, lemon). I used garlic powder and paprika today.'),
('Baked_Potato_Wedges_aka_Oven_Fried_Potato_Wedges',11,'Line a baking tray with baking parchment.'),
('Baked_Potato_Wedges_aka_Oven_Fried_Potato_Wedges',12,'Lightly spray the baking parchment with cooking spray to prevent sticking.'),
('Baked_Potato_Wedges_aka_Oven_Fried_Potato_Wedges',13,'Place potatoes on a baking tray.'),
('Baked_Potato_Wedges_aka_Oven_Fried_Potato_Wedges',14,'Bake for about 30 to 40 minutes turning them around once or twice as needed, until golden brown and crisp.'),
('Baked_Potato_Wedges_aka_Oven_Fried_Potato_Wedges',15,'I usually turn them over around 20 mins and keep a close watch over them towards the end because different ovens cook at different timings.'),
('Baked_Potato_Wedges_aka_Oven_Fried_Potato_Wedges',16,'Mine took about 35 minutes.'),
('Baked_Tandoori_Fish_in_Just_15_minutes',1,'Wash, Clean and pat dry the fish.'),
('Baked_Tandoori_Fish_in_Just_15_minutes',2,'Season with salt, pepper and lemon juice.'),
('Baked_Tandoori_Fish_in_Just_15_minutes',3,'In a separate bowl - mix all the rest of the ingredients.'),
('Baked_Tandoori_Fish_in_Just_15_minutes',4,'Give it a good mix.'),
('Baked_Tandoori_Fish_in_Just_15_minutes',5,'Add the fish - let marinate. You can leave this to marinate for a few minutes to an hour or even overnight.'),
('Baked_Tandoori_Fish_in_Just_15_minutes',6,'Preheat the oven to 200 C / 400 F.'),
('Baked_Tandoori_Fish_in_Just_15_minutes',7,'Line a baking tray with foil for easy cleanup.'),
('Baked_Tandoori_Fish_in_Just_15_minutes',8,'Spray some cooking oil to avoid the fish sticking.'),
('Baked_Tandoori_Fish_in_Just_15_minutes',9,'Place fish on the oiled foil.'),
('Baked_Tandoori_Fish_in_Just_15_minutes',10,'Baked in the preheated oven - on the middle rack.'),
('Baked_Tandoori_Fish_in_Just_15_minutes',11,'Fish takes about 15 minutes to cook.'),
('Baked_Za_atar_Chicken_Recipe',1,'Thaw the chicken at least an hour before baking. Pat dry with a clean paper towel.Tip - Frozen or wet chicken will result in too much liquid in the finished dish, plus the marinade won''t stick to it.'),
('Baked_Za_atar_Chicken_Recipe',2,'Grease a baking dish with oil. Place the chicken pieces in the baking dish.'),
('Baked_Za_atar_Chicken_Recipe',3,'In a small bowl, combine the za''atar spice, garlic and ginger powder, salt, pepper. Combine together. Add the lemon juice and olive oil - combine well.'),
('Baked_Za_atar_Chicken_Recipe',4,'Using a pastry brush, marinate the chicken on both sides.Tip - This marinated chicken can be kept in the fridge for up to 12 hours. Thaw an hour before baking.'),
('Baked_Za_atar_Chicken_Recipe',5,'Preheat the oven to 400 °F/ 200 °C/ Gas Mark 6.'),
('Baked_Za_atar_Chicken_Recipe',6,'Add the chopped onions and garlic cloves (optional) to the baking dish over the chicken.'),
('Baked_Za_atar_Chicken_Recipe',7,'Bake for 40 to 45 minutes until golden and bubbling and the chicken is cooked through. The internal temperature of the chicken should read 165 F when done.'),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Frosting',1,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the paddle attachment or hand mixer cream butter and shortening for about a minute minutes, until light and fluffy.Pro tip - the color of the butter will get lighter in color and will blend with the shortening completely. '),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Frosting',2,'Combine water with cornstarch, cocoa powder, and vanilla extract. Add it to the creaming mixture and whip until smooth. Pro tip - water will create a glue effect with the cornstarch when combined with the fat. It will also take away that starchy taste from the cornstarch'),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Frosting',3,'Next, start adding the powdered sugar one cup at a time. Once all the sugar is in - whip the buttercream for a good three minutes until light and fluffy.Pro tip - whipping for no less than 3 minutes will give a light and airy whipped cream consistency frosting. '),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Frosting',4,'This buttercream is ready to use. You can use it to frost cakes ad as well as cupcakes. Pro tip - if you have air pockets while frosting the cake, use a paddle motion with a spatula when frosting. This usually will take care of the air pockets. '),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',1,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the dough hook, combine milk, yeast, sugar, egg, egg yolks, sour cream, and vanilla. Tip - Use a whisk to combine well making sure there are no lumps'),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',2,'Then, add the flour and salt – combine well with a spatula.'),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',3,'Start the mixer on and knead until everything forms a nice ball. Then knead for 2 minutes more.'),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',4,'After 2 minutes, start adding the room temperature butter – one cube at a time. Knead until all the butter is incorporated. Then knead 2 minutes more.Tip -  The dough should now be beautifully soft, elastic, and shiny dough'),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',5,'Place in an oiled bowl and cover with plastic wrap or clean kitchen cloth. '),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',6,'Leave the dough to rise on the counter for an hour. Then place it in the fridge for another hour. Tip - The cold dough is easier to work with as the butter chills. You can leave this dough in the fridge for up to 12 hours. '),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',7,'Combine chocolate and butter in a microwave-safe bowl. Melt for a minute or more until all the chocolate is melted.'),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',8,'Leave at room temperature for the chocolate to cool. It works best if the chocolate cools but is still in spreadable consistencyTip - you can also place it in the fridge for a few minutes to chill until spreadable consistency'),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',9,'Combine the sugar and water in a saucepan. Heat on medium-low until all the sugar is melted.'),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',10,'Then, cool a minute more until syrup consistency. Set aside until ready to use.'),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',11,'Remove the dough from the fridge. Lightly dust a work surface with flour and roll the dough to a rectangle approximately 10 x 20 cm long.'),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',12,'Spread the chocolate over &frac23 of the rectangle.Tip - it is important that the chocolate is a spreadable consistency otherwise it will be messy'),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',13,'Fold the rectangle like a book. Start with the third that has no chocolate and fold it over the center half then bring the other side over the first (see video).Tip - when laminated you should have a chocolate layer between each layer. '),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',14,'Place it over a baking tray, cover with cling wrap and let chill for an hour or until just firm enough to work with. Tip - you dont'' want the chocolate to get too hard or it will shatter between the layers. So, approximately an hour is good. '),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',15,'Remove the dough from the fridge. You can divide the dough into two. Work with one portion at a time (place the other in the fridge).Tip - I like to roll it a bit bigger then divide it into two so I have two workable rectangles. '),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',16,'Roll the dough into a long rectangle strip of about 5 mm thickness, which will be about 10 x 25 cm long.'),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',17,'Divide the dough into triangles (as shown in the video). First, cut at every 4 -inches, then cut diagonally. This should give you two triangles  '),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',18,'Working with one triangle at a time, fold like a croissant. Start by stretching the triangle lengthwise creating a long tail. Then, roll like a jelly roll from the broader side towards the tail.'),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',19,'Place the shaped rugalach on a parchment-lined baking tray making sure to tuck the tail under. Cover with a clean kitchen cloth and let proof for an hour.Tip- the parchment paper also makes for easy clean-up.'),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',20,'Preheat the oven at 325 °F / 170 °C / Gas Mark 3Tip - it is best to start preheating the oven at about 45 minutes and make sure the oven is well preheated. '),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',21,'Egg wash - beat the egg and water together. Brush the proofed rugelach with this egg wash.'),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',22,'Bake for about 15 to 18 minutes or until lightly golden.'),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',23,'Brush with sugar syrup as soon as you take it out of the oven. Then transfer to a cooling rack to cool completely.Tip - the sugar syrup keeps these rugelach''s moist but do not add too much or they will be soggy. '),
('Bakery_Style_Chocolate_Rugelach',24,'Enjoy!'),
('Bakery_Style_Vanilla_Frosting',1,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the paddle attachment or hand mixer cream butter and shortening for about a minute minutes, until light and fluffy.Pro tip - the color of the butter will get lighter in color and will blend with the shortening completely. '),
('Bakery_Style_Vanilla_Frosting',2,'Combine water with cornstarch and vanilla extract. Add it to the creaming mixture and whip until smooth. Pro tip - water will create a glue effect with the cornstarch when combined with the fat. It will also take away that starchy taste from the cornstarch'),
('Bakery_Style_Vanilla_Frosting',3,'Next, start adding the powdered sugar one cup at a time. Once all the sugar is in - whip the buttercream for a good three minutes until light and fluffy.Pro tip - whipping for no less than 3 minutes will give a light and airy whipped cream consistency frosting. '),
('Bakery_Style_Vanilla_Frosting',4,'This buttercream is ready to use. You can use it to frost cakes ad as well as cupcakes. Pro tip - if you have air pockets while frosting the cake, use a paddle motion with a spatula when frosting. This usually will take care of the air pockets. '),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',1,'Preheat the oven to 160 °C/ 320 °F'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',2,'Grease and line 2 x 6-inch round baking pans with parchment paper. You can also make one 8-inch round cake (double the recipe for 2 x 8-inch round cakes) '),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',3,'Sift together - flour, baking powder, and salt - set aside'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',4,'Combine the milk and cream - set aside'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',5,'Separate eggs– ensure no yolks get into the whites.'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',6,'Egg whites - In the bowl of a stand mixer with the whisk attachment add the egg whites and cream of tartar. Start whipping on medium-low speed, then gradually add &frac13 of the sugar, one tablespoon at a time. Tip - we divide the sugar between the egg whites and the butter so add only &frac13 now.'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',7,'Once sugar is in continue whipping until soft speaks but still glossy. Remove egg whites and set aside.'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',8,'Creaming - Working quickly and using the same mixer bowl with paddle attachment this time (no need to wash). Cream butter and remaining sugar until light and fluffy.'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',9,'Add the egg yolk, vanilla, and almond extract.'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',10,'Next, add flour and milk in three batches. The mixture will be dense at this stage.'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',11,'Combine &frac13 of the whipped egg whites vigorously so it loosens the batter. FOLD the rest of the whites with a spatula by hand.'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',12,'Divide batter equally between the baking pans.  I prefer to use baking strips to avoid a dome.'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',13,'Bake on the middle rack for 20 to 25 minutes or until a skewer inserted into the center comes clean'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',14,'Let cool in the pan for 10 minutes. After 10 minutes invert onto a cooling rack.'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',15,'Watch the video of me making Italian meringue buttercream here'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',16,'Place egg whites, salt, and cream of tartar in the bowl of a stand mixer with the whisk attachment on medium speed. Once the meringue is at the soft peak stage - turn the mixer on low to avoid over mix and wait for the sugar to reach temperature'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',17,'Meanwhile, heat sugar and water in a heavy bottom light colors saucepan over medium heat. Once all the sugar is melted place a candy thermometer inside. Continue to boil until the sugar syrup reaches about 238 F on the candy thermometer (softball stage)Tip - using a heavy bottom will distribute heat evenly and prevent the sugar from caramelizing and a light-colored pan means you can see the color of the sugar and as you work.'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',18,'Turn the mixer on medium speed and start pouring the hot sugar syrup into the mixer bowl. The sugar should stream between the whisk and the edge of the bowl. Once all the syrup is in. Turn the mixer on high and whisk for about 3 minutes. The outside of the bowl will be hot at first and then be barely warm.'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',19,'When the meringue is cold and the bowl is not warm at all. Start adding the butter - one cube at a time. Tip - This is where 90% of meringue buttercreams fail DO NOT add butter if the meringue is still not cold.'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',20,'Once all the butter is in whip for another minute or two until you have a smooth and satin-like buttercream that light and fluffy. Add the vanilla and almond extract.'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',21,'Prepare simple syrup - cool completely before using.Tip- Simple syrup is just sugar water that has been boiled and cooled. Used to keep cake layers moist.'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',22,'Watch a video showing how I level, torte, and fill the cakes.Tip - Make sure the cakes are completely cold, otherwise the frosting will melt. Plus, the cakes are more delicate to handle. Chilling the cakes makes them easier to work with.'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',23,'Using a bread knife or cake leveler cut the domes off the cake layers. Then divide each layer in half horizontally so you have four layers (2 x 2 = 4 layers)'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',24,'Brush each layer with the cooled simple syrup'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',25,'Place a cake layer on the cake board or cake stand.  Top with a big dollop of buttercream - spread evenly using a straight-edge spatula.'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',26,'Place the cake in the fridge to chill for 10 to 15 minutes.Tip - Chilling the cake at this point will ensure the layers don''t move when you frost the outside. Though, if you leave the cake uncovered in the fridge for too long it can dry out. So, 10 minutes is all you need.'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',27,'Spread the remaining buttercream around and the top of the cake.Tip - A straight-edge spatula for the top, an off-set spatula, and a bench scraper for the sides work better.'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',28,'Place any remaining frosting in a piping bag with a star piping tip nozzle. Pipe buttercream little swirls all around the cake. The swirls are similar to those on a cupcake just smaller in size.'),
('Bakery_Style_White_Wedding_Cake',29,'The cake will stay fresh for up to four days at cool room temperature without frosting. Once frosted please keep it in the fridge. It can be frozen for a month or more.'),
('Balsamic_Glazed_Meatballs',1,'Combine all meatball ingredients in a bowl including the beaten egg.'),
('Balsamic_Glazed_Meatballs',2,'Make balls and set aside.'),
('Balsamic_Glazed_Meatballs',3,'In a saute pan or skillet, add oil and cook meatballs in batches on medium heat turning on all sides.'),
('Balsamic_Glazed_Meatballs',4,'Remove meatballs from the pan and set aside.'),
('Balsamic_Glazed_Meatballs',5,'To the same pan, add the stock, cook for 2 minute son medium-low heat, deglazing the pan as you cook.'),
('Balsamic_Glazed_Meatballs',6,'Then, add the red wine, balsamic vinegar, brown sugar - cook for 2 minutes until almost reduced to half.');
INSERT INTO public.chef_kaggle_steps (recipe_id,position,instruction) VALUES
('Balsamic_Glazed_Meatballs',7,'Now, add the butter and continue to cook a minute until all the butter is melted and the sauce looks glossy.'),
('Balsamic_Glazed_Meatballs',8,'Finally, return the meatballs back to the pan and cook for 5 minutes until the sauce is reduced to about half.'),
('Balsamic_Glazed_Meatballs',9,'Make sure to turn the meatballs around so they coat evenly with the sauce.'),
('Balsamic_Glazed_Meatballs',10,'The sauce gets thicker as it cools.'),
('Balsamic_Glazed_Salmon',1,'Take the salmon out of the refrigerator for at least 30 minutes to an hour. Cut it to size if necessary, pat dry with a paper towel. Then, season with just pepper. set asidePro tip - we do not use salt to season now as the soy sauce has salt as well. '),
('Balsamic_Glazed_Salmon',2,'Combine all marinade ingredients in a bowl. Add the salmon pieces and let marinate for 15 to 30 minutes turning once in between.Pro tip - The longer you marinate the darker the color of the salmon and the lesser the cooking time. I would not recommend it for more than an hour. '),
('Balsamic_Glazed_Salmon',3,'In a skillet add the oil, and place the salmon skin-side down. Season with salt and pepper. Pro tip - ensure the salmon is dry so the skin will crisp when added to the pan. '),
('Balsamic_Glazed_Salmon',4,'Cook for 3 minutes then flip the salmon and cook for 2 minutes on the second side. Pro tip - keep the heat on medium-high for the first 2 minutes this will give a nice crisp skin. '),
('Balsamic_Glazed_Salmon',5,'Then, remove from the pan and set aside.Pro tip - We remove it from the pan after a few minutes to prevent it from overcooking. Use a flat spatula to lift the salmon up and out of the pan. '),
('Balsamic_Glazed_Salmon',6,'To the same pan, add the remaining marinade along with the stock. Cook on low until it becomes thick and syrup consistency.Pro tip - the longer you cook the thicker the sauce will be. You want to keep a pouring consistency so. you can still continue to cook the salmon. '),
('Balsamic_Glazed_Salmon',7,'Return the salmon back to the pan. Baste the salmon with the sauce and continue to cook for 4 to 5 minutes more or until done.Pro tip - tilting the pan will help baste the salmon better. Try not to move the fillets much as they are delicate. '),
('Balsamic_Glazed_Salmon',8,'Taste and adjust seasoning. We have not added salt because soy salt has salt, but it is best to taste now and adjust accordingly.Pro tip - if you use low sodium soy sauce you may need an additional pinch of salt. But, taste first. '),
('Balsamic_Glazed_Salmon',9,'Remove from heat and let rest for 3 to 5 minutes before you serve.The recommended internal temperature for salmon is at medium of 145 F to 147°F or 60 to 63°C But, you can also serve it at medium-rare of about 122 to 127°F or  50 to 53°C (this is what I prefer to serve my salmon ) Pro tip - resting will continue to cook the salmon further so take that into account as well. '),
('Balsamic_Maple_Roast_Chicken',1,'Preheat the oven at 190C / 380 F.'),
('Balsamic_Maple_Roast_Chicken',2,'Clean and pat dry the chicken thoroughly. Remove any excess fat from inside. Season the inside of the chicken with salt and pepper '),
('Balsamic_Maple_Roast_Chicken',3,'Compound butter - In a small bowl combine the butter and all the other ingredients for the compound butter. '),
('Balsamic_Maple_Roast_Chicken',4,'Loosen the skin under the breast and gently fill the gap with compound butter. Brush any remaining butter over the chicken. '),
('Balsamic_Maple_Roast_Chicken',5,'Fill the bird''s cavity with the herbs, onion, lemon, and half garlic. Tie the legs with a butcher''s twine and tuck the wings under. Place the chicken in the roasting pan breast side up'),
('Balsamic_Maple_Roast_Chicken',6,'Marinade - In a bowl combine the balsamic marinade ingredients. Pour the marinade over the chicken. Place the remaining herbs in the roasting pan.'),
('Balsamic_Maple_Roast_Chicken',7,'Lastly, pour the chicken stock into the roasting pan, not over the chicken. Place the roasting pan in the oven.Tip- the stock in the pan will prevent the butter and maples syrup from burning in the oven'),
('Balsamic_Maple_Roast_Chicken',8,'Roast the chicken for 15 minutes at 220 C / 440 F – then reduce temperature to 180 C / 390 F. Bake for 80 to 90 minutes until the juices run clear basting the chicken every 15 to 20 minutes.Tip - basting gives the chicken a deeper color and more flavor from the balsamic and maple marinade'),
('Balsamic_Maple_Roast_Chicken',9,'As a guide, you bake the first 15 minutes at 220C/ 450 F, then calculate 20 minutes for every 1 lb or 500 grams chicken at 180 C/ 360 F. Of course, the best guide is until juices run clear or the internal temperature reaches 165 F / 75 C.Tip - The foolproof method would be to use a meat thermometer. The temperature should reach 165 F or 75 C in the thickest part of the thigh or 145 F in the breast.'),
('Balsamic_Maple_Roast_Chicken',10,'Remove the chicken from the oven and tent it with a foil –  Set aside'),
('Balsamic_Maple_Roast_Chicken',11,'To the same roasting rack with the remaining marinade. Remove any burnt and chard herbs.'),
('Balsamic_Maple_Roast_Chicken',12,'Add the baby potatoes and chopped fruits (peached, apples, and grapes). Add more fresh herbs.'),
('Balsamic_Maple_Roast_Chicken',13,'Bake for about 30 minutes or until fork-tender.  When done, remove from the pan with a slotted spoon leaving all the juices behind for the gravy.'),
('Balsamic_Maple_Roast_Chicken',14,'Place the rack on medium-low heat. Add the white wine and deglaze the pan'),
('Balsamic_Maple_Roast_Chicken',15,'Next, add the flour and cook until it becomes thick. If necessary add more stock or water. Strain through a sieve and pour into a sauce boat. '),
('Balsamic_Maple_Roast_Chicken',16,'Serve warm with chicken.'),
('Banana_Date_Smoothie',1,'Remove seeds from the dates.'),
('Banana_Date_Smoothie',2,'Place all ingredients in a blender and blend until smooth.'),
('Banana_Date_Smoothie',3,'Pour into individual serving glasses'),
('Banana_Date_Smoothie',4,'Enjoy'),
('Bavarian_Cream_Recipe',1,'In a small bowl, soak gelatin in 2 tbsp water - set aside to bloom for 5 min.'),
('Bavarian_Cream_Recipe',2,'In a hevy bottom saucepan, combine egg yolks, sugar, salt and cornstarch with a whisk. Scrape the vanilla bean and add it in (or add vanilla bean paste).Pro tip - the mixture will appear dry at first but it will cream as you continue to combine.'),
('Bavarian_Cream_Recipe',3,'Gently pour ½ cup whipping cream over whisking constantly to prevent lumps, followed by the milk. Pro tip - Make sure to scrape the sides of the pan to get any dry cornstarch pockets. '),
('Bavarian_Cream_Recipe',4,'Place the saucepan over medium heat and cook stirring constantly until the mixture thickens and comes to a boil. The custard is done when it is thick enough to coat the back of a spoon. Pro tip - It is important not to rush this process as we want the cornstarch to be cooked otherwise the mixture will thicken but taste starchy.'),
('Bavarian_Cream_Recipe',5,'Once the custard is ready, remove from heat and add the soaked gelatin. Combine until all the gelatin is dissolved.Pro tip - The heat in the pastry cream is enough to dissolve the gelatin so no need to place it on heat. '),
('Bavarian_Cream_Recipe',6,'Strain the custard into a clean bowl. Cover with cling wrap making sure the plastic touches the top surface to prevent skin. Chill on the counter until room temperature. Pro tip - Straining will remove any undissolved gelatin or curdled egg giving a smooth velvety finish to the bavarian cream. '),
('Bavarian_Cream_Recipe',7,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the whisk attachment, whip the remainig whipping cream to soft peaks.  Gently fold it into the cooled pastry cream as shown in the video. Pro tip - The pastry cream must be cool to room temperature. If warm, it will melt the whipped cream and you will lose volume. '),
('Bavarian_Cream_Recipe',8,'The Bavarian cream is ready to pour into individual serving cup as I have. You can also use 6 x 5 oz ramekins or similar dishes.Pro tip - I like to pour the Bavarian cream in a piping bag (without a tip) this makes it easier to pour and distribute evenly.  '),
('Bavarian_Cream_Recipe',9,'Transfer the dessert to the fridge to chill for at least 4 hours or preferably overnight. Pro tip - Place the dessert cups on a baking tray lined with a paper towel. The paper towel prevents them from moving and the baking tray makes it easier to move around.  '),
('Bavarian_Cream_Recipe',10,'Cook the blueberries, sugar, and half the water in a heavy bottom saucepan over medium heat for 3 to 4 minutes. Pro tip - Very high heat will evaporate all the liquid without helping the sugar dissolve, so be patient and cook gently. '),
('Bavarian_Cream_Recipe',11,'Combine the cornstarch with the remaining water and add it to the saucepan. Continue to cook stirring constantly.  Pro tip - It is important that the cornstarch comes to a boil and the mixture will go from opaque to transparent glossy. '),
('Bavarian_Cream_Recipe',12,'The mixture will thicken. Once it coats the back of your spoon, take it off the heat and transfer it to another bowl. Pro tip - For a sauce consitency you can pass it through  a sieve. This will remove the skin and fiber.'),
('Bavarian_Cream_Recipe',13,'Cook the strawberries, sugar, and half the water in a heavy bottom saucepan over medium heat for 3 to 4 minutes. Pro tip - Very high heat will evaporate all the liquid without helping the sugar dissolve, so be patience and cook gently. '),
('Bavarian_Cream_Recipe',14,'Combine the cornstarch with the remaining water and add it to the saucepan. Continue to cook stirring constantly.  Pro tip - It is important that the cornstarch comes to a boil and the mixture will go from opaque to transparent glossy. '),
('Bavarian_Cream_Recipe',15,'Once the mixture is transparent and glossy take it off the heat. Pour it through a strainer and use a flat spatula to press down as much of the fruit as possible. Cool until ready to use.Pro tip - Straining will remove the skin and fruit fiber giving us a smooth sauce consistency.'),
('Bavarian_Cream_Recipe',16,'Microwave - Chop the chocolate into small pieces and transfer to a microwave-safer bowl. Add the whipping cream and melt on high for a minute or more until smooth. Stovetop - Alternatively, you can also boil the cream in a saucepan and pour it over the chocolate. The heat in the cream is enough to melt the chocolate. Stir until smooth. '),
('Bavarian_Cream_Recipe',17,'Once chilled, top the Bavarian cream dessert with your favorite topping. Let chill in the fridge until ready to serve. Pro tip - Bavarian cream can also be served on its own without any fruit sauce or chocolate sauce. The vanilla Bavarian cream topped with a swirl of whipped cream is a classic found in many high-end restaurants. '),
('Bean_Paste_Recipe_for_Sugar_Flowers_or_Korean_Bean_Paste',1,'Soak bean in water overnight - 6 to 8 hours.'),
('Bean_Paste_Recipe_for_Sugar_Flowers_or_Korean_Bean_Paste',2,'Boil with 4 times the amount of water until tender - about an hour.'),
('Bean_Paste_Recipe_for_Sugar_Flowers_or_Korean_Bean_Paste',3,'Drain liquid from beans.'),
('Bean_Paste_Recipe_for_Sugar_Flowers_or_Korean_Bean_Paste',4,'Remove skin from each bean as much as possible.'),
('Bean_Paste_Recipe_for_Sugar_Flowers_or_Korean_Bean_Paste',5,'Place in a blender with a few tablespoons of the liquid from the boiling water.'),
('Bean_Paste_Recipe_for_Sugar_Flowers_or_Korean_Bean_Paste',6,'Pour into a mesh lined with cheesecloth.'),
('Bean_Paste_Recipe_for_Sugar_Flowers_or_Korean_Bean_Paste',7,'Firmly squeeze out all the liquid until you have a thick dry crumbly bean mass.'),
('Bean_Paste_Recipe_for_Sugar_Flowers_or_Korean_Bean_Paste',8,'In a bowl combine all ingredients.'),
('Bean_Paste_Recipe_for_Sugar_Flowers_or_Korean_Bean_Paste',9,'Starting from the bean mass add the flour, cornstarch, rice flour, light corn syrup, and oil.'),
('Bean_Paste_Recipe_for_Sugar_Flowers_or_Korean_Bean_Paste',10,'Combine well then add flavoring or extract.'),
('Bean_Paste_Recipe_for_Sugar_Flowers_or_Korean_Bean_Paste',11,'Wrap the bean paste in foil to prevent moisture from getting in.'),
('Bean_Paste_Recipe_for_Sugar_Flowers_or_Korean_Bean_Paste',12,'Place the foil in a steamer (see video).'),
('Bean_Paste_Recipe_for_Sugar_Flowers_or_Korean_Bean_Paste',13,'Cover and let steam for 10 minutes.'),
('Bean_Paste_Recipe_for_Sugar_Flowers_or_Korean_Bean_Paste',14,'Let cool in the foil for 10 minutes more.'),
('Bean_Paste_Recipe_for_Sugar_Flowers_or_Korean_Bean_Paste',15,'Then open foil and break into small pieces to cool completely.'),
('Bean_Paste_Recipe_for_Sugar_Flowers_or_Korean_Bean_Paste',16,'Knead the cool bean paste into a ball again.'),
('Bean_Paste_Recipe_for_Sugar_Flowers_or_Korean_Bean_Paste',17,'Place in a cling wrap to prevent drying out.'),
('Bean_Paste_Recipe_for_Sugar_Flowers_or_Korean_Bean_Paste',18,'Bean paste will stay in the fridge for up to a week.'),
('Bean_Paste_Recipe_for_Sugar_Flowers_or_Korean_Bean_Paste',19,'Can be frozen for a month.'),
('Beef_Brisket_in_Red_Wine_Gravy',1,'Combine all the rub ingredients in a bowl or mortar and pestle.'),
('Beef_Brisket_in_Red_Wine_Gravy',2,'Set aside until ready to use.'),
('Beef_Brisket_in_Red_Wine_Gravy',3,'Thaw the beef brisket, and remove any extra fat or sliver skin on top.'),
('Beef_Brisket_in_Red_Wine_Gravy',4,'Place the beef in a ceramic, glass, or plastic dish (do not use metal to marinate). I used my ceramic baking dish.'),
('Beef_Brisket_in_Red_Wine_Gravy',5,'Season generously with the brisket rub on all sides.'),
('Beef_Brisket_in_Red_Wine_Gravy',6,'Set aside to marinate for an hour on the counter or up to overnight in the fridge. Thaw an hour before cooking.'),
('Beef_Brisket_in_Red_Wine_Gravy',7,'Preheat the oven at 150 C / 300 F.'),
('Beef_Brisket_in_Red_Wine_Gravy',8,'Combine the wine, stock, and sugar and pour it into the baking dish besides the meat.'),
('Beef_Brisket_in_Red_Wine_Gravy',9,'Add some rosemary and thyme sprigs as well (see video).'),
('Beef_Brisket_in_Red_Wine_Gravy',10,'Cover with a foil and cook for 60 minutes.'),
('Beef_Brisket_in_Red_Wine_Gravy',11,'After 60 minutes, baste it and turn it over.'),
('Beef_Brisket_in_Red_Wine_Gravy',12,'Cover and cook for another 45 to 60 minutes or until the internal temperature of the meat reaches 180 F on a meat thermometer.'),
('Beef_Brisket_in_Red_Wine_Gravy',13,'The meat will continue to cook in the residue heat up to 200 - 220 F.'),
('Beef_Brisket_in_Red_Wine_Gravy',14,'Remove the brisket from the baking pan and tent with a foil.'),
('Beef_Brisket_in_Red_Wine_Gravy',15,'Let the meat rest for 30 minutes while you prepare the gravy.'),
('Beef_Brisket_in_Red_Wine_Gravy',16,'Pour the pan juices into a frying pan.'),
('Beef_Brisket_in_Red_Wine_Gravy',17,'Cook on medium-high until reduced to almost half.'),
('Beef_Brisket_in_Red_Wine_Gravy',18,'Add butter and honey.'),
('Beef_Brisket_in_Red_Wine_Gravy',19,'Continue to cook until thick like a gravy/syrup.'),
('Beef_Brisket_in_Red_Wine_Gravy',20,'Brush the brisket with the sauce before serving.'),
('Beef_Brisket_in_Red_Wine_Gravy',21,'Serve remaining gravy on the side.'),
('Beef_Chuck_Roast',1,'Trim excess fat from the beef chuck using a sharp pairing knife and sturdy cutting board. Using a butcher''s twine, tie the meat as shown in the video.Pro tip  - tieing the meat will keep the meat''s shape as it roasts. It does not have to be perfect just a few knots will do too. '),
('Beef_Chuck_Roast',2,'Using a mortar and pestle, mash the rosemary and thyme leaves. Alternatively, you can also put all these ingredients in a food processor and blend to a smooth paste. '),
('Beef_Chuck_Roast',3,'Add the garlic and salt, followed by the paprika, and cayenne. Mash to a coarse paste. Then, add the oil and pepper.  '),
('Beef_Chuck_Roast',4,'Marinate the meat well on all sides, making sure to get the top and bottom sides too.  Leave to marinate on the counter for an hour or overnight in the fridge. Thaw the meat at least an hour or two before cooking. '),
('Beef_Chuck_Roast',5,'Preheat the oven at 175°C / 350°F / Gas Mark 4'),
('Beef_Chuck_Roast',6,'Add 2 tbsp oil in the roasting pan (or skillet) over medium-high heat. Sear the beef on all sides turning with a tong. When done, remove from the pan.'),
('Beef_Chuck_Roast',7,'Place the beef on the roasting rack and add ½ cup water in the pan.Pro tip - this will prevent the oil and marinade from burning as it falls in the pan. '),
('Beef_Chuck_Roast',8,'Add a meat thermometer and set it to 135 F for medium-rare, 140 F for medium, or 145 F for medium-well. '),
('Beef_Chuck_Roast',9,'Roast on the middle rack until desired temperature - about 1 to 1 ½ hours. Mine took 1 hour 10 minutes to reach 135 F for medium-rare. Pro tip - The meat will continue to cook further with the residue heat in the meat. '),
('Beef_Chuck_Roast',10,'Remove from the oven and cover with an aluminum foil. ');
INSERT INTO public.chef_kaggle_steps (recipe_id,position,instruction) VALUES
('Beef_Chuck_Roast',11,'Move the meat to a serving platter and keep warm so you can use the pan juices for the gravy.'),
('Beef_Chuck_Roast',12,'Place the roasting pan over medium heat, add chopped onions and garlic. Saute until onions are translucent. Pro tip - we add onions for flavor but you can omit the onions if you don''t like them. '),
('Beef_Chuck_Roast',13,'Then, add the red wine and using a spatula deglaze scraping as much as you can from the pan. Pro tip - keep the heat on medium so the liquid does not evaporate too quickly. '),
('Beef_Chuck_Roast',14,'Next, add the flour and continue to cook until it thickens. Cook a minute more, then add the stock. Let it come to a boil and remove from heat. Pro tip  -  it is important to cook the flour for a while so it cooks before you add teh stock otherwise the gravy will taste starchy. '),
('Beef_Chuck_Roast',15,'Strain it thru a sieve or mesh. Pour the sauce in a sauceboat and serve it with the roast.'),
('Beef_Chuck_Roast',16,'Enjoy! '),
('Beef_Curry___Slow_Cooked',1,'Using a sharp chef''s knife and sturdy cutting board, trim excess fat and cut the beef into large bite-size cubes (about 2 inches). Set aside.Pro tip - don''t cut the meat into small pieces as the slow cooking will eventually shred it. '),
('Beef_Curry___Slow_Cooked',2,'In a pan or Dutch oven pot over medium heat saute onions in oil for about 5 to 7 minutes until lightly golden.Pro tip - the caramelized onions give this curry that depth of flavor so cook low and slow so it does not burn. '),
('Beef_Curry___Slow_Cooked',3,'Add the ginger and garlic - saute another minute. Then add the bay leaves,, spices (curry powder, cayenne, paprika, garam masala), and 2 tbsp of water. Pr tip -the water prevents the spices from burning. But, do not add too much we still need them to cook and become aromatic'),
('Beef_Curry___Slow_Cooked',4,'Once you can smell the wonderful spices - add the yogurt and meat. Season with salt and pepper. then add the lemon juice and make sure everything is well combined Pro tip - combine the yogurt well with the meat and cook on medium-low so it does not curdle. '),
('Beef_Curry___Slow_Cooked',5,'Bring to a boil over medium heat.'),
('Beef_Curry___Slow_Cooked',6,'Then, lower the heat to a simmer and cook on low for 1 to 1 ½ hours stirring occasionally. Add ¼ to ½ cup water if necessary to prevent it from sticking at the bottom.Pro tip - Depending on the cut of meat you use, it will take between 1 to 2 hours. For example, brisket takes me almost 2 hours, stew meat makes just 1 ½ hour or less'),
('Beef_Curry___Slow_Cooked',7,'When cooked to fork-tender, adjust gravy by adding a bit more water depending on how you going to serve it.Pro tip - If you serve it with chapati, naan, or roti - keep it thick. If you serve with rice, add a little water to make a gravy.'),
('Beef_Curry___Slow_Cooked',8,'Alternatively, transfer to a slow cooker or crockpot, and cook until the meat is fork-tenderPro tip- You can cook for 6 to 8 hours on low or for 3 to 4 hours on high. Personally, I like cooking on low so the meat is moist, juicy and fork-tender'),
('Beef_Curry___Slow_Cooked',9,'When done, sprinkle chopped fresh cilantro or parsley and give it one good stir.'),
('Beef_Curry___Slow_Cooked',10,'Enjoy!'),
('Beef_Enchilada_Pasta',1,'Boil the pasta in salted water until al dente. Save some of the cooking liquid for the sauce later.'),
('Beef_Enchilada_Pasta',2,'Brown the beef in oil breaking the meat apart - 2 minutes.'),
('Beef_Enchilada_Pasta',3,'Add onions and garlic and saute some more - 2 minutes.'),
('Beef_Enchilada_Pasta',4,'Add the enchilada sauce and tomato paste - cook for 5 minutes.'),
('Beef_Enchilada_Pasta',5,'Season with salt and pepper.'),
('Beef_Enchilada_Pasta',6,'Add cheeses and parsley - combine well.'),
('Beef_Enchilada_Pasta',7,'Taste and adjust seasoning.'),
('Beef_Enchilada_Pasta',8,'Finally, add the cooked drained pasta.'),
('Beef_Enchilada_Pasta',9,'Garnish with fresh parsley and more cheese '),
('Beef_and_Pepper_Stir_Fry',1,'Cut the onions into slices and then separate the layers. Similarly, cut the peppers into long ¼ inch strips - set aside '),
('Beef_and_Pepper_Stir_Fry',2,'Next, cut the beef into long, thin strips. we cut the beef into longer and thinner strips as they cook faster. Tip - Partially frozen beef cuts long and thin strips better than fully thawed soft beef. So, I cut when partially frozen and let it sit our until completely thawed'),
('Beef_and_Pepper_Stir_Fry',3,'Place all the marinade ingredients in a large bowl. Combine well then add the beef strips and mix well. Leave the beef to marinate for an hour if possible but not necessary.Tip - the beef can be left to marinate in the fridge overnight. Make sure to thaw at least an hour before cooking. '),
('Beef_and_Pepper_Stir_Fry',4,'Drain the beef from the marinade and save the marinade aside. We will add the marinade back later. '),
('Beef_and_Pepper_Stir_Fry',5,'Heat the wok on high and add one tablespoon of cooking oil. Add the ginger and garlic. Saute for 30 seconds.Tip - We don''t need too much oil as the marinade also has sesame oil. '),
('Beef_and_Pepper_Stir_Fry',6,' Then, add the drained beef. Cook on medium-high for about 2 minutes stirring continuously, preferably with a flat spatula.Tip - we stir continuously so the beef sears on all sides giving a nice color as well as crisp edges which taste nicer. '),
('Beef_and_Pepper_Stir_Fry',7,'Next, pour in the marinade and let it cook for another 2 minutes on high until all the liquid has evaporated and the beef is cooked. Remove the beef from the wok and set it aside. Tip - The marinade will help the beef cook further without drying out. '),
('Beef_and_Pepper_Stir_Fry',8,'To the same wok, add the remaining one tablespoon of oil. Add the onions and saute for two minutes. Then, add the pepper and saute for another 2 minutes until almost tender. Season with salt and pepper Tip - I like to season stir-fry veggies after they saute. This helps them retain moisture and stay crisp longer. '),
('Beef_and_Pepper_Stir_Fry',9,'Return the beef back to the pan. Combine the cornstarch with ¼ cup water and add it to the pan. Saute on high for a minute or two stirring continuously. Finally, add the cilantro and combine well. '),
('Beef_and_Pepper_Stir_Fry',10,'Check and adjust the seasoning. If necessary add more salt. Transfer to a serving platter. '),
('Beef_and_Pepper_Stir_Fry',11,'Enjoy!'),
('Beef_in_Red_Wine',1,'On a clean cutting board and using a utility knife, cut the beef into about 2-inch pieces.'),
('Beef_in_Red_Wine',2,'Season with salt and pepper.'),
('Beef_in_Red_Wine',3,'Then, dust with flour coating on all sides. Dust off excess.'),
('Beef_in_Red_Wine',4,'Add cooking 1 tbsp cooking oil to the Dutch-oven. '),
('Beef_in_Red_Wine',5,'Sear meat on medium-high. Do this in batches to prevent crowding. '),
('Beef_in_Red_Wine',6,'Turning to ensure it browns on all sides. Note - If the meat is stuck to the pan don''t force it to release. It means it still needs time to sear. Wait a minute then try again. '),
('Beef_in_Red_Wine',7,'Once all the meat is seared, take it out of the pan and set aside - keep warm.'),
('Beef_in_Red_Wine',8,'To the same pan, add remaining oil and the onions. '),
('Beef_in_Red_Wine',9,'Add a pinch of salt and sauté until onions are translucent.'),
('Beef_in_Red_Wine',10,'Then, add the garlic and ginger - sauté for another minute.'),
('Beef_in_Red_Wine',11,'Next, add the red wine and mustard paste.'),
('Beef_in_Red_Wine',12,'Deglaze the pan with a silicone spatula (or wooden spatula) - for about 2 minutes.'),
('Beef_in_Red_Wine',13,'Then, return the seared beef back to the pan.'),
('Beef_in_Red_Wine',14,'Add the stock and lemon juice - season with salt and pepper. '),
('Beef_in_Red_Wine',15,'Cover the pan and cook on medium to low heat (stovetop) for about 2 hours or until fork tender.'),
('Beef_in_Red_Wine',16,'Taste and adjust seasoning. '),
('Beer_Braised_Beef_Stew___Slow_Cooker',1,'Clean, and chop the veggies into large bite-size pieces (3-inches). '),
('Beer_Braised_Beef_Stew___Slow_Cooker',2,'Using a chef''s knife and sturdy cutting board, clean beef of any excess fat and cut into 3-inch chunks'),
('Beer_Braised_Beef_Stew___Slow_Cooker',3,'Season beef with salt, pepper, and toss in the flour – coat well.Tip - The flour gives these that toasted brown look and will help thicken the sauce later.'),
('Beer_Braised_Beef_Stew___Slow_Cooker',4,'In a skillet over medium heat sear the beef with oil on all sides.Tip - Cook 2 minutes on one side before you turn over. Then cook 2 minutes on the other side as well.'),
('Beer_Braised_Beef_Stew___Slow_Cooker',5,'Once the beef is browned remove from the pan and set aside'),
('Beer_Braised_Beef_Stew___Slow_Cooker',6,'To the same skillet - add a tablespoon more oil and saute the onion, ginger, and garlic. Remove and set aside'),
('Beer_Braised_Beef_Stew___Slow_Cooker',7,'To the same skillet add ½ cup stock or water and deglaze the pan - scraping all the caramelized bits.'),
('Beer_Braised_Beef_Stew___Slow_Cooker',8,'Add the veggies in the slow cooker or crock-pot followed by the onion mixture and deglazed juices and seared beef.  '),
('Beer_Braised_Beef_Stew___Slow_Cooker',9,'Add rest of the ingredients, tomato paste, brown sugar, dried or fresh herbs, paprika, remaining stock, and beer.'),
('Beer_Braised_Beef_Stew___Slow_Cooker',10,'Cook in the slow cooker or crockpot until the meat is fork-tender. You can cook for 6 to 8 hours on low or for 3 to 4 hours on high. Personally, I like cooking on low so the meat is moist, juicy and fork-tender'),
('Berry_Smoothie__Mixed_Berries_',1,'Blend all the ingredients except the honey in a blender until smooth.'),
('Berry_Smoothie__Mixed_Berries_',2,'Taste and adjust for sweetness. Add the honey if necessary. '),
('Berry_Smoothie__Mixed_Berries_',3,'Pour into individual serving glasses and garnish with fresh fruit or mint leaves. '),
('Best_Blackberry_Mousse',1,'Blend the blackberries in a food processor with ¼ cup hot water until smooth. Pro tip - The hot water will ensure the seeds blend too.'),
('Best_Blackberry_Mousse',2,'Strain through a sieve or mesh. Then add the sugar and salt. Combine well.Pro tip - straining thru a sieve will take away all the fiber and seeds which gives a nicer consistency for the mousse.'),
('Best_Blackberry_Mousse',3,'Optional - For a more concentrated flavor, this puree can be reduced to half in a saucepan over medium heatPro tip - if you choose to reduce the puree, you will need to double the number of blackberries in the recipe to make 6 servings.'),
('Best_Blackberry_Mousse',4,'Combine the gelatin with 2 tbsp of water. Let soak for 3 minutes then heat in the microwave for 30 to 40 seconds until completely dissolved. Let cool slightlyPro tip - if you have any white scum on top of the melted gelatin, take it out with a spoon.'),
('Best_Blackberry_Mousse',5,'Add the melted gelatin to the blackberry puree. The best way to do this is to add a few tablespoons of puree to the gelatin. Then combine the two.Pro tip - adding a little puree to the gelatin first will temper and prevent the gelatin from becoming lumpy.'),
('Best_Blackberry_Mousse',6,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the whisk attachment - whip the cream with vanilla extract until stiff peaks.'),
('Best_Blackberry_Mousse',7,'Then, gently combine the whipped cream and blackberry mixture until you have no more white streaks. This is your blackberry mousse ready'),
('Best_Blackberry_Mousse',8,'Divide the mousse evenly between 6 individual glasses. Pro tip - I like to pour the mousse into a piping bag and then pour it into the glasses. This makes it easier to pour and keeps the glasses clean.'),
('Best_Blackberry_Mousse',9,'Chill the mousse in the fridge for at least 3 hours - preferably 4 hours or overnight.'),
('Best_Blackberry_Mousse',10,'For garnish, you can top with whipped cream and blackberry. I used a fresh blackberry on each.'),
('Best_Blackberry_Mousse',11,'Enjoy!'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',1,'Preheat the oven to 325°F/ 165°C/ Gas Mark 3 '),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',2,'Grease and line 3 x 8-inch or 2 x 9-inch round baking pans'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',3,'Add coffee to the boiling water to dissolve and set aside to cool.'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',4,'Dry ingredients - In a bowl combine the flour, baking powder, baking soda, cocoa powder, and salt. Set aside'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',5,'Thaw eggs on the counter for 10 minutes or place in warm water for 5 minutes Pro tip - warm eggs will whip better than cold eggs and will reach the ribbon stage faster. '),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',6,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the whisk attachment whip the whole eggs. Pro tip - Start by whipping the eggs on low and increase the speed gradually to medium-high. This way the eggs will have a stronger structure and your baked desserts won''t skin in the oven. '),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',7,'Gradually add the sugar while whipping at the same time. Once all the sugar is in continue to whip for 2 to 3 minutes more.Pro tip - If the sugar is added too quickly it can cause the eggs to speckle or separate.  '),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',8,'The mixture will be about 3 to 4 times the original volume until you reach a ribbon stage consistency. Pro tip - ribbon stage is pale, thick, foamy batter. When you lift the whisk the batter falls down in ribbons. Hence the term ribbon stage. '),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',9,'Next, gradually add in the oil ­while whipping at the same time. Followed by the buttermilk, coffee, and vanilla extract. '),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',10,'Lastly,­ add in the flour in three batches – still using the whisk attachment. The batter will look deflated a bit and that''s ok. Pro tip - do not overmix the batter with the flour or you will risk losing all the volume you just created. '),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',11,'Divide batter equally between the prepared baking pans.Pro tip - I like to use cake strips to ensure my layer cakes bake flat.'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',12,'Bake for 30 to 35 minutes or until a skewer inserted in the center comes clean.'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',13,'Cool in the baking pan for 5 minutes. Invert and cool on a wire rack completely before you decorate'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',14,'See the video - how I make Swiss meringue buttercream'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',15,'Cocoa paste - Combine water and cocoa powder until you have a paste. Set aside to cool completely (gives a deeper darker chocolate color to the meringue) '),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',16,'Melt the chocolate in a microwave-safe bowl or double boiler. '),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',17,'In the bowl of a stand mixer, place the egg whites and sugar and place it over a pot of simmering water - this is called a double boiler.  Pro tip - the top bowl must not touch the simmering water in the bottom pot or the eggs will cook. '),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',18,'Using the whisk whip until all the sugar has dissolved and the egg whites are barely warm (about 160 F)'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',19,'Take the bowl off the heat and place it on the stand mixer. Whip the egg whites until you have a thick meringue with stiff peaks. '),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',20,'Let the mixer continue to whip on low until the mixer bowl feels cool to touch.Pro tip - it is VERY important that the meringue is cool if not the butter will melt. '),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',21,'Gradually add the butter one cube at a time with the mixer on medium speed. Once all the butter has been added turn the mixer up to medium-high and whip for 2 minutes. '),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',22,'Finally, add the vanilla extract, cocoa paste, and melted cooled chocolate. Make sure everything is well combined and you have a smooth chocolate buttercream. Set aside until ready to use. '),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',23,'Prepare simple syrup - cool completely before using.Pro tip- Simple syrup is just sugar water that has been boiled and cooled. Used to keep cake layers moist.'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',24,'Using a bread knife or cake leveler cut the domes off the cake layers');
INSERT INTO public.chef_kaggle_steps (recipe_id,position,instruction) VALUES
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',25,'Brush each layer with the cooled simple syrup'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',26,'Place a cake layer on the cake board or cake stand.'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',27,'Top with a big dollop of buttercream - spread evenly using a straight-edge spatula. Place the next layer followed by more buttercream, then the final layer. '),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',28,'Place the cake in the fridge to chill for 10 to 15 minutes.Pro tip - Chilling the cake at this point will ensure the layers don''t move when you frost the outside. Though, if you leave the cake uncovered in the fridge for too long it can dry out. So, 10 minutes is all you need.'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',29,'Spread the remaining buttercream around and on the top of the cake.Pro tip - A straight-edge spatula foR the top, an offset spatula, and a bench scraper for the sides work better.'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',30,'I’ve used an icing comb to create a pattern on the outside but you can choose to create a smooth effect with a bench scraper or a rustic finish with a spatula.'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cake_EVER_',31,'Place any remaining frosting in a piping bag and with a round tip and pipe small kisses as I have done.'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Mousse',1,'Melt chocolate in the microwave or double boiler - set aside to cool.'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Mousse',2,'Whip the cream with powdered sugar, salt, and cornstarch until soft peaks.'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Mousse',3,'Add cream cheese followed by vanilla extract.'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Mousse',4,'Combine the melted chocolate with the whipped cream mixture.'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Mousse',5,'Pour into individual serving glasses.'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Mousse',6,'Chill for an hour to set.'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Mousse',7,'Crush the cookies in a ziplock bag or food processor.'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Mousse',8,'Pile about 2 to 3 tablespoons on the top of each mousse.'),
('Best_Chocolate_Cheesecake_Mousse',9,'Chill further for at least 2 hours or until ready to serve.'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',1,'In a bowl cream butter and sugar for just a minute until well combined.'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',2,'Add the vanilla, salt and egg yolk – and combine well.'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',3,'Lastly, fold the flour – fold until combined.'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',4,'Make a disc and wrap in plastic wrap.'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',5,'Chill the dough in the refrigerator for at least two hours until firm to roll.'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',6,'Dust the work surface with flour.'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',7,'Open the dough and roll carefully from the center out turning as you go.'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',8,'Use your tart pan as a guide to know how big you need it.'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',9,'Transfer the dough to the tart pan.'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',10,'Gently press the dough into the tart pan making sure to press down into the shape of the pan.'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',11,'Trim the excess dough at the edges with a rolling pin, or your thumb.'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',12,'Chill the tart shell for a minimum of 30 minutes.'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',13,'Preheat oven at 190 C/ 380 F'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',14,'Peel, core, and chop apples into small slices about &frac18 inchTip - I find an apple corer works great to core the apples. If you don''t have one, its better to  cut the apples in half and then trim the unwanted center'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',15,'Add lemon juice and toss to combine well.'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',16,'Next, add the pumpkin spice, salt, sugar, and nutmeg – combine well.'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',17,'Finally, add the flour – combine well.'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',18,'Pour the apples in the chilled pastry shell – spread evenly.'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',19,'In a food processor add the flour, salt, sugar, and chilled cubed butter'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',20,'Pulse until it is large breadcrumb consistency'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',21,'Spread the crumble over the apples – making sure it coats the entire tart evenly.'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',22,'Bake the crumble tart in the preheated oven for about 45 to 50 minutes'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',23,'If the crumble on top starts to get too brown – tent with a piece of aluminum foilTip - if the edges of the tart get too dark you can use a pie shield to tent it. '),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',24,'When baked – cool on the wire rack for at least 15 minutes'),
('Best_EVER_Apple_Crumble_Tart',25,'You can serve this warm or room temperature.'),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',1,'Grease and line 3 x 7-inch or 2 x 8- inch round cake pans'),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',2,'Preheat the oven to 325°F / 165°C / Gas Mark 3'),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',3,'In a mixing bowl combine the flour, baking powder, baking soda, and salt. Set aside'),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',4,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with a whisk attachment whip the eggs until light and fluffy - remove and set aside.Pro tip - you can also whip the eggs after you prepare the basic batter. But, this method means you do not need to wash the mixer bowl in between. But, you must work quickly. '),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',5,'Next, working quickly cream the butter and sugar until light and fluffy about 2 minutes'),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',6,'Then, add the vanilla extract, sour cream, and butterscotch sauce - combine wellPro tip - the butterscotch sauce gives the cake that flavor. Though, the color comes from the dark brown sugar. '),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',7,'Next, add flour mixture and combine well but do not overmix. Pro tip - we do not want to activate the gluten in the batter so mix until just combined.'),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',8,'Finally, fold whipped eggs into the batterPro tip - First, combine &frac13 of the egg with a whisk to prevent lumps, Then, fold the rest in with a spatula using the folding method.'),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',9,'Divide batter equally between the prepared baking pans.Pro tip - I like to use cake strips to ensure my layer cakes bake flat. You can use a measuring cup or weighing scale to ensure you have equal amounts. '),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',10,'Bake on the center rack for 25 to 30 mins or until a skewer inserted in the center comes out clean'),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',11,'Cool in the baking pan for 5 minutes. Invert and cool on a wire rack completely before you decoratePro tip - it is very important that the cakes are completely cooled before frosting. Otherwise, the frosting will melt on the warm cakes. '),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',12,'I shared how to make butterscotch sauce in this video.'),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',13,'Place the cream in a microwave-safe bowl - heat it up for 30 secs and set aside. Pro tip - heating the cream for a while will help blend it better with the caramelized sugar.'),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',14,'In a heavy-based saucepan, on medium-low heat, melt butter gradually. Then add the brown sugar, salt, corn syrup, and lemon juice. '),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',15,'Stir continuously until melted making sure to keep the heat on low. Pro tip - brown sugar is quite sandy when melted. So it is difficult to know if it is melted. It must look like almost a paste. '),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',16,'Gradually, add the warm cream, stirring continuously. Remove from heat and cool to room temperature. '),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',17,'I shared how to make Swiss meringue buttercream in this video.'),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',18,'Place egg whites and sugar in the bowl of the stand mixer.Pro tip - make sure the bowl is grease-free otherwise the egg whites will not whip'),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',19,'Using a whisk, place the bowl over a double boiler and constantly whip until all the sugar has dissolved and the egg whites are fairly warm (about 160 F).Pro tip - you don''t need a thermometer, as long as all the sugar has completely melted your eggs are ready to use'),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',20,'Take the bowl off the heat and whip the egg whites until you have a thick meringue with stiff peaks.Pro tip - it is best to start whipping eggs at medium speed then increase speed as you go for the best meringue'),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',21,'Let the mixer continue to whip on medium-low until the mixer bowl feels cool to touch. Then gradually add butter, one cube at a time, with the mixer at medium speed.Pro tip - it is VERY important that the meringue is cooled completely before you add the butter otherwise you will have a soupy mess. '),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',22,'Once all the butter is added, whip on medium-high for 2 minutes. Lastly, add the vanilla. Combine well until everything is well combined.'),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',23,'Prepare simple syrup – cool completely before using.Pro tip - simple syrup is just sugar and water boiled for 3 minutes. It keeps the cake layers moist. '),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',24,'Once cooled, cut the domes off the cake layers using a serrated knife. Save the domes for the cake balls for the top of the cake. Brush each layer with the cooled, simple syrup.'),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',25,'Place a cake layer on the cake board or cake stand.Pro tip -if you plan to move the cake again, it is best to use a cake circle under the cake, so you can pick the cake with its base and without any accidents. '),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',26,'Top with a big dollop of the frosting – spread evenly with an offset spatula or spoon. Then, top the second cake layer on top followed by more buttercream, then the top layer. Pro tip - it is best to lift individual cake layers on pieces of clean cardboard or cake lifter so you do not break them from table to cake. '),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',27,'Place the cake in the fridge to chill for 10 to 15 minutes.Pro tip - Chilling the cake at this point will ensure the layers don''t move when you frost the outside. Though, if you leave the cake uncovered in the fridge for too long it can dry out. So, 10 minutes is all you need'),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',28,'Crumb coat - Spread more buttercream around and on top of the cake. (see video). Chill the cake for another 15 to 30 minutes.Pro tip - chilling the crumb-coated cake will ensure no cake crumbs get into the rest of the buttercream and you will have a nice clean cake. '),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',29,'Spread the remaining buttercream around and on top of the cake.Pro tip - A straight-edge spatula for the top, an offset spatula, and a bench scraper for the sides work better.'),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',30,'Final smoothing - dip an off-set spatula and bench scraper in warm water and smooth the sides and top of the cake.'),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',31,'Use the cooled but still pouring consistency butterscotch sauce as a drip on the cake. Pro tip - if the sauce is set heat it in the microwave for 10 seconds or more until pouring consistency. '),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',32,'Place the cake domes in a bowl and break them apart into crumbs. Alternatively, you can also place the domes in the food processor and pulse to breadcrumb consistency. '),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',33,'Add just enough buttercream and butterscotch sauce to create a dough-like consistency. Rolled the cake pop mixture into balls. Place them in the fridge for at least 15 minutes.'),
('Best_EVER_Butterscotch_Cake',34,'When chilled place them on the cake tops. And place any remaining crumbs around the cake. '),
('Best_Funfetti_Cake',1,'Preheat the oven at 325 F / 165 C / Gas Mark 3'),
('Best_Funfetti_Cake',2,'Grease and line a 9-inch round cake pan or 8-inch square baking pan.'),
('Best_Funfetti_Cake',3,'Dry ingredients - whisk or combine flour, baking powder, baking soda, and salt. Set aside.'),
('Best_Funfetti_Cake',4,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the paddle attachment, cream butter and sugar until light and fluffy. Add the eggs one at a time followed by the vanilla extract. Pro tip - ensure the eggs are room temperature and add them gradually one at a time to prevent the batter curdling. '),
('Best_Funfetti_Cake',5,'Next, add the flour and buttermilk in three batches.  Then, fold in the sprinkles with a spatula. Pro tip - Scrape the bottom and sides of the bowl to ensure you have a smooth batter. Do not overmix at this point to prevent bleeding.'),
('Best_Funfetti_Cake',6,'Pour the batter into the prepared baking pan. Bake in the preheated oven for 35 to 45 minutes until a skewer inserted in the center comes out clean.'),
('Best_Funfetti_Cake',7,'Cool on the baking tray for 10 minutes. Then, invert onto a cooling rack until completely cold. '),
('Best_Funfetti_Cake',8,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the paddle attachment, whip the butter until light and fluffy at least 2 to 3 minutes. Add condensed milk in three batches whipping well after each addition. Pro tip - the batter will look very loose at first then as you will it will become a light and fluffy '),
('Best_Funfetti_Cake',9,'Add the vanilla extract and whip some more until light and airy '),
('Best_Funfetti_Cake',10,'Spread a generous amount of frosting on the cake. Use an off-set spatula to spread it evenly.'),
('Best_Funfetti_Cake',11,'Sprinkle the edges with more sprinkles.'),
('Best_Granola_Recipe___Pecan_Pie',1,'Preheat the oven to 160 C / 320 F'),
('Best_Granola_Recipe___Pecan_Pie',2,'Roughly chop the pecans and set aside'),
('Best_Granola_Recipe___Pecan_Pie',3,'In a small mixing bowl combine the wet ingredients -  juice, maple, sugar, oil, salt, ground ginger, and cinnamon - combine well and set aside'),
('Best_Granola_Recipe___Pecan_Pie',4,'In a larger mixing bowl combine the rolled oats, chopped pecan, chia seeds, flax seeds, and wheat germ.'),
('Best_Granola_Recipe___Pecan_Pie',5,'Next, pour the mixture of liquid ingredients over the mixture of dry ingredients.'),
('Best_Granola_Recipe___Pecan_Pie',6,'Mix well - you want every grain of oat to be coated with the liquid ingredients (this will help toast them beautifully) '),
('Best_Granola_Recipe___Pecan_Pie',7,'Pour the mixture into a baking tray. I like to line my baking tray with parchment paper for easy clean-up'),
('Best_Granola_Recipe___Pecan_Pie',8,'Bake for 30 minutes stirring every 10 minutes until the oats are lightly golden'),
('Best_Granola_Recipe___Pecan_Pie',9,'Remove from the oven and cool completely before you store it in an airtight container. I like to use these glass containers.'),
('Best_Granola_Recipe___Pecan_Pie',10,'This batch will last for up to a month at room temperature.'),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',1,'In a microwave safe bowl or double boiler - add creamer and gelatin - let bloom for 2 minutes.'),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',2,'Melt in the microwave at 50% power in 30-sec intervals until completely dissolved (no grains left)'),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',3,'While still warm and working quickly - add in.'),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',4,'Butter/veg shortening, light corn syrup, glycerin, vanilla - stir well.');
INSERT INTO public.chef_kaggle_steps (recipe_id,position,instruction) VALUES
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',5,'The mixture should still be in a liquid state not set!! If necessary place in the microwave for 30 secs'),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',6,'Place one cup powdered sugar in a bigger bowl.'),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',7,'Add the cocoa powder and mix well.'),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',8,'Make a hollow in the center, and'),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',9,'Pour in the wet ingredients - stir.'),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',10,'Add the 2 tbsp of hot water - stir well.'),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',11,'Now start adding more powdered sugar.'),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',12,'Bring it all together with a wooden spoon first.'),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',13,'Then transfer onto a work surface dusted with powdered sugar, and'),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',14,'Knead until smooth and pliable.'),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',15,'Avoid adding too much powder sugar or the rested fondant later will be stiff and less elastic.'),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',16,'Divide fondant dough into two discs.'),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',17,'Place in a ziplock bag and a sealed container to prevent drying out.'),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',18,'Let rest in the fridge for 3 hours or overnight on the counter.'),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',19,'Knead the fondant until smooth and pliable.'),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',20,'Veg shortening works best when kneading fondant. '),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',21,'You can store this fondant at room temperature in a cool dark place for three months.'),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',22,'This can be frozen for over 6 months if sealed well.'),
('Best_Homemade_Chocolate_Fondant_Recipe',23,'Ensure to always wrap fondant well to prevent drying out.'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Dough',1,'In a mixing bowl or measuring cup combine warm water (110 F), yeast, sugar, and oil. Stir and set aside to foam for 3 mins.Pro-tip- instant yeast does not need to be activated but I like to ensure my yeast is good and working for me. You may choose to add all ingredients directly to the flour. '),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Dough',2,'Measure the flour and salt in a mixing bowl or stand mixer with the dough hook. Add the yeast mixture and combine well.Pro-tip - if you do not like kneading I highly recommend using a stand mixer with the hook attachment. '),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Dough',3,'Knead - By hand - transfer to a well-dusted worktop and knead for 5 to 6 minutes - Stand mixer - once all the flour is well incorporated knead on medium for 4 to 5 minutes '),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Dough',4,'When the dough is soft, shiny, but still slightly sticky shape into a ball. Place the dough in an oiled bowl seam side down. Coat the surface with oil to prevent drying. Cover with a clean kitchen cloth or plastic wrap. '),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Dough',5,'Leave in a warm place. Let rise for 60 to 90 minutes until double in volume. Pro-tip - in winter you may need 90 minutes or more but in summer the dough may double in 45 minutes. If you can''t attend to it at that moment. De-gas, reshape, and let double in volume again. '),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Dough',6,'When the dough is double in volume transfer to a well-dusted floured surface.  De-gas, reshape into a ball. Then roll into a small log. Pro-tip - at this point there is no need for additional flour. So use a light dusting of flour'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Dough',7,'Divide the dough into three (for 3 x 12-inch thin-crust pizzas) or two (for 2 x 12-inch thick-crust pizzas).Pro tip - Let the dough rest again for 10 minutes (it will become easier to stretch).'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Dough',8,'Preheat the oven with a pizza stone for at 425°F/220°C/Gas Mark 6 for at least 20 minutes. Pro tip -  the pizza must go into a very hot oven only then will you get a good balance of soft, chewy and golden crust. '),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Dough',9,'Roll one piece of dough to about 12 inches. The dough is soft and elastic you can stretch the dough with your hand or use a rolling pin. Transfer pizza to the pizza peel or pizza pan (see video).Pro tip - Place parchment paper on a pizza peel or use a pizza tray (parchment is less messy than cornmeal or flour).'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Dough',10,'Let the pizza base rest for 5 to 10 minutes. Brush the edges of the pizza with olive oil. Pro tip - resting will proof the dough and make those edges puff when baked. Brushing with oil will give a nice golden crisp crust.'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Dough',11,'Spread the pizza sauce and add your toppings. Generously sprinkle with cheese – I like to use a mix of mozzarella, parmesan, and cheddar.'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Dough',12,'Transfer the pizza to the preheated oven from the pizza peel to the pizza stone (or baking tray).'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Dough',13,'Bake for about 10 to 12 minutes until the edges are crisp and golden and the cheese is melted beautifully.'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',1,'In a bowl, combine warm water, yeast, sugar, and oil – mix well.'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',2,'In a mixer bowl with dough hook, combine the flour and salt.'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',3,'Pour in the yeast mixture (see video).'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',4,'Turn the mixer on medium-high speed until all the flour is incorporated.'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',5,'Once all the flour is incorporated, let the mixer run on medium speed for 3 minutes.'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',6,'The dough should be elastic, slightly sticky, but very soft and supple.'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',7,'Transfer to a lightly floured work surface. Bring all the dough into a ball.'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',8,'Tip – finger test – when you stick a finger in the dough should spring back.'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',9,'Place the dough in an oiled bowl and cover with a clean kitchen towel for 60 to 90 mins until double in volume.'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',10,'Preheat oven with pizza stone for at 200 C / 390 F for about 30 minutes.'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',11,'Lightly punch the dough to remove all air. '),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',12,'Divide the dough into two or three (for 3 x 12-inch thin-crust pizzas) or two (for 2 x 12-inch thick-crust pizzas) (see video).'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',13,'Tip - Let the dough rest again for 10 minutes (it will become easier to roll and stretch).'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',14,'Roll one piece of dough to about 12 inches (see video).'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',15,'Tip - Place parchment paper on a pizza peel or use a pizza tray (parchment is less messy than cornmeal or flour).'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',16,'Transfer pizza to the pizza peel or pizza tray (see video).'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',17,'Tips - Let the base rest for 5 to 10 minutes - this will proof the base just a little which makes those edges puffy. '),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',18,'Tip - Brush the edges of the pizza with olive oil (this will give a nice golden crisp crust).'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',19,'Spread tomato sauce (and tomato slices if using) (see video).'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',20,'Sprinkle the parmesan and place the mozzarella slices.'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',21,'Transfer the pizza to the preheated oven. From the pizza peel to the pizza stone (or baking tray).'),
('Best_Homemade_Pizza_Margherita',22,'Bake for about 10 to 12 minutes until the edges are crisp and golden and the cheese is melted beautifully.'),
('Best_Juicy_Beef_Burgers',1,'In a bowl, combine the ground beef with all other ingredients. Pro tip - Bring it all together but do not overwork the mixture as it will make the burgers tough.'),
('Best_Juicy_Beef_Burgers',2,'Divide your mixture into 4 large or 6 medium patties.Pro tip - The 4 large burgers will be approximately 8 oz  or 250 grams each and 4 medium will be about 6 oz or 160 grams each.'),
('Best_Juicy_Beef_Burgers',3,'Dip your hands in water (this prevents sticking) and helps shape the patties. Make a ball then flatten and shape edges.Pro tip - You can keep these wrapped in the fridge until you are ready to grill them. Thaw the patties to room temperature an hour before grilling.'),
('Best_Juicy_Beef_Burgers',4,'Heat the grill on medium high. Today, I am using an indoor grill but cast iron pan works just fine. Remember to keep the heat at medium-high.'),
('Best_Juicy_Beef_Burgers',5,'Place burger - grill for 3 to 4 minutes on each side until desired doneness. For the last minute – add the sliced cheese (optional).Pro tip - Burgers are high in fat, so you do not need to oil the gril. The fat in the meat will render and baste itself keeping it moist. When the fat burns on the grill it gives the burger that smokey flavor.  '),
('Best_Juicy_Beef_Burgers',6,'Combine all sauce ingredients in a bowl. Set aside.Pro tip - This sauce is perfect not just in the burger with the beef patties but also to dip your fries and onion rings. '),
('Best_Juicy_Beef_Burgers',7,'Split the burger buns and toast the edges on the grill. - Place the bun on the plate and add some sauce - Then, place the burger on the sauce and- Top the burger with veggies. I like to add some tomato, grilled onions, and lettuce. '),
('Best_Juicy_Beef_Burgers',8,'Serve burgers with your choice of sides like fries, onion rings, or salad.'),
('Best_Kahlua_Buttercream_Frosting',1,'Melt chocolate in a microwave safe bowl or double boiler - set aside to cool.'),
('Best_Kahlua_Buttercream_Frosting',2,'Cream the butter with Kahlua and vanilla'),
('Best_Kahlua_Buttercream_Frosting',3,'Gradually add the powdered sugar and continue to cream until light and fluffy.'),
('Best_Kahlua_Buttercream_Frosting',4,'Lastly, combine the cooled melted chocolate.'),
('Best_Kahlua_Buttercream_Frosting',5,'Tip - to prevent the chocolate from seizing add a little buttercream to the chocolate -  fold well. Then combine both the mixtures together. This will ensure a smooth buttercream'),
('Best_Kahlua_Buttercream_Frosting',6,'Cream the butter with Kahlua and vanilla'),
('Best_Kahlua_Buttercream_Frosting',7,'Gradually add the powdered sugar and continue to cream until light and fluffy.'),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',1,'Preheat the oven to 170 C/340 F.'),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',2,'Grease and line one 13 x 19 inch sheet pan of two 8 x 10 inch rectangular pans.'),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',3,'Have all your ingredients ready at room temperature.'),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',4,'Add the boiling water into the coffee and Cocoa powder - set aside to cool.'),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',5,'Combine the yogurt and the mix - use to whisk to ensure no lumps. '),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',6,'Sift the flour, baking powder, baking soda, and salt.'),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',7,'In another bowl - add melted butter and oil.'),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',8,'Add both the sugars. '),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',9,'Using a whisk whip until the sugars.. '),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',10,'Add eggs one at a time until each is well combined.'),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',11,'Next, add the cooled cocoa mixture into the sugar mixture - mix well.'),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',12,'Followed by the yogurt/milk mixture - stir well.'),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',13,'Lastly, add the vanilla.'),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',14,'Add the wet ingredients to the dry ingredients. '),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',15,'Use a whisk to ensure no lumps or dry flour remains behind.'),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',16,'This is a very liquid batter and that''s normal. '),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',17,'Pour into your baking pan and bake in the preheated oven until a skewer inserted into the center comes out clean.'),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',18,'A single 13 x 11 sheet pan will take about 30 to 40 minutes.'),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',19,'Two small rectangular pans will take 20 to 30 minutes each.'),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',20,'As soon as you take the hot cake out of the oven.'),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',21,'Sprinkle the chocolate chips on the cake surface and cover with a foil for ten minutes to cool.'),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',22,'The heat in the chocolate will melt the chocolate chips.'),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',23,'After 10 minutes remove foil.'),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',24,'Use a spatula to smear the melted chocolate.'),
('Best_Moist_Chocolate_Sheet_Cake',25,'Decorate when completely cold.'),
('Best_Orange_Cake',1,'Preheat the oven to 325°F / 165°C / Gas Mark 3.'),
('Best_Orange_Cake',2,'Grease and line 2× 6-inch baking pans with parchment paper. You can also double this recipe to make 2 x 8-inch round cakes.Pro tip - I am baking in 2 pans, so I can torte in half to make four. But, you can also use 3 x 6-inch round pans to make 3 layers. That way you don''t have to torte.'),
('Best_Orange_Cake',3,'Dry ingredients - Combine flour, baking powder, baking soda, and salt – set aside.'),
('Best_Orange_Cake',4,'Reduce orange juice - Place the orange juice in a saucepan over medium heat and reduce it to &frac13 (almost ½ cup). Cool completely. Pro tip - by reducing the liquid in the orange juice we concentrate the flavor.  '),
('Best_Orange_Cake',5,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the paddle attachment, cream the butter, oil, orange juice, and sugar until light and fluffy. Add the eggs, one at a time, making sure each is well incorporated. Pro tip - Adding eggs one at a time will prevent the batter from curdling'),
('Best_Orange_Cake',6,'Next, add the flour, sour cream, and cooled orange juice reduction in three batches making sure to scrape the sides of the bowl often. Then, add the vanilla and orange extract and combine well.Pro tip - Do not overmix at this stage as we do not want to activate the gluten in our flour.  ');
INSERT INTO public.chef_kaggle_steps (recipe_id,position,instruction) VALUES
('Best_Orange_Cake',7,'Pour the batter into the two prepared baking pans and bake for 20 to 25 minutes on the middle rack or until a center inserted in the center comes out clean. Pro tip - It is a great idea to use cake strips around my baking pans to prevent a dome. That way you don''t lose much height on your layer cakes. '),
('Best_Orange_Cake',8,'Once baked, leave in the pan for no more than 10 minutes. Then, invert onto a cooling rack to cool completely. Pro tip - Always frost cakes only when they are completely cooled. Otherwise, the frosting will melt. '),
('Best_Orange_Cake',9,'Watch my video on how to make Swiss meringue buttercream'),
('Best_Orange_Cake',10,'Place egg whites and sugar in the bowl of the stand mixer. Pro tip - make sure the bowl is grease-free otherwise the egg whites will not whip'),
('Best_Orange_Cake',11,'Using a whisk, place the bowl over a double boiler and constantly whip until all the sugar has dissolved and the egg whites are fairly warm (about 160 F).Pro tip - you don''t need a thermometer, as long as all the sugar has completely melted your eggs are ready to use'),
('Best_Orange_Cake',12,'Take the bowl off the heat and whip the egg whites until you have a thick meringue with stiff peaks.Pro tip - it is best to start whipping eggs at medium speed then increase speed as you go for the best meringue'),
('Best_Orange_Cake',13,'Let the mixer continue to whip on medium-low until the mixer bowl feels cool to touch. Then gradually add butter, one cube at a time, with the mixer at medium speed.Pro tip - it is VERY important that the meringue is cooled completely before you add the butter otherwise you will have a soupy mess. '),
('Best_Orange_Cake',14,'Once all the butter is added, whip on medium-high for 2 minutes. Lastly, add the vanilla. Combine well until everything is well combined.'),
('Best_Orange_Cake',15,'In a saucepan over medium heat cook the orange juice and sugar. Once the sugar is dissolved bring it to a boil. Cool completely before you use it on the cake.'),
('Best_Orange_Cake',16,'Once cooled, cut the domes off the cake layers using a serrated knife. Brush each layer with the cooled, orange syrup.'),
('Best_Orange_Cake',17,'Place a cake layer on the cake board or cake stand. Top with a dollop of buttercream and spread evenly. Pro tip -if you plan to move the cake again, it is best to use a cake circle under the cake, so you can pick the cake with its base and without any accidents. '),
('Best_Orange_Cake',18,'Next, top the second cake layer on top followed by more buttercream. Then, place the last cake layer on top.Pro tip - it is best to lift individual cake layers on pieces of clean cardboard or cake lifter so you do not break them from table to cake. '),
('Best_Orange_Cake',19,'Crumb coat or spread a little buttercream around the cake. (this helps seal the crumbs). Place the cake in the fridge to chill for 10 to 15 minutes.Pro tip - Chilling the cake at this point will ensure the layers don''t move when you frost the outside. Though, if you leave the cake uncovered in the fridge for too long it can dry out. So, 10 minutes is all you need'),
('Best_Orange_Cake',20,'Add orange gel food color to the remaining buttercream. Transfer the buttercream to a piping bag with a leaf piping tip nozzle. Pipe around the cake in a zig-zag from the bottom to the top.'),
('Best_Pavlova_Recipe',1,'Preheat the oven to 305F/150°C/ Gas Mark 2Pro tip - we start with a higher temperature then change to a lower temperature when we place the pavlova in the oven. '),
('Best_Pavlova_Recipe',2,'Line a baking tray with parchment paper. Trace an 8-inch circle as a guide on the parchment paper. Flip the paper so the pencil side is down not under the meringue.'),
('Best_Pavlova_Recipe',3,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with whisk attachment - whip the egg whites with salt on medium speed. Gradually add the sugar one tablespoon at a timePro tip - adding the sugar slowly prevents the protein from drying out. Adding sugar quickly can cause the meringue to become flat and runny later too.'),
('Best_Pavlova_Recipe',4,'When all the sugar has been added - continue to whip the meringue until you have stiff peaks.Pro tip - the meringue should be sticky with stiff peaks but still have a shiny appearance.'),
('Best_Pavlova_Recipe',5,'Switch to a spatula - fold in the vanilla extract. Then sift in the cream of tartar and cornstarch.Pro tip - Cream of tartar helps stabilizes the protein in the meringue and prevents it from separating. The cornstarch absorbs all the excess moisture and gives a crisp meringue'),
('Best_Pavlova_Recipe',6,'Spread the meringue on the circle you created - being careful to stay inside the circle. Use a spatula to smooth the sides evenly.  Keep the sides high and the top flat.'),
('Best_Pavlova_Recipe',7,'Place the pavlova in the oven on the center rack.'),
('Best_Pavlova_Recipe',8,'Close the oven door and immediately reduce the oven temperature to 265°F/130°C/Gas Mark ½ (DO NOT OPEN THE OVEN DOOR DURING BAKING).'),
('Best_Pavlova_Recipe',9,'Bake for 90 minutes - when the baking time is done do not open the door, let the pavlova cool inside the oven naturally.Pro tip - You can leave it in the oven for 2 to 3 hours up to 12 hours.'),
('Best_Pavlova_Recipe',10,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the whisk attachment whip the cream with powdered sugar.'),
('Best_Pavlova_Recipe',11,'Use an off-set spatula to gently loosen the pavlova from the parchment paper. Place it on a serving platter or cake board.Pro tip - once assembled this is a delicate dessert to move around so always assemble on a serving platter and not too early as the moisture from the whipping cream will make them soft'),
('Best_Pavlova_Recipe',12,'Evenly spread or pipe the whipped cream on each pavlova. Arrange the fruits of your choice. I''m using sliced strawberries, fresh blueberries, kiwi, and mint leaves for garnish.'),
('Best_Pavlova_Recipe',13,'Enjoy!'),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',1,'Preheat the oven to 325°F/ 165°C / Gas Mark 3'),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',2,'Grease and line 2× 6-inch baking pans with parchment paper. You can double this recipe to make 2 x 8-inch round cakes Pro tip - I am baking in 2 pans, so I can torte in half to make four but you can also use 3 x 6-inch round pans to make 3 layers that way you don''t have to torte. '),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',3,'Dry ingredients - Combine flour, cocoa powder, baking powder, baking soda, and salt – set aside'),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',4,'Red food color -  combine the gel color with the water - set aside'),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',5,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the paddle attachment cream the butter, oil, and sugar until light and fluffy. Add the eggs one at a time making sure each is well incorporated. Pro tip - adding eggs one at a time will prevent the batter from curdling.  '),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',6,'Next, add the flour and buttermilk in three batches making sure to scrape the sides of the bowl often. Pro tip - do not overmix at this stage as we do not want to activate the gluten in our flour.  '),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',7,'Next, add the prepared red food color and vanilla extract. Finally, add the vinegar and combine well. Pro tip - Make sure the oven is hot and the baking pans are ready because once you add the vinegar the mixture will start to bubble.'),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',8,'Pour the batter between the prepared baking pans and bake for 20 to 25 minutes on the middle rack or until a center inserted in the center comes out clean. Pro tip - It is a great idea to use cake strips around my baking pans to prevent a dome. That way you don''t lose much height on your layer cakes. '),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',9,'Once baked leave in the pan for no. more than 10 minutes. Invert onto a cooling rack to cool completely. Pro tip - always frost cakes only when they are completely cooled otherwise the frosting will melt. '),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',10,'Watch a video - how I make my Italian Meringue Buttercream (IMBC)'),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',11,'Place egg whites, salt, and cream of tartar in the bowl of a stand mixer with the whisk attachment on medium speed. Once the meringue is at the soft peak stage - turn the mixer on low to avoid over mix and wait for the sugar to reach temperature'),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',12,'Meanwhile, heat sugar and water in a heavy bottom light colors saucepan over medium heat. Once all the sugar is melted place a candy thermometer inside. Continue to boil until the sugar syrup reaches about 238 F on the candy thermometer (softball stage)Pro tip - using a heavy bottom will distribute heat evenly and prevent the sugar from caramelizing and a light-colored pan means you can see the color of the sugar and as you work.'),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',13,'Turn the mixer on medium speed and start pouring the hot sugar syrup into the mixer bowl. The sugar should stream between the whisk and the edge of the bowl. Once all the syrup is in. Turn the mixer on high and whisk for about 3 minutes. The outside of the bowl will be hot at first and then be barely warm.'),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',14,'When the meringue is cold and the bowl is not warm at all. Start adding the butter - one cube at a time. Pro tip - This is where 90% of meringue buttercreams fail DO NOT add butter if the meringue is still not cold.'),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',15,'Continue to boil until the sugar syrup reaches about 238 F on the candy thermometer (softball stage). This takes about 5 to 7 minutes on medium heat.'),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',16,'Once all the butter is in whip for another minute or two until you have a smooth and satin-like buttercream that light and fluffy. Add the vanilla extract.'),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',17,'Prepare simple syrup - cool completely before using.Pro tip- Simple syrup is just sugar water that has been boiled and cooled. Used to keep cake layers moist.'),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',18,'Watch a video showing how I level, torte, and fill the cakes.Pro tip - Make sure the cakes are completely cold, otherwise, the frosting will melt. Plus, the cakes are more delicate to handle. Chilling the cakes makes them easier to work with.'),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',19,'Using a bread knife or cake leveler cut the domes off the cake layers. Then divide each layer in half horizontally so you have four layers (2 x 2 = 4 layers)'),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',20,'Brush each layer with the cooled simple syrup. Place a cake layer on the cake board or cake stand.  Top with a big dollop of buttercream - spread evenly using a straight-edge spatula.'),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',21,'Place the cake in the fridge to chill for 10 to 15 minutes.Pro tip - Chilling the cake at this point will ensure the layers don''t move when you frost the outside. Though, if you leave the cake uncovered in the fridge for too long it can dry out. So, 10 minutes is all you need.'),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',22,'Spread the remaining buttercream around and the top of the cake.Pro tip - A straight-edge spatula for the top, an off-set spatula, and a bench scraper for the sides work better.'),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',23,'Add a few drops of pink gel food color to half of the remaining white buttercream. Put both colors of buttercream in a piping bag with a star piping tip nozzle'),
('Best_Red_Velvet_Cake',24,'Pipe swirls around the cake. These swirls are exactly what you would do on a cupcake just smaller and on the side and top of the cake.  Decorate as desired. '),
('Best_Strawberry_Mousse',1,'Blend the strawberries in a food processor until smooth. Strain through a sieve or mesh. Then, add the sugar, salt, and liquor. Combine well.Tip - Straining thru a sieve will take away all the fiber and seeds which gives a nicer consistency for the mousse. '),
('Best_Strawberry_Mousse',2,'Optional - For a more concentrated flavor, this puree can be reduced to half in a saucepan over medium heat.Tip - If you choose to reduce the strawberry puree, you will need to double the amount of strawberries in the recipe to make 6 servings. '),
('Best_Strawberry_Mousse',3,'Save ½ cup puree aside for the top garnish. This is optional as well. If you plan to top with whipped cream instead of puree for the garnish, you can use all this puree in the mousse.'),
('Best_Strawberry_Mousse',4,'Next, combine the gelatin with 2 tbsp of water. Let soak for 3 minutes then heat in the microwave for 30 to 40 seconds until completely dissolved. Let cool slightly.Tip - If you have any white scum on top of the melted gelatin, take it out with a spoon. '),
('Best_Strawberry_Mousse',5,'Add the melted gelatin to the strawberry puree. The best way to do this is to add a few tablespoons of strawberry puree to the gelatin. Then combine the two.Tip - Adding a little strawberry puree to the gelatin first will temper and prevent the gelatin from becoming lumpy.'),
('Best_Strawberry_Mousse',6,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the whisk attachment, whip the cream with powdered sugar and vanilla extract until stiff peaks.'),
('Best_Strawberry_Mousse',7,'Then, gently combine the whipped cream and strawberry mixture until you have no more white streaks. Your strawberry mousse is ready.'),
('Best_Strawberry_Mousse',8,'Divide the mixture evenly between 6 individual glasses. Top with the remaining strawberry puree we saved earlier.Tip - I like to pour the mousse into a piping bag and then pour it into the glasses. This makes it easier to pour and keeps the glasses clean.'),
('Best_Strawberry_Mousse',9,'Chill the mousse in the fridge for at least 3 hours - preferably 4 hours or overnight.'),
('Best_Strawberry_Mousse',10,'For garnish, you can top with whipped cream and strawberries. I used a slice of strawberry on each. '),
('Best_Strawberry_Mousse',11,'Enjoy!'),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',1,'Yeast - In a bowl of a stand mixer with the hook attachment, combine warm milk, sugar, and instant dry yeast. (you can also knead this by hand). Let rest for 3 to 5 minutes until foamy.Tip - it is not necessary to activate instant yeast but I always like to ensure my yeast is good and water is at the right temperature by activating it. This way I don''t waste ingredients'),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',2,'Wet Ingredients - To the prepared yeast mixture add the egg, vanilla, and butter.'),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',3,'Dry ingredients - In a bowl combine flour, salt, and nutmeg. '),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',4,'Add the wet ingredients into the dry ingredients - Yeast mixture to flour mixture.'),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',5,'Combine well until all the flour is incorporated. Then knead for 3 minutes on the stand mixer or 5 minutes by hand. Tip - Avoid adding too much extra flour when kneading. We want a soft, elastic, slightly sticky dough'),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',6,'Place the dough in an oiled bowl and let rise for 60 to 90 minutes or until double in volume.'),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',7,'After an hour, the dough should have been doubled in volume.'),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',8,'Transfer to a well-dusted work surface. Degas/delate then shape into a ball again. '),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',9,'On a lightly floured surface, using a rolling pin, roll to about ¼ inch thickness.'),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',10,'Using a 3-inch cookie cutter cut out as many discs as you can. Then use a ½ inch cookie cutter to make the center hole. Alternatively, you can also use a donut cutter.donut cutterTip - dust the edges of the cookie-cutter with flour so it will give you clean edges. '),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',11,'Transfer the donuts to a baking tray that has been lined with parchment paper and dusted with flour. Tip - The flour will prevent the donuts from sticking to the parchment paper. '),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',12,'Gather the remaining dough and cut-outs into a ball. Roll again using as little flour as possible to make the donuts. Tip - Keep some donut holes for testing the temperature of the oil. Alternatively, you can use a thermometer.'),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',13,'Cover the baking tray with a clean kitchen cloth to prevent the donuts from drying.'),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',14,'Place the donuts in the fridge for about 45 minutes to an hour to prove it again. They will rise and be cold but easier to handle when chilled.'),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',15,'Pour oil into a heavy pot or deep fryer and bring to about 350 °F to 360 °FTip 1- make sure you have enough oil so the donuts will be at least half immersed in oil when puffed.Tip 2- You want the oil hot, but not too hot. When you drop a donut hole it should come up in about 30 seconds, if it comes up too soon means the oil is too hot. Too slow means the oil is too cold. Adjust accordingly. '),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',16,'Gently add the cold donuts to the oil - Tip - Add two to three depending on the size of your skillet. If you add too many it will lower the temperature of the oil which will lead to the donuts becoming too oily. '),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',17,'Let the donut cook for 30 seconds, then flip, and cook on the other side for another 30 seconds. This way you will get an even color on both sides.'),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',18,'Continue to cook gently turning as necessary until golden brown.Tip - if the oil is too hot the donuts will brown quickly but still be raw inside so find that optimum temperature that works/ '),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',19,'Remove and drain on a paper hand towel. '),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',20,'Combine the cream cheese and whipping cream together with a whisk. Add powdered sugar – and mix well.'),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',21,'Lastly, add the coffee and vanilla extract. The glaze should be a thick pouring consistency – if necessary add a tbsp or two more of cream.'),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',22,'Once cooled, dunk each donut in the glaze. Let the excess drip well before you place it on the platter to prevent messy sides.'),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',23,'Let the chocolate set for a few minutes before you dust half a side with cocoa powder. Tip - use a piece of cardboard to block half the donut while you dust the cocoa powder '),
('Best_Tiramisu_Donuts',24,'Enjoy!'),
('Best_Tuna_Patties',1,'Drain the tuna well in a colander. '),
('Best_Tuna_Patties',2,'In a mixing bowl combine all ingredients with the tuna except the egg. Taste and adjust for seasoning. '),
('Best_Tuna_Patties',3,'Then add the egg and combine well. You should be able to shape the mixture into a little patty. If not add a few more breadcrumbs or a tablespoon of water. '),
('Best_Tuna_Patties',4,'Divide the mixture into four or six small patties. '),
('Best_Tuna_Patties',5,'Add oil or butter to a frying pan or cast-iron skillet on medium heat. '),
('Best_Tuna_Patties',6,'Cook the patties for 3 minutes on each side until lightly golden'),
('Best_Tuna_Patties',7,'Serve hot with ketchup, mayonnaise, or tartar sauce'),
('Best_Vanilla_Cupcakes',1,'Preheat the oven at 160 C / 325 F. Line a cupcake pan with cupcake liners'),
('Best_Vanilla_Cupcakes',2,'In a bowl, combine flour, baking powder, baking soda and salt. Set aside'),
('Best_Vanilla_Cupcakes',3,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the whisk attachment, whip the egg with sugar until light and fluffy,'),
('Best_Vanilla_Cupcakes',4,'Gradually add the oil, followed by the buttermilk, water, and vanilla extract.'),
('Best_Vanilla_Cupcakes',5,'Lastly, add the flour mix (continue to use the whisk attachment) to ensure you have a smooth batter. (don''t overmix) '),
('Best_Vanilla_Cupcakes',6,'Divide the batter between 12 to 15 cupcake liners'),
('Best_Vanilla_Cupcakes',7,'Bake for 18 to 20 minutes or until a toothpick inserted in the center comes out clean.');
INSERT INTO public.chef_kaggle_steps (recipe_id,position,instruction) VALUES
('Best_Vanilla_Cupcakes',8,'Cool in the pan for 5 minutes then transfer to a cooling rack to cool completely.'),
('Best_Vanilla_Cupcakes',9,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the paddle attachment, cream butter, whipping cream, salt, vanilla extract, and custard powder for a minute until smooth'),
('Best_Vanilla_Cupcakes',10,'Add the powdered sugar one cup at a time. Once all the powdered sugar is in – continue to whip for 2 minutes until light and fluffy.'),
('Best_Vanilla_Cupcakes',11,'Transfer the frosting to a piping bag with a star tip or similar. Pipe a generous swirl on each cupcake. '),
('Best_Vanilla_Cupcakes',12,'Enjoy!'),
('Black_Bean_Coconut_Curry__Vegan_',1,'Have all ingredients ready - this gets done very quickly'),
('Black_Bean_Coconut_Curry__Vegan_',2,'Heat oil in a saute pan. Add the garlic and ginger. Followed by the onion and cilantro. Cook for about 3 to 5 minutes until the onions are nice and translucentPro tip - it is important to always saute the veggies and spices well at each stage to get the maximum flavor.  '),
('Black_Bean_Coconut_Curry__Vegan_',3,'Add the spices and a little of the liquid from the beans. Cook spices for about another minute until fragrant. Next, add the coconut cream and cook for 3 minutes.Pro tip - cook on low heat adding a few more tablespoons of water as necessary making sure you get a nice aroma from the spices.  '),
('Black_Bean_Coconut_Curry__Vegan_',4,'Add the black beans and lemon juice. Season with salt and pepper. Cook for a minute or two more. Mash a few beans into the sauce. This will thicken the sauce. '),
('Black_Bean_Coconut_Curry__Vegan_',5,'Server with steamed white rice, chapati, naan, or even with crusty bread.'),
('Black_Beans_Curry',1,'In a saute pan, over medium heat, add oil and saute the onions, cinnamon, and bay leaves until onions are translucent.'),
('Black_Beans_Curry',2,'Add the ginger and garlic and saute for another minute. Then, add the chopped tomatoes and saute a minute more. Pro tip - it is important to always saute the veggies and spices well at each stage to get the maximum flavor.  '),
('Black_Beans_Curry',3,'Next, add curry powder, paprika, and cayenne - with ¼ cup water. Cook until the spices are fragrant. Pro tip - cook on low heat adding a few more tablespoons of water as necessary making sure you get a nice aroma from the spices.  '),
('Black_Beans_Curry',4,'Add the black beans, sour cream or yogurt, and chopped cilantro. Season with salt and pepper'),
('Black_Beans_Curry',5,'Cover and cook for 10 minutes more until thick and creamy.  Taste and adjust seasoning. Garnish with freshly chopped cilantro.'),
('Blackberry_Clafoutis',1,'Preheat the oven at 325°F/ 165°C/ Gas Mark 3'),
('Blackberry_Clafoutis',2,'Pan - Generously brush the baking pan with soft room temperature butter. For this recipe, your can use either a 9-inch pie pan or an 8-inch cast-iron skillet. '),
('Blackberry_Clafoutis',3,'Fruit - Choose six pretty looking blackberries and save them aside for garnish later. Spread the remaining blackberries in the tart pan evenly.'),
('Blackberry_Clafoutis',4,'Custard - Place all remaining ingredients in a food processor. Blend until smooth.Pro tip - blend until just combined, as we do not want to activate the gluten in the flour. You can also do this with a whisk in a bowl but ensure you have no lumps. '),
('Blackberry_Clafoutis',5,'Assemble - Gently pour the custard batter over the blackberries. Place on a baking tray for easy cleanup.Pro tip - I use the back of my spoon to soften the pour so it won''t ruin my fruit arrangement. '),
('Blackberry_Clafoutis',6,'Bake - Bake on the middle rack for about 35 to 40 minutes. Remove from the oven and cool completely.Pro tip - when done the batter will look set with not jiggly and with a slight puff. This puff will settle as it cools '),
('Blackberry_Clafoutis',7,'Serving - A clafoutis can be served warm, at room temperature, or cold. Serve on its own or dusted with powdered sugar. You can also serve with a scoop of ice cream or a dollop of whipped cream.'),
('Blackberry_Doughnuts___Sufganiyah',1,'Dry ingredients - In a bowl combine flour, salt, and grated nutmeg.'),
('Blackberry_Doughnuts___Sufganiyah',2,'Yeast - In a bowl of a stand mixer with the hook attachment, combine warm milk, sugar, yeast, egg, and vanilla. '),
('Blackberry_Doughnuts___Sufganiyah',3,'Add the flour to the yeast mixture and combine well until all the flour is incorporated. Add the butter and combine well again. Then knead for 3 minutes on the stand mixer or 5 minutes by hand. Tip - Avoid adding too much extra flour when kneading. We want a soft, elastic, slightly sticky dough'),
('Blackberry_Doughnuts___Sufganiyah',4,'Place the dough in an oiled bowl and let rise for 60 to 90 minutes or until double in volume.'),
('Blackberry_Doughnuts___Sufganiyah',5,'Once double in volume - invert on a floured surface.  Divide the dough into 2 sections. Then, divide each section into 6 - making 12 doughnutsTip - Always make one or two mini doughnuts for the purpose of testing oil temperature.'),
('Blackberry_Doughnuts___Sufganiyah',6,'Roll each portion into a ball and place it on a parchment-line baking tray dusted with flour to prevent sticking.Tip - Roll each piece into a smooth ball. Gather the seams and roll between your palms until you have a smooth ball. If the balls are not smooth, your doughnuts will look cracked.'),
('Blackberry_Doughnuts___Sufganiyah',7,'Once all the balls are rolled, flatten it slightly. Cover the baking tray with a clean kitchen cloth to prevent the donuts from drying.Tip - Flattening will ensure you have a doughnut shape when it rises and deep-fries as compare to a ball '),
('Blackberry_Doughnuts___Sufganiyah',8,'Place the donuts in the fridge for about an hour to prove again, or until almost double in volume.Tip -They will rise and be cold but easier to handle when chilled. Alternatively, you can let them rise at room temperature for 30 minutes.'),
('Blackberry_Doughnuts___Sufganiyah',9,'Heat cooking oil in a large pot or deep fryer to about 350 °F to 360 °FTip - You don''t want the oil too hot. They need to be cooked inside before they brown on the outside.  If the oil is too hot the donuts will get too dark or stay uncooked inside.'),
('Blackberry_Doughnuts___Sufganiyah',10,'Add a mini doughnut to test the oil. Once the oil is ready - add two or three doughnuts at a time.Tip- You need enough oil so the doughnuts will float, and not touch the bottom of the pot.'),
('Blackberry_Doughnuts___Sufganiyah',11,'Do not crowd the pan as the temperature of the oil will drop/cool down too fast. The doughnuts should rise in 30 secs as they puff.'),
('Blackberry_Doughnuts___Sufganiyah',12,'Cook for 30 seconds on one side then flip and let cook another 30 seconds on the other side. You will need about 2 to 3 minutes for each donut to cook and be beautifully brown. '),
('Blackberry_Doughnuts___Sufganiyah',13,'Remove onto a paper towel and let cool for 10 minutes before you fill and serve'),
('Blackberry_Doughnuts___Sufganiyah',14,'Whip the cream with powdered sugar and cornstarch. Combine the whipped cream, blackberry puree, and vanilla.'),
('Blackberry_Doughnuts___Sufganiyah',15,'Add your filling in a piping bag with a bismark piping tip or similarTip - Depending on your filling let the donuts cool for at least 10 minutes before you fill them or the filling will melt.'),
('Blackberry_Doughnuts___Sufganiyah',16,'Dust with powdered sugar if desired. Top with more filling on the top (optional)  or jam.'),
('Blackberry_Doughnuts___Sufganiyah',17,'Enjoy!'),
('Blackberry_Ice_Cream_No_Churn',1,'In the bowl of a stand mixer, with the whisk attachment, whip the whipping cream until almost stiff peaks. Pro tip - The more you whip the cream the fluffier the ice cream. But, do not overwhip or you will churn the whipping cream into butter. '),
('Blackberry_Ice_Cream_No_Churn',2,'Next, add the condensed milk and vanilla extract. Mix a minute more to combine. Pro tip - This is your basic no-churn vanilla ice cream. 😜'),
('Blackberry_Ice_Cream_No_Churn',3,'Crush the blackberries with a fork. Then, add them to the whipped cream mixture and combine. Pro tip - I like to give it a gentle swirl just enough to combine and marble it. Alternatively, stir vigorously to blend it into a smooth blackberry pink color. '),
('Blackberry_Ice_Cream_No_Churn',4,'Pour into an ice cream storage container and freeze for at least 4 hours or overnight. Pro tip - For the creamiest ice cream, thaw the container for at least 10 minutes before you attempt to scoop the ice cream. This will soften any ice crystals. '),
('Blackberry_Ice_Cream_No_Churn',5,'Enjoy!'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',1,'Preheat the oven to 160C/320 F'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',2,'Cut the peaches in half, and slice them thin.'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',3,'If you cut them in advance - drizzle 1 tsp of lemon juice to prevent them from oxidizing.'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',4,'Sift the flour with the baking powder, baking soda, and salt - set aside.'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',5,'Chop the butter for crumb into small pieces but keep them chilled in the fridge until ready to use.Prepare crumb topping'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',6,'Place the flour, almond meal, sugar, lemon zest, salt, and spices in a food processor'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',7,'Lastly, add the chilled butter cubes'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',8,'Pulse for a few seconds at a time until it resembles breadcrumb consistency'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',9,'Alternatively, you can use your fingers to cut the butter into the dry mixture until it reaches breadcrumb consistency.'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',10,'Keep the crumb topping chilled in the fridge until ready to use.Prepare batter'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',11,'Cream butter and sugar until light and fluffy'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',12,'Add eggs one at a time.'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',13,'Followed by the jam - combine well.'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',14,'Add the flour mix along with the sour cream and buttermilk.'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',15,'Lastly, add the vanilla.'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',16,'Pour the batter into an 8 x 8 square cake pan or 9 x 13 sheet pan (see notes above)'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',17,'Sprinkle the blackberries all over.'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',18,'I like to tuck them into the batter so they sink in.'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',19,'Layer the chopped peaches on top - they won''t really be seen under the crumb.'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',20,'Sprinkle the prepared crumb topping all over generously.Bake'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',21,'Bake in a preheated oven for almost an hour until a skewer inserted in the center comes clean'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',22,'Cool on a wire rack for at least 15 minutes before you attempt to cut into it.'),
('Blackberry_Nectarine_Crumb_Cake_Recipe',23,'This can be served as is and needs nothing else - but you are feeling indulgent serve with some freshly whipped cream.'),
('Blackberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart',1,'Blackberry Puree - Pulse the blackberries in a food processor or blender until smooth. Sieve thru a fine mesh to remove seeds. Use the amount requested in this recipe.Pro tip - straining the puree will remove the seeds which will give a velvety texture to the panna cotta '),
('Blackberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart',2,'Using a food processor, crush the graham crackers until bread crumb consistency. Add melted butter and sugar. Combine well so there are no dry crumbs. Alternatively, place them in a ziplock bag and crush them with a rolling pin.Pro tip - make sure you do not have large cookie chunks as that can cause the crust to break easily when slices'),
('Blackberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart',3,'Pour into the tart pan and use the back of the spoon or glass to press the crumbs into the pan. Place the tart in the freezer for an hour.Pro tip - freezing the tart will prevent the panna cotta mixture from soaking into the crust. '),
('Blackberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart',4,'Sprinkle gelatin over the cold milk. Stir and set aside for 3 to 5 minutes to bloom. Pro itp - soaking the gelatin will ensure it dissolved into a smooth not grainy mixture. '),
('Blackberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart',5,'In a heavy-bottom saucepan over medium-heat, heat the cream & sugar until sugar dissolves and cream comes to an almost boil. '),
('Blackberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart',6,'Add the vanilla extract and the soaked gelatin milk. Continue to cook until the gelatin is all dissolved and the mixture is well heated thru. Pro tip - we do not want to boil the gelatin as it can make the gelatin chewy. '),
('Blackberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart',7,'Take the mixture off the heat and add the blackberry puree. Sieve the mixture thru a mesh to get any undissolved gelatin or remaining blackberry seeds.'),
('Blackberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart',8,'Gently pour the mixture into the cooled/partially frozen tart shell. Pro tip - I prefer to pour over the back of a spoon for a gentle pour so it does not disturb the cookie crumbs.  '),
('Blackberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart',9,'Carefully place the tart in the fridge and chill for at least 4 hours until the pannacotta is set.Pro tip - place the tart on a baking tray so it is easier to move it around without spilling. '),
('Blackberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart',10,'Combine remaining blackberry puree with water. Add sugar and gelatin. Let soak for 3 to 5 minutes.'),
('Blackberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart',11,'Heat over medium until all the gelatin dissolves and comes to a boil. Strain thru a sieve to remove any seeds. Cool until barely warmPro tip - we want to bring it to the boil and take it off the heat immediately. Cook the gelatin too much will make it chewy. '),
('Blackberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart',12,'Gently pour over the set blackberry panna cotta. Chill in the freezer for an hour, then remove from the freezer and chill in the fridge until ready to serve. Pro tip - Chilling in the freezer for an hour will set the jello instantly and prevent it from soaking into the tart.'),
('Blackberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart',13,'Once chilled – garnish the top of the blackberry tart. I’ve used whipped cream, fresh blackberries, and cherries in season.'),
('Blueberry_Banana_Smoothie',1,'Add all ingredients except honey to a blender and blend until smooth'),
('Blueberry_Banana_Smoothie',2,'Taste for sweetness. If necessary add the honey and blend once more. '),
('Blueberry_Banana_Smoothie',3,'Pour into individual serving glasses and enjoy!'),
('Blueberry_Bars',1,'Preheat oven to 190 °C / 380 °F / Gas Mark 5'),
('Blueberry_Bars',2,'Line an 8 x 8 square cake pan or a 7 x 9" rectangle pan with parchment paper leaving an overhang so you can pick the bars out.'),
('Blueberry_Bars',3,'In a bowl of a food processor - add flour, sugar, salt, vanilla extract, and butter. Pulse a few times - until breadcrumb consistency. Tip - Alternatively, you can use a pastry blender or your fingers to squish the butter into the flour until you reach a breadcrumb consistnecy'),
('Blueberry_Bars',4,'Save almost half of the mixture for the topping in the refrigerator. Tip - I like to use more for the base and lesser for the top. That way the base makes for better squares'),
('Blueberry_Bars',5,'Add the 2 tbsp of milk to the remaining mixture and pour it into the prepared baking pan. Use the back of a spoon or glass to press it down firmly.Tip - pressing firmly will give a firmer crust that will make better pieces later. '),
('Blueberry_Bars',6,'Bake for 10 minutes until lightly golden but not cooked thru. Cool for 5 minutes.'),
('Blueberry_Bars',7,'In a mixing bowl, add the blueberries, sugar, lemon, vanilla extract, salt, and cornflour. Combine well. Set asideTip - Do not prepare the filling too early.  The juices will make the base too wet and soggy.'),
('Blueberry_Bars',8,'Spread the cream cheese over the crust evenly with a spatula.  Pour the blueberry mixture over the cream cheese mixture and spread evenly.'),
('Blueberry_Bars',9,'Finally, top with the crumble mixture (we saved it in the refrigerator earlier) '),
('Blueberry_Bars',10,'Continue to bake for another 35 to 40 minutes until lightly golden. Cool completely then cut into 16 squares'),
('Blueberry_Cheesecake___Baked',1,'Pre-heat the oven at 350°F / 177°C/ Gas Mark 3.'),
('Blueberry_Cheesecake___Baked',2,'Prepare pan - Wrap the outside of a 9-inch springform pan in aluminum foil.  We will also need a roasting rack larger than the springform pan. I am using an 8-inch springform pan because I like a little height in my cheesecakes.  Pro tip - The aluminum foil will prevent water from entering the cheesecake while baking in a water bath.'),
('Blueberry_Cheesecake___Baked',3,'In a saucepan, over medium heat, add the blueberries, sugar, lemon juice, and ¼ cup water. Cook on low to medium heat until all the sugar has dissolved. Use a vegetable masher to mash some of the fruit. Pro tip - Mashing will add a nice thicker consistency to the topping but make sure to leave some blueberries whole. '),
('Blueberry_Cheesecake___Baked',4,'Combine the remaining water with cornstarch.  Add it to the blueberries. Continue to cook on low heat until the filling is thick and glossy. Pro tip - Cornstarch can settle to the bottom of the water so you must stir it just before adding it to the saucepan. '),
('Blueberry_Cheesecake___Baked',5,'Remove and cool before you pour it over the cheesecake, or serve it alongside the cheesecake. Pro tip - The filling will thicken as it cools so keep that in mind when you take it off the heat. '),
('Blueberry_Cheesecake___Baked',6,'Crush the graham cracker/biscuits in a food processor. Add sugar and the melted butter and stir to combine.Pro tip - You can also place them in a ziplock bag and use a rolling pin to crush them.'),
('Blueberry_Cheesecake___Baked',7,'Pour crumbs into the prepared springform pan. Use the back of your spoon or measuring cup to press the crumbs firmly to form a crust.Pro tip - Pressing down firmly will ensure a good base for the cheesecake and it won''t fall apart when you cut slices.');
INSERT INTO public.chef_kaggle_steps (recipe_id,position,instruction) VALUES
('Blueberry_Cheesecake___Baked',8,'Bake in the oven for 10 minutes. Once baked set aside to cool slightly.'),
('Blueberry_Cheesecake___Baked',9,'Reduce the oven temperature to  300°F / 150°C/ Gas Mark 2.'),
('Blueberry_Cheesecake___Baked',10,'In the bowl of a stand mixer, with the whisk paddle attachment, combine cream cheese and sour cream. Then, add the sugar. Followed by the cornflour and vanilla extract.Pro tip - The cream cheese must be at room temperature. Otherwise, the batter will be lumpy. And if necessary, place a warm bowl on top of the cream cheese to help thaw faster. '),
('Blueberry_Cheesecake___Baked',11,'Add the eggs, one at a time, making sure to incorporate each well.Pro tip - We want each egg to incorporate well but we do not want to incorporate too much air into the batter. Otherwise, the top will crack when baking. So, do not overmix.'),
('Blueberry_Cheesecake___Baked',12,'Double boiler - Pour the batter into the prepared springform pan over the baked crust. Place the springform pan in a deep baking pan or roasting rack.  Pour 2 cups of hot water into the roasting rack outside the springform pan. Pro tip - The water will create steam in the oven and prevent the custard-based cheesecake from drying out. '),
('Blueberry_Cheesecake___Baked',13,'Bake for 70 to 80 minutes until set. Remove from the oven and let cool for 30 minutes on the counter. Then, run a knife or spatula around the edge of the cake but do not remove it from the pan. Pro tip - As the cheesecake cools it will shrink slightly. Running the knife around will prevent any cracks on the top of the cheesecake. '),
('Blueberry_Cheesecake___Baked',14,'Chill the cheesecake for at least 4 hours - preferably overnight. You can pour the blueberry filling over the cheesecake before chilling it. Or, serve the blueberry filling along with the cheesecake as I have done here.'),
('Blueberry_Cream_Cake_with_Crumb_Topping',1,'Preheat oven to 170 C / 340 F'),
('Blueberry_Cream_Cake_with_Crumb_Topping',2,'Grease and line a loaf pan or a 7" round cake pans'),
('Blueberry_Cream_Cake_with_Crumb_Topping',3,'Swift flour, baking powder, baking soda, and salt.'),
('Blueberry_Cream_Cake_with_Crumb_Topping',4,'If using frozen blueberries drain them well.'),
('Blueberry_Cream_Cake_with_Crumb_Topping',5,'Cream together butter, cream cheese and sugar until light and fluffy'),
('Blueberry_Cream_Cake_with_Crumb_Topping',6,'Add eggs one at a time'),
('Blueberry_Cream_Cake_with_Crumb_Topping',7,'Followed by vanilla'),
('Blueberry_Cream_Cake_with_Crumb_Topping',8,'Combine blueberries in the flour mixture, combine well so they are all coated with the flour.'),
('Blueberry_Cream_Cake_with_Crumb_Topping',9,'Add half the flour mix (with blueberries) and the yogurt - fold into the batter'),
('Blueberry_Cream_Cake_with_Crumb_Topping',10,'Then add rest of the flour mix - fold until no dry flour is visible.'),
('Blueberry_Cream_Cake_with_Crumb_Topping',11,'Pour batter into prepared baking pan'),
('Blueberry_Cream_Cake_with_Crumb_Topping',12,'Gently mix the flour, salt, sugar and cold butter with your hands until you reach breadcrumb consistency'),
('Blueberry_Cream_Cake_with_Crumb_Topping',13,'Sprinkle over the cake evenlyBake'),
('Blueberry_Cream_Cake_with_Crumb_Topping',14,'Bake in a preheated oven for 30 to 40 minutes or until a skewer inserted comes out clean'),
('Blueberry_Cream_Cake_with_Crumb_Topping',15,'Cool in the pan for 10 minutes then remove onto a wire rack to cool completely.'),
('Blueberry_Cream_Cake_with_Crumb_Topping',16,'Enjoy!'),
('Blueberry_Ice_cream_No_Churn',1,'In the bowl of a stand mixer, with the whisk attachment, whip the whipping cream until almost stiff peaks. Pro tip - The more you whip the cream the fluffier the ice cream. But, do not overwhip or you will churn the whipping cream into butter. '),
('Blueberry_Ice_cream_No_Churn',2,'Next, add the condensed milk and vanilla extract. Mix a minute more to combine. Pro tip - This is your basic no-churn vanilla ice cream. 😜'),
('Blueberry_Ice_cream_No_Churn',3,'Pulse the blueberries in a blender then pass thru a sieve - discard the skins and set the juice asidePro tip - Removing the skin makes a smooth creamy velvety texture ice cream. '),
('Blueberry_Ice_cream_No_Churn',4,'Then, add the blueberry puree to the whipped cream mixture and combine. Pro tip - I like to stir well to blend it into a smooth blueberry color. Alternatively, you can add the puree in two batches and give it a gentle swirl just enough to get a marbled color and texture. '),
('Blueberry_Ice_cream_No_Churn',5,'Pour into an ice cream storage container and freeze for at least 4 hours or overnight. Pro tip - For the creamiest ice cream, thaw the container for at least 10 minutes before you attempt to scoop the ice cream. This will soften any ice crystals. '),
('Blueberry_Ice_cream_No_Churn',6,'Enjoy!'),
('Blueberry_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',1,'Place two small ceramic plates in the freezer so we can use these to test the jam later. Alternatively, you can use a candy thermometer to check the doneness of the jam. '),
('Blueberry_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',2,'Check the blueberries and remove any bad, discolored, or bruised ones. Give them a quick wash and drain in a colander.Pro tip - Soft blueberries can be used but discolored and bruised ones will ruin the jam. Also, don''t soak blueberries in water for too long as they do soak up moisture. '),
('Blueberry_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',3,'In a heavy bottom pan, combine the blueberries, sugar, salt, and lemon juice.Pro tip - If you are using frozen berries, let the blueberries macerate in sugar and lemon juice for a few hours before cooking. This softens the blueberry skin considerably. '),
('Blueberry_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',4,'Cook on medium heat until the sugar is dissolved. Then, turn the heat up and let the mixture come to a boil. Let it boil for two minutes on medium-high. Pro tip - Boiling the jam is important as it releases pectin from the skin and seed in fruits. '),
('Blueberry_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',5,'Then, turn the heat to medium-low. The jam should still be simmering but at a low simmer, not bubbling. Use a potato masher to mash the fruit – so you have a smoother jam-like consistency.Pro tip - Mashing the fruit is optional, as the fruit will break down into smaller chunks similar to preserve as it cooks. However, mashing will give smoother consistency like jam. '),
('Blueberry_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',6,'Continue to simmer for about 20 to 30 minutes more stirring often so it does not stick to the bottom of the pan. The jam will continue to thicken as well as deepen in color as it cools.Pro tip - The cooking time will depend on the quantity of the jam as well as the heat applied to it. It''s ok to cook a little longer but there must be a simmer for the fruit to release pectin.'),
('Blueberry_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',7,'Remove one of the ceramic plates from the freezer. Place a teaspoon of jam on the cold plate. Pro tip - The cold plate will help cool the jam almost instantly and give you a good indication if the jam is ready. '),
('Blueberry_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',8,'Set aside for 2 to 3 minutes then test with your finger. Simply move/push the jam with your finger. If it wrinkles/crinkles it means the jam is ready. And if not, let the jam cook a couple of minutes more and test again.Pro tip - You may need to test the jam on a ceramic plate more than once or a couple of times depending on how early you start checking.'),
('Blueberry_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',9,'Alternatively, you can use a candy thermometer - the jam should reach 105 C / 221 F.Pro tip - I find the thermometer to be the easiest and fail-proof method to check for doneness. '),
('Blueberry_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',10,'Optional - Just when you are ready to take the jam off the heat add a teaspoon of butter and stir well. Butter helps dissolve foam that accumulates on top of the jam. Pro tip - You don''t need more than 1 teaspoon of butter to help with the foam. It will also give you that glossy shine.'),
('Blueberry_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',11,'Pour the jam into warm sterilized jars leaving ¼ inch space from the top. Use a clean sterilized knife or spatula to move the jam a bit – this will remove any air pockets.'),
('Blueberry_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',12,'Place a piece of wax paper on the top before you place the lid on tightly. Clean the rim of the jar with a clean paper towel. Top the lid. Alternatively, use the lid with screw-on rings that come with the canning jars.'),
('Blueberry_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',13,'Sterilize 4 x 8 oz (250 g) jars by washing them in hot soapy water or cleaning them in the dishwasher with a gentle cycle. Then, place them in the oven for 20 minutes at a low 284 F / 140 CPro tip-  I find the dishwasher does a good job of cleaning and the oven dries any excess moisture in the bottles.'),
('Blueberry_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',14,'Note - Leave them in the oven until you are ready to use them (you can turn the oven off). Don’t forget to wash and sterilize the bottle lids as well.'),
('Blueberry_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',15,'Place a rack in the bottom of a large stockpot. Fill half the pot with water. Bring the water in the pot to a boil on high heat.'),
('Blueberry_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',16,'Lower the jars over the rack leaving enough space between the jars.Pro tip - The level of water should be at least an inch above the top of the jars. So if necessary, pour more boiling water.'),
('Blueberry_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',17,'Bring the water to a boil again. Cover the pot and process/simmer for 15 minutes.'),
('Blueberry_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',18,'Then, carefully remove the jars from the stockpot and place them on a kitchen towel to absorb any excess moisture. Cool completely. Pro tip - The hot jars are very delicate so make sure to use tongs when taking them out and place them on soft towels to prevent them from breaking. '),
('Blueberry_Jam___No_Pectin__3_ingredients_',19,'Press the top of the lid to ensure the seal is tight – the lid should not move at all. Store in a cool dry place.'),
('Blueberry_Macarons',1,'Place almond meal and powdered sugar in a food processor. Sift it and discard any big or remains that does not go thru. However, if you have a lot in the sifter - pulse some more and strain again. Tip - pulsing and staining will ensure you have a flour consistency. So do not skip this step.'),
('Blueberry_Macarons',2,'Whip egg whites - Place the egg whites with cream of tartar in a grease-free bowl of a stand mixer with the whisk attachment. Start whisking on medium speed. (in the video I am using a hand mixer so you can see better but a stand mixer is ) Tip - the cream of tartar helps stabilize the egg whites. You can omit but it is especially helpful when making macarons in warm weather or humid places.'),
('Blueberry_Macarons',3,'After a minute start adding the granulated sugar one spoon at a time.Tip - adding the sugar one spoon at a time will prevent the protein in the egg whites from breaking down. '),
('Blueberry_Macarons',4,'Once all the sugar has been added - turn to medium-high and whip until stiff peaks. Add extract and food color - mix the color well.'),
('Blueberry_Macarons',5,'Fold in - Next, fold the almond mixture into the whipped egg whites in three batches.'),
('Blueberry_Macarons',6,'Macronage - once the almond mixture has been incorporated, we need to bring it to the right consistency. See video on how I do this. Use a spatula and spread the mixture around in the bowl - then bring it back to the center. Do it again and again until you have the right consistency. I usually have to do this about 4 to 5 times with each batch.'),
('Blueberry_Macarons',7,'Consistency - you need, what is called a dropping consistency or a thick ''lava-like'' or ''cake batter'' consistency. This means when you hold a little batter on the spatula and it drops down like a ribbon that blends back into itself.Tip - getting the right consistency sometimes takes time. So, watch that part of a video carefully. '),
('Blueberry_Macarons',8,'Pipe - Transfer batter into a piping bag with a large round tip (No.12). Pipe similar size macarons onto a parchment-lined baking tray using a template.Tip- templates ensure all shells are similar in size. This is helpful when we make the finished macarons. You can print free templates found on google or make your own with a cookie cutter. '),
('Blueberry_Macarons',9,'Piping technique - The best way to pipe the macarons, hold the piping bag at 90%. Squeeze until you have a good mound then swirl the tip to one side. But don''t worry if you have a point,.When you tap the pan these usually settle down.'),
('Blueberry_Macarons',10,'Tap baking pan - Tap the baking tray on the counter several times.Tip - Tapping helps so all the air pockets will rise to the top and release. That way you won''t have big holes in your macarons. I do three taps on each side as shown in the video.'),
('Blueberry_Macarons',11,'Rest - Let the macarons sit in a cool dry place for about 30 to 50 minutes until it forms a skin on the top. If you touch the shell it should not stick to your finger. Tip -  In places, with high humidity, this can take up to 60 minutes. As long as it does not stick to your finger when you touch it - you are good to go.'),
('Blueberry_Macarons',12,'While the macarons are drying - preheat the oven to 150 C / 300 F. Tip - I usually start my oven at about 20 minutes because that''s how long it takes in my home. '),
('Blueberry_Macarons',13,'Bake the macarons for 12 to 15 minutes depending on your oven. (some ovens can take up to 18 minutes) The tops will look set but the bottom should not be wet. The top shell should be shiny and the bottom crusty (also called macaron feet).Tip - do not open the oven door for the first 10 minutes of baking. When you shake the pan they must look set. Remember they continue to bake with the residue heat on the baking tray. '),
('Blueberry_Macarons',14,'Cool on the baking tray for at least 10 minutes before you remove and transfer them to a cooling rack. Tip - trying to remove the macarons from the hot tray can cause the tops to separate from the bottom feet. Once you let them cool they will come off easily. So, be patient.'),
('Blueberry_Macarons',15,'Watch my video on how to make this blueberry filling '),
('Blueberry_Macarons',16,'In a heavy-bottom saucepan combine all filling ingredients making sure you have no lumps. Cook over medium to high until it comes to boil and you have a thick shinny filling. Tip - the cornstarch in the mixture needs to cook which takes the mixture from opaque to glossy. '),
('Blueberry_Macarons',17,'Watch my video and step by step progress for Swiss Meringue Buttercream'),
('Blueberry_Macarons',18,'In the bowl of a stand mixer add the eggs whites, salt, cream of tartar, and sugar. Place the bowl over a pot of simmering water. Whisk the egg whites over the simmering water until all the sugar has melted. '),
('Blueberry_Macarons',19,'Place the mixer bowl on the stand and start at medium to low speed with a whisk attachment increasing the speed gradually. Whisk to firm peaks, shiny meringue.'),
('Blueberry_Macarons',20,'Touch the mixer bowl. If it’s still warm wait, run the mixer on low until it cools. Once the bowl feels warm to the touch, start adding the butter one cube at a time. Then, add the vanilla extract and whip on medium-high speed for 2 minutes until you have a light and fluffy buttercream. '),
('Blueberry_Macarons',21,'On a baking tray pair similar size macarons shells so you have similar size macarons'),
('Blueberry_Macarons',22,'Add the filling in one piping bag and the buttercream in another bag. You can use a round piping tip but it''s not necessary.'),
('Blueberry_Macarons',23,'Pipe a ring of buttercream on one macaron shell, then pipe the filling in the center of that buttercream ring. Place the second shell on top. Continue until you have filled all macarons.'),
('Blueberry_Macarons',24,'Macarons must be stored in the refrigerator and are best eaten one or two days later. (if you can wait) '),
('Blueberry_Macarons',25,'Enjoy!'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',1,'Using a food processor crush the graham crackers until bread crumb consistency. Alternatively, place them in a ziplock bag and crush them with a rolling pin.'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',2,'Add melted butter and sugar. Combine well so there are no dry crumbs.'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',3,'Pour into the tart pan and use the back of the spoon or glass to press the crumbs into the pan.'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',4,'Place the tart in the freezer for an hour.'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',5,'Pulse the blueberries in a food processor or blender until smooth.'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',6,'Sieve thru a fine mesh to remove the skin.'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',7,'Use the amount requested in this recipe.'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',8,'Sprinkle gelatin over the cold milk. Stir and set aside for 3 to 5 minutes.'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',9,'In a heavy-bottom saucepan, heat the cream & sugar until sugar dissolves and cream comes to an almost boil.'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',10,'Add the vanilla and the soaked gelatin milk.'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',11,'Continue to cook until the gelatin is all dissolved and the mixture is well heated thru.'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',12,'Take the mixture off the heat.'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',13,'Sieve the mixture thru a mesh to get any undissolved gelatin or remaining blueberry skin. (this is your white panna cotta mixture).'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',14,'Take ½ cup of the white pannacotta mixture in a bowl and add the blueberry puree – and combine well.'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',15,'Gently pour half the mixture into the cooled/partially frozen tart shell. ( I prefer to pour over the back of a spoon for a gentle pour).'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',16,'Carefully, place the tart in the fridge and let chill for 30 minutes to an hour until the top is almost set.'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',17,'For the second layer – Add only half of the remaining white mixture to the blueberry pannacotta mixture.'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',18,'Gently pour only half the blueberry panna cotta mixture over the chilled first layer. (I prefer to pour over the back of a spoon for a gentle pour).'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',19,'Carefully place the tart in the fridge and chill again for 30 minutes to an hour until the top is almost set.'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',20,'Lastly, combine both the remaining panna cotta mixtures (white and blue).'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',21,'Gently pour the mixture over the previous cooled layers. (I prefer to pour over the back of a spoon for a gentle pour).'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',22,'Carefully place the tart in the fridge and this time chill for at least 4 hours until the pannacotta is set.'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',23,'Decorate with fresh blueberries and whipped cream as shown in the video.'),
('Blueberry_Panna_Cotta_Tart_Recipe',24,'Enjoy!'),
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',1,'Use a pairing knife and trim excess fat from the leg of lamb. Pat it dry and set aside.'),
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',2,'You can put all the marinade ingredients in a food processor and blend until smooth.'),
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',3,'Alternatively, If you use a mortar and pestle, like me, start by crushing the salt and pepper, followed by the garlic, and thyme. Then, add the cumin, paprika, and olive oil. ');
INSERT INTO public.chef_kaggle_steps (recipe_id,position,instruction) VALUES
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',4,'Marinate the leg of lamb inside and all around.'),
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',5,'Place the sprigs of rosemary and thyme inside the leg of lamb. Place in a glass, or ceramic bowl, and cover with plastic wrap (do not use aluminum bowls to marinate meat as it causes oxidization).'),
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',6,'Marinate the lamb for 2 hours on the counter or up to overnight in the fridge. '),
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',7,'In a small bowl, combine the honey, lemon, zest, salt, and pepper - set aside.'),
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',8,'Thaw the leg of lamb an hour or two before roasting.'),
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',9,'Preheat the oven at 375 F or 160 C for at least 20 minutes.'),
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',10,'Remove the herbs from inside the leg of lamb and place them in the roasting rack (that way they won''t be in the slices when we cut and serve the meat later).'),
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',11,'Roll the lamb and use butcher''s twine to tie it together (see video).'),
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',12,'Place the lamb on the roasting rack along with the herbs.'),
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',13,'Brush the lamb with the prepared honey lemon glaze.'),
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',14,'I insert my oven-safe meat thermometer in the middle, thickest part of the meat.'),
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',15,'Roast for about 65 to 60 minutes until the internal temperature of the meat reaches 135 F. '),
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',16,'Baste it once in between with the honey lemon glaze.'),
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',17,'Remove from the oven. '),
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',18,'Move the lamb to a serving platter and cover with aluminum foil - let rest at least 20 minutes to help the juices settle.'),
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',19,'Place the roasting rack on medium-low heat with ½ cup water. '),
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',20,'Add the wine and use a flat spatula to deglaze the pan scraping as much as you can, but avoid the burnt parts.'),
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',21,'Then, add the flour and continue to thicken. '),
('Boneless_Leg_of_Lamb',22,'Strain the gravy through a sieve or mesh and pour the gravy in a sauceboat.'),
('Braided_Apple_Puff_Pastry',1,'Peel, core, and slice the apples into small cubes.'),
('Braided_Apple_Puff_Pastry',2,'Add a pinch of salt and lemon juice.'),
('Braided_Apple_Puff_Pastry',3,'Followed by the sugar, flour, and cinnamon.'),
('Braided_Apple_Puff_Pastry',4,'Cook on medium heat for 3 to 5 minutes.'),
('Braided_Apple_Puff_Pastry',5,'Let cool completely.'),
('Braided_Apple_Puff_Pastry',6,'Preheat the oven at 200 C/ 390 F.'),
('Braided_Apple_Puff_Pastry',7,'Open the chilled puff pastry on a floured surface.'),
('Braided_Apple_Puff_Pastry',8,'Roll into a rectangle about the size of a sheet pan 13 x 9 (approximately).'),
('Braided_Apple_Puff_Pastry',9,'Mark the puff pastry sheet into three lengthways so it will give you three panels. The center panel will hold the filling and the sides will be flipped over.'),
('Braided_Apple_Puff_Pastry',10,'Place the apple filling in the center evenly.'),
('Braided_Apple_Puff_Pastry',11,'Cut off two corners (triangles) from the top and bottom - see video'),
('Braided_Apple_Puff_Pastry',12,'Using a sharp knife or pizza wheel, cut slanting strips along both sides of the pastry.'),
('Braided_Apple_Puff_Pastry',13,'Fold both ends at the top and bottom over the filling (this will prevent the filling coming out when baking).'),
('Braided_Apple_Puff_Pastry',14,'Braid the pastry by crossing the strips over the filling overlapping each other (see video).'),
('Braided_Apple_Puff_Pastry',15,'When you reach the end, you can overlap any excess strips or cut them off.'),
('Braided_Apple_Puff_Pastry',16,'Pick the pastry with the parchment paper and transfer it to the baking tray.'),
('Braided_Apple_Puff_Pastry',17,'Brush the pastry with egg wash and sprinkle brown sugar.'),
('Braided_Apple_Puff_Pastry',18,'Bake in the preheated oven for about 30 to 35 minutes until the top is crisp and golden brown.'),
('Braided_Apple_Puff_Pastry',19,'When baked, cool in the pan for 10 minutes.'),
('Braided_Apple_Puff_Pastry',20,'Use a long pallet knife or spatula to move the long pastry so it won''t break.'),
('Braided_Apple_Puff_Pastry',21,'Serve at room temperature or warm -  just on its own or with a dollop of ice cream.'),
('Braised_Lamb_in_Red_Wine',1,'Using a chef''s knife and sturdy cutting board, cut the lamb into 2-inch cubes. Pat dry to remove any excess moisture.Tip - Ensure the meat is dry so it will sear not stew when browning.'),
('Braised_Lamb_in_Red_Wine',2,'Season with salt and pepper. Then, coat generously with flour. Dust off any excess flour.Tip - The flour adds caramelization and also helps thicken the sauce. But, any excess can burn in the oil giving it a bitter taste. So, dust off well any excess flour.'),
('Braised_Lamb_in_Red_Wine',3,'In a heavy-bottom pan or Dutch oven, over medium to high heat, add 1 tbsp oil and add the meat pieces. Do not crowd the pan. Do this in batches.Tip - Adding too many pieces at once will stew not sear, so best to do this in batches. '),
('Braised_Lamb_in_Red_Wine',4,'Use a meat tong to turn the meat and get an even color on all sides. Adjust the heat from medium to high, so you get good caramelization. Remove from the pan and set aside. Tip - If the meat is stuck to the pan, do not forcibly remove it. It means it needs more time. Try again in a minute. '),
('Braised_Lamb_in_Red_Wine',5,'To the same pan, add the remaining oil, and saute the onions, garlic, carrots, and celery until onions are translucent - about 4 minutes. '),
('Braised_Lamb_in_Red_Wine',6,'Then, add the brown sugar and saute until the brown sugar is also well caramelized - about 2 minutes. Tip - Caramelizing the sugar adds flavor and color. So, do this gently on low heat without burning the sugar. '),
('Braised_Lamb_in_Red_Wine',7,'Next, add the red wine and deglaze the pan. Let it come to a boil and simmer for 2 minutes. This will reduce the wine and concentrate the flavors.'),
('Braised_Lamb_in_Red_Wine',8,'Next, add the crushed tomatoes and vinegar. Season with salt and pepper.'),
('Braised_Lamb_in_Red_Wine',9,'Then, return the lamb back to the pan followed by the broth. '),
('Braised_Lamb_in_Red_Wine',10,'Add the fresh rosemary and thyme. Give it all a good stir. Bring to a boil.'),
('Braised_Lamb_in_Red_Wine',11,'Cover the pan, lower the heat to a simmer and cook on low for 1 to 1 ½ hour or until the meat is fork-tender. Tip - The cut of meat and the size of the pieces you use, will determine the time it needs to cook. Leg of lamb cut into 2-inch pieces will take about 1 ¼ hour. Lamb stew meat will take about an hour. Lamb shanks usually take me about 1 ½ hours. '),
('Braised_Lamb_in_Red_Wine',12,'Make sure to stir occasionally. If necessary, add ¼ to ½ cup water to ensure it does not burn at the bottom. Tip - If you use a Duch oven like me, you won''t need to add water as it retains moisture. But, a pan with a lid, where steams escapes, will need a little water over time. So, keep an eye and stir as necessary. '),
('Braised_Lamb_in_Red_Wine',13,'When done, taste and adjust seasoning. Check consistency and if necessary add a little more water. '),
('Braised_Lamb_in_Red_Wine',14,'Sprinkle chopped parsley for garnish before serving. '),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',1,'Preheat the oven at 190 C/ 380 F '),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',2,'Clean the mushrooms well by wiping them with a moist paper towel.'),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',3,'Remove the stalks gently so you do not break the mushrooms'),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',4,'Using a teaspoon carefully scrape off the gills to create more space (inside of the mushroom caps).'),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',5,'Chop the mushrooms stalks finely and add them to the chopped onions.'),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',6,'Line a baking tray with Aluminium foil for easy cleanup.'),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',7,'Coat the foil with olive oil to prevent the mushrooms from sticking.'),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',8,'Then lightly coat the mushroom caps with olive oil. This will prevent them from drying out.'),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',9,'Pulse the bread slices in the food processor until they are fine crumb consistency.'),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',10,'In a mixing bowl add all the filling ingredients'),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',11,'Chopped mushrooms stalks'),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',12,'Both fresh and dried breadcrumbs'),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',13,'Minced garlic, and cooked onions (optional)'),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',14,'Chopped herbs,'),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',15,'Grated cheeses'),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',16,'Season with salt and Pepper to taste (use less salt as the cheese is salty)'),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',17,'Mix well – then drizzle two tbsp of Olive Oil'),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',18,'Hold each mushroom in your palm and gently stuff the cavity with the bread crumb stuffing.'),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',19,'Place them on the baking tray.'),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',20,'Drizzle with remaining Olive Oil'),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',21,'Bake in a preheated oven for about 20 to 25 minutes until the tops are nice and golden.'),
('Breadcrumb_Stuffed_Mushrooms',22,'Garnish with fresh cilantro or parsley before serving.'),
('Breaded_Chicken_Breast_Pan_Fried',1,'Cut each chicken breast horizontally into two, so you have 8 slices. Use a mallet, meat tenderizer or rolling pin to flatten the pieces Pro tip - you can also ask your butcher to butterfly and prepare these for you as well. '),
('Breaded_Chicken_Breast_Pan_Fried',2,'Pat dry the chicken pieces, season with salt and pepper. Set aside to marinate for a while'),
('Breaded_Chicken_Breast_Pan_Fried',3,'In a bowl and whisk, combine egg, yogurt, mustard, salt, and pepper. Then, add the flour and combine well. Make sure there are no lumps.Pro tip- any lumps will prevent the mixture from sticking to the chicken and it will cook as lumps. '),
('Breaded_Chicken_Breast_Pan_Fried',4,'Add the chicken pieces to the marinade and let marinate for 15 minutes to an hour.Pro tip - you can leave this to marinate for up to 2 hours. '),
('Breaded_Chicken_Breast_Pan_Fried',5,'In a flat tray or shallow dish or plate, combine breadcrumb, sesame seeds, and parsley. Season with salt and pepper. Combine well. Pro tip - make sure you season well and combine well so you don''t have uneven seasoning around the chicken'),
('Breaded_Chicken_Breast_Pan_Fried',6,'Using a fork, pick a piece of chicken from the marinade and generously coat it with the breadcrumb mixture (see video).Pro tip - I like to use one hand for the wet chicken and the other for the dry breadcrumb mixture. This prevents the breadcrumbs from getting lump. '),
('Breaded_Chicken_Breast_Pan_Fried',7,'Set aside while you do all the rest of the chicken pieces. Pro tip - you can prepare the coated chicken pieces and leave them in the fridge for up to 12 hours. '),
('Breaded_Chicken_Breast_Pan_Fried',8,'To a frying pan (preferably non-stick), add 1 tbsp oil and 1 tbsp butter. Place three to four chicken pieces (do not overcrowd the pan).Pro tip - the butter gives the breadcrumbs a nice golden color and makes the chicken crispy. '),
('Breaded_Chicken_Breast_Pan_Fried',9,'Let cook on one side without touching for one minute on medium-high. Reduce the heat to medium-low and cook the chicken for 2 minutes more.Pro tip - avoid turning too often as this will prevent you from getting that beautiful golden color. '),
('Breaded_Chicken_Breast_Pan_Fried',10,'Flip the chicken, add another tablespoon of butter or oil as necessary.'),
('Breaded_Chicken_Breast_Pan_Fried',11,'Cook on the second side for one minute on medium-high. Then, lower the heat and cook for another minute on medium-low.Pro tip - The one-minute high-heat cooking is what makes the crust crispy. But, be careful not to burn it.'),
('Breaded_Chicken_Breast_Pan_Fried',12,'Remove the chicken on a clean paper hand towel to absorb excess fat.'),
('Breaded_Chicken_Breast_Pan_Fried',13,'Continue with the rest of the chicken pieces. Pro tip - it is best to clean the pan if you have any burnt breadcrumbs otherwise the burnt crumbs will stick to the next batch of chicken and burn some more. '),
('Brioche_Loaf___Pullman_Sandwich_Loaf',1,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the hook attachment, combine – warm milk, yeast, sugar, and eggs.Tip - while most doughs can be kneaded by hand, a brioche is rich in butter so, it is best to use a stand mxier for kneading. '),
('Brioche_Loaf___Pullman_Sandwich_Loaf',2,'Combine salt with the flour, then add it to the mixer as well. Knead on medium speed for about a minute scraping the sides of the bowl.Tip - Always make sure the salt is well incorporated in the flour before you add it to the yeast.'),
('Brioche_Loaf___Pullman_Sandwich_Loaf',3,'Once all the flour is incorporated. Knead the dough for two minutes until smooth. The dough will be soft and sticky – that''s ok.'),
('Brioche_Loaf___Pullman_Sandwich_Loaf',4,'Next, add the soft room temperature butter one cube at a time. Once all the butter is in, knead again for 2 to 4 minutes until smooth and elastic, and soft.Tip - this is a very soft and loose dough, so, resist the temptation to add more flour. '),
('Brioche_Loaf___Pullman_Sandwich_Loaf',5,'Remove the dough from the mixer bowl onto a lightly floured surface. Shape into a smooth ball. '),
('Brioche_Loaf___Pullman_Sandwich_Loaf',6,'Place in an oiled bowl and cover with plastic wrap or damp kitchen cloth. Leave to rise in a warm place for about an hour until doubled in volume.'),
('Brioche_Loaf___Pullman_Sandwich_Loaf',7,'Then, punch the dough down. Cover again and let rise in the fridge for 6 hours up to 12 hours.'),
('Brioche_Loaf___Pullman_Sandwich_Loaf',8,'At this point, the dough will be very chilled and firm (because it’s a butter-rich dough).'),
('Brioche_Loaf___Pullman_Sandwich_Loaf',9,'Invert on to a lightly floured surface. Knead for just 30 seconds to make it smooth and pliable again.'),
('Brioche_Loaf___Pullman_Sandwich_Loaf',10,'First, make a ball then roll it into a nice tight sausage shape the length of the Pullman pan.'),
('Brioche_Loaf___Pullman_Sandwich_Loaf',11,'Place into a sprayed Pullman loaf pan seam side down. Cover loaf pan with plastic wrap.');
INSERT INTO public.chef_kaggle_steps (recipe_id,position,instruction) VALUES
('Brioche_Loaf___Pullman_Sandwich_Loaf',12,'Let rise in a warm place. This can take about 90 minutes up to 2 hours (because we started with chilled dough).'),
('Brioche_Loaf___Pullman_Sandwich_Loaf',13,'Once you see your dough is almost halfway up the sides – spray the cover of the Pullman pan lid and place it on.Tip - you want to place the lid on before it rises to the top so you don''t ruin the rise. '),
('Brioche_Loaf___Pullman_Sandwich_Loaf',14,'Preheat the oven to 170 C / 350 F for at least 10 minutes.'),
('Brioche_Loaf___Pullman_Sandwich_Loaf',15,'Place the loaf pan on the center rack in the hot oven. Bake for about 30 to 40 minutes '),
('Brioche_Loaf___Pullman_Sandwich_Loaf',16,'The bread is done when you tap the bottom of your loaf and you will hear a hollow sound.'),
('Brioche_Loaf___Pullman_Sandwich_Loaf',17,'Partially open the lid and let cool for 10 minutes – before you remove and let cool completely.'),
('Brioche_Loaf___Pullman_Sandwich_Loaf',18,'Always let bread rest for at least an hour before you cut – I know it’s hard but it will keep the bread moist.'),
('Brioche_Loaf___Pullman_Sandwich_Loaf',19,'Enjoy!'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',1,'Combine flour and salt well.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',2,'In the mixer bowl, combine - warm milk, yeast, sugar, and eggs.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',3,'Add flour to the mixer as well.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',4,'Knead on medium speed scraping the sides of the bowl.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',5,'Once all the flour is incorporated, knead the dough for two minutes until smooth.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',6,'The dough will be soft and sticky - that''s ok.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',7,'Next, gradually add the soft room temperature butter, one cube at a time.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',8,'Once all the butter is in, knead again for 2 minutes until smooth and elastic and soft.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',9,'Remove the dough from the mixer bowl.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',10,'Form into a smooth ball.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',11,'Place in an oiled bowl and cover with plastic wrap or damp kitchen cloth.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',12,'Leave to rise in a warm place for about an hour until doubled in volume.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',13,'Then, punch the dough down and form into a ball.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',14,'Cover again and let rise in the fridge for 6 hours up to 12 hours.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',15,'At this point, the dough will be very chilled and firm (because it''s a butter-rich dough).'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',16,'Invert on to a lightly floured surface.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',17,'Knead for just 30 seconds to make it smooth and pliable again.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',18,'Divide the dough into 5 portions.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',19,'Shape each portion into a tight ball, tucking seams under.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',20,'Then, shape each ball into a sausage.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',21,'Place these into a sprayed loaf pan.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',22,'Cover loaf pan with plastic wrap.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',23,'Let rise in a warm place. This can take about 90 minutes up to 2 hours (because we started with chilled dough).'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',24,'Once you see your dough is almost halfway up the sides'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',25,'Preheat the oven to 170 C / 340 F for at least 10 minutes.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',26,'Brush the loaf with beaten egg ( use only egg yolk/water mixture for a darker color).'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',27,'Place the loaf pan on the center rack in the hot oven.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',28,'Bake the smaller loaves for about 30 to 35 minutes.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',29,'The bread is done when you tap the bottom of your loaf and you will hear a hollow sound.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',30,'Partially open the lid and let cool for 10 minutes - before you remove and let cool completely.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',31,'Always let bread rest for at least an hour before you cut it - I know it''s hard but it will keep the bread moist.'),
('Brioche_Sandwich_Bread_Recipe',32,'Enjoy!'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',1,'Preheat the oven to 170 C/ 340 F.'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',2,'Grease and line 3 x 6-inch round cake pans or 2 x 7-inch round cake pans.'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',3,'Dry ingredients - In a bowl combine flour with baking powder, nutmeg, and salt - set aside.'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',4,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the paddle attachment, cream the brown butter and sugars until light and fluffy.'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',5,'Add the eggs one at a time. Followed by the vanilla extract.'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',6,'Next, add the flour mixture along with the whipping cream. Scrape the bottom of the bowl to ensure you have a smooth mixture. '),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',7,'Divide batter equally between the prepared baking pans.Tip - I like to use cake strips to ensure my layer cakes bake flat.'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',8,'Bake for 30 to 35 minutes or until a skewer inserted in the center comes clean.'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',9,'Cool in the baking pan for 5 minutes. Invert and cool on a wire rack completely before you decorate.'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',10,'In a bowl of a stand mixer with the paddle attachment cream the butter until smooth.'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',11,'Add salt and vanilla – mix a minute longer, until well combined'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',12,'Then, add the powdered sugar one cup at a time'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',13,'Once all the powdered sugar has been incorporated. Gradually add the whipping cream while the mixer is still running. '),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',14,'Continue to mix on medium-high for 2 to 3 minutes more until you have a light and fluffy buttercream.'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',15,'The cream in the mixture will whip and give you almost stiff peaks.Tip- If the buttercream is too soft, you haven''t whipped enough. However, If the butter is melting chill the bowl for 10 minutes then whip again. (this can happen in warmer temperatures)'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',16,'Prepare simple syrup - cool completely before using.Tip- Simple syrup is just sugar water that has been boiled and cooled. Used to keep cake layers moist.'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',17,'Using a bread knife or cake leveler cut the domes off the cake layers'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',18,'Brush each layer with the cooled simple syrup'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',19,'Place a cake layer on the cake board or cake stand'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',20,'Top with a big dollop of buttercream - spread evenly using a straight-edge spatula.'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',21,'Then top the second cake layer on top followed by more buttercream and the last layer.'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',22,'Place the cake in the fridge to chill for 10 to 15 minutes.Tip - Chilling the cake at this point will ensure the layers don''t move when you frost the outside. Though, if you leave the cake uncovered in the fridge for too long it can dry out. So, 10 minutes is all you need.'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',23,'Smear the remaining buttercream around and top of the cake.Tip - A straight-edge spatula fo the top, an off-set spatula and bench scraper for the sides work better.'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',24,'For a naked cake-effect scrape off as much buttercream from the outside of the cake with a bench scraper.'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',25,'Place any remaining frosting in a piping bag with a star tip and pipe a border or swirls on top of the cake.'),
('Brown_Butter_Cake',26,'Enjoy!'),
('Butter_Chicken_in_20_minutes',1,'In a glass or stainless mixing bowl, combine the yogurt, all the spices, ginger, garlic, and lemon juice. Combine well.'),
('Butter_Chicken_in_20_minutes',2,'You can leave this to marinate for 15 minutes on the counter up to 12 hours in the refrigerator.'),
('Butter_Chicken_in_20_minutes',3,'In a skillet or saute pan, add oil and ghee.'),
('Butter_Chicken_in_20_minutes',4,'Add the whole spices – saute 30 seconds.'),
('Butter_Chicken_in_20_minutes',5,'Then, add the chicken with marinade.'),
('Butter_Chicken_in_20_minutes',6,'Stir fry for 2 minutes on medium-high.'),
('Butter_Chicken_in_20_minutes',7,'Then, add the tomato paste – combine well.'),
('Butter_Chicken_in_20_minutes',8,'Cover and cook for 15 minutes.'),
('Butter_Chicken_in_20_minutes',9,'Open pan, taste and adjust seasoning.'),
('Butter_Chicken_in_20_minutes',10,'Garnish with cilantro leaves.'),
('Butter_Chicken_in_20_minutes',11,'Server over steamed rice, chapati or naan.'),
('Buttermilk_Crispy_Chicken',1,'Skin, wash, pat dry the chicken drumsticks. Season salt and pepper.'),
('Buttermilk_Crispy_Chicken',2,'In a mixing bowl combine the buttermilk, egg, garlic powder, mustard, and flour. Season with salt and pepperTip - this chicken can be marinated for an hour on the counter or up to overnight in the fridge'),
('Buttermilk_Crispy_Chicken',3,'Add the chicken pieces and combine well. Leave to marinate for 30 minutes up to overnight in the fridge'),
('Buttermilk_Crispy_Chicken',4,'Pulse the cornflakes in a food processor until it resembles breadcrumb consistencyTip - you want thick breadcrumb consistency, not fine breadcrumb consistency. '),
('Buttermilk_Crispy_Chicken',5,'In a bowl combine all the dry ingredients - cornflakes, Parmesan, salt, and pepper. '),
('Buttermilk_Crispy_Chicken',6,'Preheat the oven at 200 C / 390 FTip - If you chose to marinate the chicken overnight - make sure to remove it out of the fridge for at least an hour.'),
('Buttermilk_Crispy_Chicken',7,'Using a fork to work with, add one piece of chicken into the cornflake coating. Coat it generously with the mixture'),
('Buttermilk_Crispy_Chicken',8,'Shake off any excess and place the coated chicken pieces on a parchment-lined baking tray.'),
('Buttermilk_Crispy_Chicken',9,'Lightly spray the chicken pieces with cooking spray.Tip - a spray works best to give a light coating if you don''t have an oil spray you can use oil and a pastry brush too. '),
('Buttermilk_Crispy_Chicken',10,'Baked in the oven on the center rack for 20 to 25 minutes. Turn the chicken pieces over and spray one more time. Tip - try to spray the chicken evenly so you have an even color when baked. Otherwise, yo will have parts that will look pale and dry. '),
('Buttermilk_Crispy_Chicken',11,'Bake for another 20 to 25 minutes until lightly golden. Remove the oven and let cool for 10 minutes before serving'),
('Butternut_Squash_Fries',1,'Preheat the oven to 220 C/ 428 F.'),
('Butternut_Squash_Fries',2,'Line a baking tray with parchment paper for easy cleanup - set aside'),
('Butternut_Squash_Fries',3,'To clean the butternut squash cut off the two ends at the top and bottom. Use a vegetable peeler and peel the squash. '),
('Butternut_Squash_Fries',4,'Then, use a large chef''s knife to split the squash in two. Remove the seed and cut each half in half, then, cut each half into four or five slices.'),
('Butternut_Squash_Fries',5,'Place the slices in a bowl, add salt, pepper, and olive oil. And any additional seasoning like paprika, thyme, rosemary, etc.'),
('Butternut_Squash_Fries',6,'Layer the slices on the prepared baking tray'),
('Butternut_Squash_Fries',7,'Bake for about 20 to 25 minutes until cooked through. '),
('Butternut_Squash_Fries',8,'Serve immediately '),
('Butterscotch_Buttercream_Frosting___2_Methods',1,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the paddle attachment cream the butter and salt until pale, light, and fluffy Pro-tip - the butter must be room temperature otherwise it will make a lumpy buttercream '),
('Butterscotch_Buttercream_Frosting___2_Methods',2,'Next, add the butterscotch sauce in two batches making sure to combine well. Pro-tip - the mixing will look very soft, loose, and almost curdled. Just keep whipping.'),
('Butterscotch_Buttercream_Frosting___2_Methods',3,'Next, add the powdered sugar and continue to whip. Once all the powdered sugar is well-combined turn the mixer to medium-high and whip for three full minutes until light and fluffyPro-tip - the butter and cream in the butterscotch sauce will whip into a light and airy buttercream so don''t skip the whipping.  '),
('Butterscotch_Buttercream_Frosting___2_Methods',4,'Finally, add the vanilla extract and combine well. ');
INSERT INTO public.chef_kaggle_steps (recipe_id,position,instruction) VALUES
('Butterscotch_Buttercream_Frosting___2_Methods',5,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the paddle attachment, whip the butterscotch sauce with the premade buttercream until light and fluffy. Pro-tip - if you don''t whip enough the buttercream will be a soft consistency. '),
('Butterscotch_Cake_for_Two',1,'Preheat the oven at 325 °F/ 165 °C / Gas Mark 3'),
('Butterscotch_Cake_for_Two',2,'Grease and dust with flour 2 x 6 oz ramekins for baking.'),
('Butterscotch_Cake_for_Two',3,'In a bowl, combine flour, baking powder, baking soda, and salt – Set aside'),
('Butterscotch_Cake_for_Two',4,'In a bowl, cream butter and sugar until light and fluffy. Add the eggs followed by the whipping cream and vanilla extract.  '),
('Butterscotch_Cake_for_Two',5,'Finally, add the flour mixture and combine well but do not overmix. '),
('Butterscotch_Cake_for_Two',6,'Divide batter between the two ramekins. Smooth the top. '),
('Butterscotch_Cake_for_Two',7,'Bake for about 18 to 20 mins until a skewer inserted in the center comes clean'),
('Butterscotch_Cake_for_Two',8,'Serve warm or at room temperature.'),
('Butterscotch_Cake_for_Two',9,'This cake is delicious on its own but a dollop of ice cream or butterscotch on the side would work wonderfully too.'),
('Butterscotch_Cake_for_Two',10,'Enjoy!'),
('Butterscotch_Cupcakes_with_Butterscotch_Buttercream',1,'Preheat the oven to 160 C / 320 F.'),
('Butterscotch_Cupcakes_with_Butterscotch_Buttercream',2,'Prepare baking cups or cupcake wrappers in a muffin tray. '),
('Butterscotch_Cupcakes_with_Butterscotch_Buttercream',3,'Cream butter and sugar until light and fluffy. '),
('Butterscotch_Cupcakes_with_Butterscotch_Buttercream',4,'Add eggs one at a time scraping the sides of the bowl often.'),
('Butterscotch_Cupcakes_with_Butterscotch_Buttercream',5,'Next, add cream and all-purpose flour in three batches.'),
('Butterscotch_Cupcakes_with_Butterscotch_Buttercream',6,'Lastly, add vanilla.'),
('Butterscotch_Cupcakes_with_Butterscotch_Buttercream',7,'Use an ice cream scoop to distribute the cupcakes evenly between 15 to 18 cupcakes wraps or 12 to 15 baking cups.'),
('Butterscotch_Cupcakes_with_Butterscotch_Buttercream',8,'Bake in a preheated oven for about 18 to 22 minutes or until the skewer inserted comes out clean.'),
('Butterscotch_Cupcakes_with_Butterscotch_Buttercream',9,'Chill Cupcake completely before you decorate.'),
('Butterscotch_Cupcakes_with_Butterscotch_Buttercream',10,'Make the butterscotch as directed in the recipe card below (more details on the individual post).'),
('Butterscotch_Cupcakes_with_Butterscotch_Buttercream',11,'Let the sauce cool completely so it won''t melt the buttercream.'),
('Butterscotch_Cupcakes_with_Butterscotch_Buttercream',12,'Use the amount needed to make buttercream and save the rest to drizzle on top. '),
('Butterscotch_Cupcakes_with_Butterscotch_Buttercream',13,'Make the buttercream as detailed in the recipe card below (more details on the individual post).'),
('Butterscotch_Cupcakes_with_Butterscotch_Buttercream',14,'You can place buttercream into a piping bag with your favorite piping tip and pipe a swirl. '),
('Butterscotch_Cupcakes_with_Butterscotch_Buttercream',15,'Alternatively, use a spatula to create a dome on the cupcake.'),
('Butterscotch_Cupcakes_with_Butterscotch_Buttercream',16,'Finally, use a spoon or small thin spatula to drizzle the butterscotch sauce over the cupcakes.'),
('Butterscotch_Cupcakes_with_Butterscotch_Buttercream',17,'These cupcakes will stay at room temperature in good weather for up to 2 days.'),
('Butterscotch_Cupcakes_with_Butterscotch_Buttercream',18,'In the fridge for about 4 days if wrapped well.'),
('Butterscotch_Fruitcake_Recipe',1,'Preheat the oven at 150 C/ 340 F.'),
('Butterscotch_Fruitcake_Recipe',2,'Grease and dust with flour a 9-inch bundt pan.'),
('Butterscotch_Fruitcake_Recipe',3,'Combine flour with salt, baking powder, baking soda, and spices.'),
('Butterscotch_Fruitcake_Recipe',4,'In a separate bowl – combine the dried fruits together.'),
('Butterscotch_Fruitcake_Recipe',5,'Add a few tablespoons of the flour mixture into the mixed fruits.'),
('Butterscotch_Fruitcake_Recipe',6,'Toss the fruit so each one is well coated in flour.'),
('Butterscotch_Fruitcake_Recipe',7,'Take a moment to separate the big lumps of fruit (especially the dates) and toss them in the flour.'),
('Butterscotch_Fruitcake_Recipe',8,'Set aside.'),
('Butterscotch_Fruitcake_Recipe',9,'Cream butter and light brown sugar until light and fluffy.'),
('Butterscotch_Fruitcake_Recipe',10,'Add eggs, one at a time, until well incorporated.'),
('Butterscotch_Fruitcake_Recipe',11,'Then, add the sour cream – and combine well.'),
('Butterscotch_Fruitcake_Recipe',12,'Next, add in the flour mixture – and combine well.'),
('Butterscotch_Fruitcake_Recipe',13,'Followed by the vanilla.'),
('Butterscotch_Fruitcake_Recipe',14,'Now, gently fold in the mixed fruits followed by the chopped cashews – do not over mix.'),
('Butterscotch_Fruitcake_Recipe',15,'Pour the batter into the prepared baking pan.'),
('Butterscotch_Fruitcake_Recipe',16,'Sprinkle the almond slices on top.'),
('Butterscotch_Fruitcake_Recipe',17,'Bake in a preheated oven for about 80 to 90 minutes or until a skewer inserted in the center comes clean.'),
('Butterscotch_Fruitcake_Recipe',18,'Cool in the baking tray for 10 minutes, then invert on a baking rack and cool completely.'),
('Butterscotch_Fruitcake_Recipe',19,'Lightly dust with confectioners sugar.'),
('Butterscotch_Fruitcake_Recipe',20,'Enjoy this fruitcake on its own. Or Serve with a side of butterscotch sauce for that added luxury.'),
('Butterscotch_Irish_Cream_Recipe',1,'In a small bowl, combine instant coffee with hot water - stir until it dissolves. Set aside'),
('Butterscotch_Irish_Cream_Recipe',2,'In a bowl or large measuring cup. Combine the butterscotch sauce, chocolate syrup, coffee, and vanilla. Using a whisk works better'),
('Butterscotch_Irish_Cream_Recipe',3,'Next, add in the cream followed by the evaporated milk.  You can use a hand blender to combine well.'),
('Butterscotch_Irish_Cream_Recipe',4,'Lastly, add the whiskey - combine well.'),
('Butterscotch_Irish_Cream_Recipe',5,'Pour into sterilized liquor storage bottles (these bottle seal properly so the alcohol won''t evaporate) '),
('Butterscotch_Irish_Cream_Recipe',6,'Store in the refrigerator for up to two months.'),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',1,'Preheat oven to 325 °F / 365 °C / Gas Mark 3'),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',2,'Grease and line two 7-inch round cake pans or 3 x 6-inch round cake pans '),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',3,'In a bowl, combine flour with baking powder, baking soda, and salt - set aside.'),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',4,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the whisk attachment whip the whole eggs on medium for two minutesTip - it is important that the eggs are warm or at least room temperature so we can get maximum volume. '),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',5,'Gradually start adding sugar one tablespoon at a time whipping constantly on medium speed. Once all the sugar is in; turn the mixer to medium-high and whip until light and fluffy – ribbon stageTip - adding the sugar helps improve the emulsification properties giving us the maximum volume. '),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',6,'Slowly add the cooking oil and buttermilk. Followed by the vanilla extract and almond extract. Tip - add the oil slowly but don''t overmix as we do not want the eggs to curdle. '),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',7,'Next, add in the flour mixture making sure you have no lumps. Continue to use the whisk but do not over whip at this time. Or you will lose all the volume in the eggs.Tip - Don''t overmix at this stage. We don''t want to lose volume or activate the gluten in our flour. .You can fold the flour into the batter with a spatula '),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',8,'Divide batter equally between the prepared baking pans.Tip - I like to use cake strips to ensure my layer cakes bake flat.'),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',9,'Bake for about 25 to 30 minutes or until a skewer inserted in the center comes out clean.'),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',10,'Cool in the pan for 5 minutes then invert on a cooling rack and cool completely before you store or decorate.Tip - Wrap in plastic wrap and place in the freezer for an hour. This will make fewer crumbs when torting and leveling the cake.'),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',11,'In a bowl of a stand mixer with the paddle attachment cream the butter until smooth.'),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',12,'Add salt, fresh cream and vanilla – mix a minute longer, until well combined'),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',13,'Then, add the powdered sugar one cup at a time'),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',14,'Once all the powder sugar has been incorporated. Continue to mix on medium-high for 2 to 3 minutes more until you have a light and fluffy buttercream.'),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',15,'The cream in the mixture will whip and give you almost stiff peaks.Tip- If the buttercream is too soft, you haven''t whipped enough. However, If the butter is melting chill the bowl for 10 minutes then whip again. (this can happen in warmer temperatures)'),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',16,'Prepare simple syrup - cool completely before using.Tip- Simple syrup is just sugar water that has been boiled and cooled. Used to keep cake layers moist.'),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',17,'Using a bread knife or cake leveler cut the domes off the cake layers. Cut each layer in half horizontally giving you a total of four layers. Brush each layer with the cooled simple syrup'),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',18,'Place a cake layer on the cake board or cake stand.Tip -if you plan to move the cake again, it is best to use a cake circle under the cake, so you can pick the cake with its base and without any accidents.'),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',19,'Top with a big dollop of buttercream – spread evenly using a straight-edge spatula. Sprinkle some chopped Cadbury egg pieces or chocolate.'),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',20,'Then top the second cake layer on top followed by buttercream and chopped Cadbury eggs or chocolate then top with the last cake. Until you have stacked all four layers of cake.Tip - it is best to lift individual cake layers on pieces of clean cardboard or cake lifter so you do not break them from table to cake.'),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',21,'Spread the remaining buttercream around and the top of the cake. I created horizontal lines on the side of the cake with a spatula (see video) Tip - A straight-edge spatula for the top, an off-set spatula, and a bench scraper for the sides work better.'),
('Cadbury_Creme_Egg_Cake',22,'Use the remaining buttercream to pipe swirls on top. Top each swirl with half a Cadbury cream egg.'),
('Cajun_Chicken_with_Rice',1,'Combine the cajun spice with the brown sugar, salt, and pepper - set aside.'),
('Cajun_Chicken_with_Rice',2,'Clean, pat dry the chicken pieces.'),
('Cajun_Chicken_with_Rice',3,'Generously sprinkle the chicken on both sides with the prepared cajun spice. (see video) '),
('Cajun_Chicken_with_Rice',4,'Let marinate for 30 mins up to 8 hours in the fridge.'),
('Cajun_Chicken_with_Rice',5,'Wash and soak the rice for 30 minutes. Then, drain and set aside.'),
('Cajun_Chicken_with_Rice',6,'In a skillet, on medium-heat, add 1 tbsp oil and 1 tbsp butter.'),
('Cajun_Chicken_with_Rice',7,'Add the chicken pieces and cook on both sides for 2 minutes each.'),
('Cajun_Chicken_with_Rice',8,'Remove the chicken from the pan - keep warm.'),
('Cajun_Chicken_with_Rice',9,'Add the remaining oil and butter.'),
('Cajun_Chicken_with_Rice',10,'Saute onions and garlic until onions are translucent.'),
('Cajun_Chicken_with_Rice',11,'Then, add the rice - saute for 2 minutes.'),
('Cajun_Chicken_with_Rice',12,'Next, add the cajun spice, and tomato paste - saute 30 seconds.'),
('Cajun_Chicken_with_Rice',13,'Add the chicken broth and season with salt and pepper.'),
('Cajun_Chicken_with_Rice',14,'Return the chicken back to the pan.'),
('Cajun_Chicken_with_Rice',15,'Add the cream and cilantro.'),
('Cajun_Chicken_with_Rice',16,'Bring to a boil. As soon as it comes to a boil - reduce heat to a minimum.'),
('Cajun_Chicken_with_Rice',17,'Cover and cook on low for 20 minutes.'),
('Cajun_Chicken_with_Rice',18,'Once the 20 minutes are done - keep it covered for another 15 minutes if possible - this will help all the excess moisture dry out.'),
('Cajun_Chicken_with_Rice',19,'Open the pan and fluff the rice.'),
('Cajun_Chicken_with_Rice',20,'Sprinkle with more chopped cilantro.'),
('Cake_Decorators_Chocolate_Ganache_Recipe',1,'Place chocolate in a heatproof bowl - set aside'),
('Cake_Decorators_Chocolate_Ganache_Recipe',2,'Pour cream in a saucepan and bring to an almost boil but do not boil. Tip - I heat it in the microwave for a minute at 100% - keep an eye so it does not overpour.'),
('Cake_Decorators_Chocolate_Ganache_Recipe',3,'Next, pour hot cream over the chocolate. Cover and let sit for two minutes. Stir until smooth.Tip: the heat in the cream should be just enough to melt the chocolate, so keep stirring. For some reason, if you still have bits of unmelted chocolate, place the bowl over another bowl of hot water and stir till melted.  A little heat is all it takes.');
INSERT INTO public.chef_kaggle_steps (recipe_id,position,instruction) VALUES
('Cake_Decorators_Chocolate_Ganache_Recipe',4,'Break the chocolate in a microwave-safe bowl. Pour cream over the chocolate'),
('Cake_Decorators_Chocolate_Ganache_Recipe',5,'Place the bowl in the microwave for a minute on high. Stir well until you have a smooth ganache'),
('Cake_Decorators_Chocolate_Ganache_Recipe',6,'If necessary - continue to heat in the microwave at 30-seconds intervals until you have a smooth mix.Tip: the heat in the cream should be just enough to melt the chocolate, so keep stirring.'),
('Cake_Decorators_Chocolate_Ganache_Recipe',7,'When cake decorating we do not use the ganache soon after it''s made. We let it rest.'),
('Cake_Decorators_Chocolate_Ganache_Recipe',8,'It''s best to let the ganache at room temperature or fridge for at least a couple of hours ( I usually keep it overnight)'),
('Cake_Decorators_Chocolate_Ganache_Recipe',9,'This helps set the ganache again and give it the stability we need for covering a cake. '),
('Cake_Decorators_Chocolate_Ganache_Recipe',10,'To use ganache we need a spreadable peanut butter consistency. Most often you need to give a good mix and it will be enough. But, in a cooler climate, you may need a 10 seconds burst in the microwave. Tip- chocolate melts easily so 10 seconds is a lot for chocolate. Any more and you will lose that spreadable consistency. '),
('Cake_Decorators_White_Chocolate_Ganache',1,'Place chocolate in a heatproof bowl - and set aside. Pour cream in a saucepan and bring to an almost boil but do not boil.'),
('Cake_Decorators_White_Chocolate_Ganache',2,'Next, pour hot cream over the chocolate. Cover and let sit for a minute.'),
('Cake_Decorators_White_Chocolate_Ganache',3,'Stir until smooth with a heatproof spatula.Pro tip: the heat in the cream should be just enough to melt the chocolate, so keep stirring. But, If you still have undissolved chocolate use a blender to blend to a smooth consistency.'),
('Cake_Decorators_White_Chocolate_Ganache',4,'Break the chocolate in a microwave-safe bowl. Pour cream over the chocolate.'),
('Cake_Decorators_White_Chocolate_Ganache',5,'Place the bowl in the microwave for a minute on high.'),
('Cake_Decorators_White_Chocolate_Ganache',6,'Stir with a silicone spatula well until you have a smooth ganache. If necessary - continue to heat in the microwave at 30-sec intervals until you have a smooth mix.Pro tip - White chocolate melts easily. So, try to use the heat in the cream to melt the chocolate rather than heat it. Overheated white chocolate can separate easily.'),
('Cake_Decorators_White_Chocolate_Ganache',7,'Ganache rested may not necessarily be ideal to just start using. Depending on your climate, it may be too firm or too soft. So, you still need to bring it to consistency. '),
('Cake_Decorators_White_Chocolate_Ganache',8,'The ideal consistency is peanut butter consistency. You want to be able to hold the ganache on the spatula and spread it around the cake.'),
('Cake_Decorators_White_Chocolate_Ganache',9,'The best way to bring it to the right consistency is:In cold weather - stick it in the microwave for 10 secs.Chilled ganache - If the ganache was in the fridge, keeping it out for an hour helps to bring it to the right consistency.Hot and humid climate - just a vigorous stir with a spatula is all you need because chocolate melts at room temperature. Pro tip - when it comes to chocolate 10 secs is a lot so don''t over-heat it'),
('Candied_Fruit_Fruitcake',1,'Preheat the oven to 170 C / 340 F'),
('Candied_Fruit_Fruitcake',2,'Grease and dust with flour an (8-inch) or 6-cup bundt pan. Alternatively, you can also use an 8 x 3-inch round pan or 9 x 4-inch loaf pan.'),
('Candied_Fruit_Fruitcake',3,'Candied fruit - Add 2 tbsp flour to the chopped candied fruit - set aside'),
('Candied_Fruit_Fruitcake',4,'Dry ingredients - In a bowl, combine flour, baking powder, baking soda, salt, and spices- set aside.'),
('Candied_Fruit_Fruitcake',5,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the paddle attachment cream the butter, cream cheese, and sugar until light and fluffy. Tip - make sure the cream cheese is at room temperature so it creams well and not get lumpy'),
('Candied_Fruit_Fruitcake',6,'Add the vanilla extract followed by the eggs one at a time. Tip - adding room temperature eggs one at a time will prevent the batter from curdling. '),
('Candied_Fruit_Fruitcake',7,'Add the flour and buttermilk in three additions. '),
('Candied_Fruit_Fruitcake',8,'Then add the candied fruit and the chopped nuts. Combine well.Tip - do not overmix at this point. The flour coating the fruit works as the glue holding on to the batter. Overmixing will cause the flour to blend into the batter and therefore sink to the bottom. '),
('Candied_Fruit_Fruitcake',9,'Pour into the prepared baking pan.  Bake in the preheated oven on the middle rack for 60 to 70 minutes until a skewer inserted in the center comes clean'),
('Candied_Fruit_Fruitcake',10,'Cool in the pan for 10 minutes then invert onto a cooling rack and cool completely. '),
('Candied_Fruit_Fruitcake',11,'Dust with powdered sugar (optional). Enjoy!'),
('Candied_Fruit_Shortbread_or_Tutti_Frutti_Bars',1,'Preheat the oven to 160C / 320 F'),
('Candied_Fruit_Shortbread_or_Tutti_Frutti_Bars',2,'Line an 8 x 8-inch square baking pan with parchment paper'),
('Candied_Fruit_Shortbread_or_Tutti_Frutti_Bars',3,'In a bowl - combine condensed milk and flour well.'),
('Candied_Fruit_Shortbread_or_Tutti_Frutti_Bars',4,'Add candied fruit, leave a few to sprinkle on top. Combine well'),
('Candied_Fruit_Shortbread_or_Tutti_Frutti_Bars',5,'Pour into the prepared baking pan'),
('Candied_Fruit_Shortbread_or_Tutti_Frutti_Bars',6,'Bake on the center rack for 20 minutes'),
('Candied_Fruit_Shortbread_or_Tutti_Frutti_Bars',7,'Cool in the pan for 10 minutes'),
('Candied_Fruit_Shortbread_or_Tutti_Frutti_Bars',8,'Cut into 16 squares as shown in the video'),
('Candied_Fruit_Shortbread_or_Tutti_Frutti_Bars',9,'If stored well, these squares will stay good for up to 2 weeks.'),
('Candy_Christmas_Cookies',1,'Preheat the oven at 180 C / 356 F.'),
('Candy_Christmas_Cookies',2,'Combine flour, salt, baking powder, and baking soda - Set aside.'),
('Candy_Christmas_Cookies',3,'Cream butter and sugar until light and fluffy.'),
('Candy_Christmas_Cookies',4,'Add vanilla followed by the egg.'),
('Candy_Christmas_Cookies',5,'Mix for two minutes until light and fluffy again.'),
('Candy_Christmas_Cookies',6,'Add flour mixture and combine well.'),
('Candy_Christmas_Cookies',7,'Use a cookie scooper to scoop dough onto a cookie sheet.'),
('Candy_Christmas_Cookies',8,'Sprinkle remaining crushed candy on each cookie.'),
('Candy_Christmas_Cookies',9,'Bake in the preheated oven for 10 to 12 minutes until lightly golden on the bottom.'),
('Candy_Christmas_Cookies',10,'Leave on the baking tray for 5 minutes then'),
('Candy_Christmas_Cookies',11,'Cool on a wire rack completely before you store in the cookie jar'),
('Candy_Christmas_Cookies',12,'These cookies will stay good for up to two weeks on the counter.'),
('Cantaloupe_Orange_Smoothie',1,'Add all ingredients except honey to a blender and blend until smooth'),
('Cantaloupe_Orange_Smoothie',2,'Taste and adjust sweetness - if necessary add the honey. '),
('Cantaloupe_Orange_Smoothie',3,'Pour into individual serving glasses '),
('Cantaloupe_Orange_Smoothie',4,'Enjoy!'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',1,'Preheat the oven to 170 C/340 F'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',2,'Grease and line 3  x 6 inch round pans or 2 x 8 inch round pans.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',3,'Mix the spices together and set aside.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',4,'Peel, core and chop apples into ½ inch pieces'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',5,'Add half the mixed spice and 3 tbsp flour (use from the measured flour)'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',6,'Combine well and set aside.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',7,'Combine together the flour with baking powder, baking soda, mixed spices, and salt'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',8,'set aside.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',9,'Cream butter and sugar until light and fluffy'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',10,'Add eggs one at a time'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',11,'Followed by the vanilla and applesauce'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',12,'Next, add the flour and buttermilk in three additions.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',13,'Lastly, add the chopped apples – combine well but do not over mix.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',14,'Divide the batter between the baking pans'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',15,'Spread the top so it’s an even layer.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',16,'Bake in the preheated oven for 25 to 30 minutes or until a skewer inserted comes clean.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',17,'Cool in the pan for 10 minutes then on a  wire rack until cool completely.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',18,'Place the sugar, lemon, and water in a deep light-colored pan (so you can see the color)'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',19,'With the heat on medium-low cook the sugar.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',20,'Shake the pan as you need but do not use a spoon. It is important to keep the heat on medium-low so the sugar will caramelize not burn.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',21,'Swirl the pan slowly guiding the heat distribution'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',22,'The sugar should now start to color into a golden amber.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',23,'One all the sugar is amber, add in the butter and whisk constantly.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',24,'Followed by the cream. (watch your hands and the mixer will rise when you add the butter and cream)'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',25,'Cool for a few minutes in the pan then pours into a glass jar or pot. As the mixture cools it will get thicker.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',26,'Place the butter and salt in the mixer bowl.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',27,'Using the paddle attachment – mix the butter until light and creamy.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',28,'Next, add half a cup of caramel sauce – combine well.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',29,'Add the remaining sauce – combine again.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',30,'Lastly, the powdered sugar – combine well.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',31,'Once all the ingredients have been added – whip for three minutes until the butterscotch is light and fluffy.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',32,'Level the apple cake layers if they have any dome.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',33,'Layer them with caramel buttercream frosting in between as shown in the video'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',34,'Frost the outside with more caramel buttercream – chilling in between steps as necessary.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',35,'Lastly, use the caramel sauce to create the drip as shown in the video.'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',36,'To decorate – put any remaining frosting in a piping bag with a piping nozzle'),
('Caramel_Apple_Cake_Recipe_with_Caramel_Buttercream',37,'Create some pattern on the top.'),
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',1,'Preheat oven to 160 C/ 320 F'),
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',2,'Prepare an 8-inch baking pan – grease and line with baking paper'),
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',3,'Mash bananas and set aside'),
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',4,'Sift or combine baking powder, baking soda, salt, spices, and flour'),
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',5,'Cream butter and sugar until light and creamy'),
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',6,'Add eggs one at a time, followed by vanilla extract'),
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',7,'Then add in the mashed banana'),
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',8,'Lastly, add in the flour and buttermilk in three batches – until well combined'),
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',9,'Pour into the prepared baking pan'),
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',10,'Bake for about 35 to 45 minutes until a skewer inserted in the center comes out clean.'),
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',11,'Cool completely before decorating');
INSERT INTO public.chef_kaggle_steps (recipe_id,position,instruction) VALUES
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',12,'Place the sugar, lemon, and water in a deep light colored pan (so you can see the color)'),
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',13,'With the heat on medium-low cook the sugar.'),
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',14,'Shake the pan as you need but do not use a spoon. It is important to keep the heat on medium-low so the sugar will caramelize not burn'),
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',15,'One all the sugar is amber, add in the butter and whisk constantly.'),
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',16,'Followed by the cream. (watch your hands and the mixer will rise when you add the butter and cream)'),
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',17,'Cool for a few minutes in the pan then pours into a glass jar or pot. As the mixture cools it will get thicker.'),
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',18,'Brush the cake with simple syrup'),
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',19,'Put the whipped cream in a piping bag with a large star tip. Pipe a border of whipped cream around the edges.'),
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',20,'Pour caramel on top and spread towards the edges. The whipped cream should hold the caramel in place.'),
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',21,'Place the cake the fridge to chill for a while so the caramel sets.'),
('Caramel_Banana_Cake',22,'Alternatively, skip the damn and let the caramel spill over the edges'),
('Caramel_Brownies',1,'Place the sugar, water, and corn syrup in a heavy-bottomed saucepan.'),
('Caramel_Brownies',2,'With the heat on medium, bring to a boil. Shake and swirl the pan slowly guiding the distribution of heat.'),
('Caramel_Brownies',3,'The sugar should now start to change color into a golden amber.'),
('Caramel_Brownies',4,'Once all the sugar is amber, add in the butter followed by the cream. Be careful as it will rise. If necessary take it off the heat until it settles. '),
('Caramel_Brownies',5,'Cool for a few minutes in the pan. Then, pour it into a glass jar or pot. As the mixture cools it will get thicker.'),
('Caramel_Brownies',6,'Use &frac13 cup for the brownie batter and the remaining for the top. You can use all or only as much as you want.'),
('Caramel_Brownies',7,'Preheat oven 170 C /340 F. Grease and line an 8 x 8-inch square cake pan with parchment paper leaving an overhang so you can pick the brownies out.'),
('Caramel_Brownies',8,'Dry ingredients - Whisk flour and salt in a bowl.'),
('Caramel_Brownies',9,'Melt butter and chocolate in the microwave-safe bowl or double boiler.'),
('Caramel_Brownies',10,'Add the caramel, followed by the sugar - combine until sugar is almost dissolved.'),
('Caramel_Brownies',11,'Add the eggs, one at a time. Followed by the vanilla extract.'),
('Caramel_Brownies',12,'Next, sift in the cocoa powder and flour mixture - combine well. Mix well until you have a smooth well-incorporated batter.'),
('Caramel_Brownies',13,'Pour into the prepared baking pan. Drizzle 4 tbsp of the caramel sauce (optional).'),
('Caramel_Brownies',14,'Bake at for 30 to 40 minutes. '),
('Caramel_Brownies',15,'Cool in the pan until barely warm. Then Drizzle the remaining caramel sauce'),
('Caramel_Brownies',16,'Let cool completely - so the caramel sets. Cut into 16 squares (see video).Tip - you will get neater slices with clean edges if you let the brownies chill for a bit. '),
('Caramel_Brownies',17,'Enjoy!'),
('Caramel_Buttercream_Frosting',1,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the paddle attachment cream the butter and salt until pale, light, and fluffy Pro-tip - the butter must be room temperature otherwise it will make a lumpy buttercream '),
('Caramel_Buttercream_Frosting',2,'Next, add the caramel sauce in two batches making sure to combine well. Pro-tip - the mixing will look very soft, loose, and almost curdled. Just keep whipping.'),
('Caramel_Buttercream_Frosting',3,'Next, add the powdered sugar and continue to whip. Once all the powdered sugar is well-combined turn the mixer to medium-high and whip for three full minutes until light and fluffyPro-tip - the butter and cream in the butterscotch sauce will whip into a light and airy buttercream so don''t skip the whipping.  '),
('Caramel_Buttercream_Frosting',4,'Finally, add the vanilla extract and combine well. '),
('Caramel_Buttercream_Frosting',5,'In the bowl of a stand mixer with the paddle attachment, whip the caramel sauce with the premade buttercream until light and fluffy. Pro-tip - if you don''t whip enough the buttercream will be a soft consistency. '),
('Caramel_Filing_for_Cakes_Tarts_and_Desserts',1,'Place brown sugar, golden syrup, and butter in a heavy-bottom saucepan over medium heat. Stir until all the butter has melted and the sugar has dissolved. Pro tip - Stir often and the heat to medium otherwise the sugar around the edges will burn and give the caramel a burnt taste. '),
('Caramel_Filing_for_Cakes_Tarts_and_Desserts',2,'Reduce the heat and continue to cook until the mixture becomes darker in color. This takes about 2 to 3 minutes. Pro tip - once all the moisture has evaporated the sugar will start to caramelize further. This will give the caramel a deeper color. '),
('Caramel_Filing_for_Cakes_Tarts_and_Desserts',3,'Next, reduce the heat to low. Add the condensed milk and let come to a boil on low heat again. Pro tip- when you add the condensed milk the mixture may appear curdled or separated but just combine and it will all become smooth. '),
('Caramel_Filing_for_Cakes_Tarts_and_Desserts',4,'Cook on low for about another minute or two stirring constantly. The mixture will get thicker. Add the vanilla extract and take it off the heat. Pro tip - we want a smooth creamy texture that coats the back of a spoon. '),
('Caramel_Filing_for_Cakes_Tarts_and_Desserts',5,'Set aside to cool slightly before you pour into a mason jar or fill a tart. Pro tip - The mixture will continue to thicken as it cools. You can pour warm caramel into a tart to help it smooth out easily. '),
('Caramel_Filing_for_Cakes_Tarts_and_Desserts',6,'Enjoy!'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',1,'Preheat the oven to 160 C / 320 F.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',2,'Line a muffin pan with cupcake liners.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',3,'Sift the flour with salt, baking powder, and baking soda.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',4,'Cream the butter and sugar until light and foamy.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',5,'Add the eggs, one at a time.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',6,'Next, add in the sour cream and flour mixture alternating in 3 batches.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',7,'Finally, add the vanilla extract.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',8,'Use an ice cream scoop to divide the batter between the 12 cupcake liner.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',9,'Bake in the preheated oven for about 18 to 20 minutes or until the skewer inserted in the center comes out clean.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',10,'Cool completely but do not put in the fridge.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',11,'Place the sugar, lemon, and water in a deep light-colored pan (so you can see the color).'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',12,'With the heat on medium-low, cook the sugar.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',13,'Shake and swirl the pan slowly guiding the heat distribution.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',14,'The sugar should now start to color into a golden amber.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',15,'Once all the sugar is amber, add in the butter and stir constantly.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',16,'Followed by the cream. (watch your hands and the caramel will rise when you add the butter and cream).'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',17,'Add the salt and barely combine'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',18,'Cool for a few minutes in the pan, then pour it into a mason jar or bowl.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',19,'As the mixture cools it will get thicker. At least 3 hours.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',20,'Place a pot with some water and let come to almost boil.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',21,'Place eggs whites, salt, cream of tartar, and sugar in a mixer bowl (or any stainless steel bowl).'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',22,'Place the mixer bowl over this hot water pot.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',23,'Use a whisk and start to whisk lightly. The sugar in the egg whites will start to melt.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',24,'Test the sugar with your fingers. Dip a clean finger in and rub the mixer between your fingers, if you feel the gains of sugar – continue to whisk.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',25,'When the sugar has melted, remove from heat.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',26,'Place the bowl on the mixer and start at medium to low speed with a whisk attachment. After a minute or two whip at medium to high speed.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',27,'Whisk to firm peaks, shiny meringue.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',28,'Touch the mixer bowl. If it’s still warm wait, run the mixer on low until it cools.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',29,'If it’s cool to touch, start adding your butter one cube at a time. (DO NOT ADD BUTTER TO WARM MERINGUE).'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',30,'After all the butter is added, run the mixer on high for two minutes more. This should give you a light, and airy cream.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',31,'Prepare a piping bag with caramel sauce (if necessary microwave the caramel for 10 seconds).'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',32,'Prepare another piping bag with Swiss meringue buttercream and your favorite piping nozzle.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',33,'Use a cupcake core or a melon baller to make a hole in the center of the cupcake.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',34,'Fill with caramel sauce. Place the core back on.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',35,'Pipe a buttercream swirl on top.'),
('Caramel_cupcakes_with_Swiss_meringue_buttercream_and_caramel_sauce',36,'Drizzle more melted caramel on the top as well.'),
('Caramelized_Onions_Roasted_Red_Peppers_Quiche',1,'Place flour, salt, and butter in a food processor.'),
