('Chicken_Schnitzel',15,'Then coat it with the breadcrumb mixture (bowl 3). Use your hands to press lightly making sure it''s well coated.'),
('Chicken_Schnitzel',16,'Remove from the breadcrumb mix and place it on a clean plate.'),
('Chicken_Schnitzel',17,'Do the same with all the pieces and set aside. These can be made up to two days and kept in the fridge'),
('Chicken_Schnitzel',18,'To a frying pan (preferably non-stick) add 1 tbsp oil and 1 tbsp butter'),
('Chicken_Schnitzel',19,'Place three to four chicken pieces (do not overcrowd the pan)'),
('Chicken_Schnitzel',20,'Let cook on one side without touching for one minute on medium-high. Reduce the heat to medium-low and cook the chicken for 2 minutes more'),
('Chicken_Schnitzel',21,'Flip the chicken, add another tablespoon of butter or oil as necessary'),
('Chicken_Schnitzel',22,'Cook on the second side for one minute on medium-high then lower the heat and cook for another minute on medium-low.'),
('Chicken_Schnitzel',23,'Tip - The one-minute high cooking is what makes the crust crispy. But, be careful not to burn it.'),
('Chicken_Schnitzel',24,'Remove the chicken on a clean paper hand towel to absorb excess fat.'),
('Chicken_Shawarma_Recipe',1,'Cut the chicken thighs and legs into two pieces. If using chicken breast leave them as they are.'),
('Chicken_Shawarma_Recipe',2,'Season with salt, pepper, and lemon juice.'),
