('Chicken_Shawarma_Recipe',22,'Drizzle some more tahini sauce.'),
('Chicken_Shawarma_Recipe',23,'Fold the bread over the filling – to make a wrap.'),
('Chicken_Shawarma_Recipe',24,'Alternatively, you can split a pita bread in half, fill it with salad, and chicken shawarma pieces. Drizzle with tahini sauce and serve.'),
('Chicken_Skewers___Grilled',1,'Prep Chicken - Clean, wash, and cut the chicken into bite-size pieces. Pat dry on a paper towel to remove excess moisture.Pro tip - Cut the chicken into about 1-inch pieces as too large will keep the chicken raw in the middle. Also, make sure the chicken is dry so the marinade will stick to it. '),
('Chicken_Skewers___Grilled',2,'Prep Veggies - Cut vegetables also into small pieces similar to the chicken. Cut each bell pepper in a quarter then each quarter into 4 pieces after taking off the stalk and seeds. Do the same with the onions and tomatoes if using large tomato. Pro tip - Prepare the veggies no more than 4 hours before cooking so they stay fresh. I like to add the chicken marinade into my veggies as well so they pick up flavor from the chicken. '),
('Chicken_Skewers___Grilled',3,'Soak the bamboo skewers in water for 30 minutes at least.Pro tip - Soaking the skewers in water will prevent them from burning on the grill so do not skip this step.  '),
('Chicken_Skewers___Grilled',4,'Marinade - Place all marinade ingredients in a bowl. Add the chicken pieces. Cover and set aside to marinate for an hour on the counter or up to 12 hours in the fridge. Pro tip - If you marinate for longer in the fridge, make sure to take the chicken out an hour before you plan to cook it. '),
('Chicken_Skewers___Grilled',5,'Skewer - Thread the chicken and vegetable pieces alternating each other. I prefer one piece of chicken one piece veggie or sometimes 1 piece of chicken and two pieces of veggies. Pro tip - The skewers can be prepared ahead of time and kept in the fridge for up to 4 hours. '),
('Chicken_Skewers___Grilled',6,'Heat a grill pan on medium-high heat. Place few skewers at a time - do not overcrowd the grill. Brush each skewer with cooking oil. Pro tip - The char marks on the chicken can be controlled by raising and lowing the heat under the grill.'),
('Chicken_Skewers___Grilled',7,'Let cook for at least 3 minutes before you try to move it. When it''s done on one side it will release from the pan. Turn to the other side and cook for 2 to 3 more minutes.Pro tip - As a guide, each skewer with chicken breast takes 5 to 6 minutes to cook on all sides. Skewer with chicken thigh meat will take about 8 to 10 minutes on all sides. '),
('Chicken_Skewers___Grilled',8,'Serve with fragrant rice or pita bread with tahini and hummus.'),
('Chicken_Stir_Fry',1,'Prep the chicken - Clean, wash, and pat dry the chicken. Cut into bite-size cubes.Tip - since I am using broccoli today I cut the chicken into one-inch cubes. But, you can also cut them into strips'),
('Chicken_Stir_Fry',2,'Marinade - In a bowl, combine all the marinade ingredients. Tip - It is best to use low sodium soy sauce which is less salty. But, if you use regular make sure to add less salt in the recipe.'),
('Chicken_Stir_Fry',3,'Marinate the chicken - Add the marinade to the chicken. Stir well and set aside. Tip - you can leave the chicken to marinate for 30 minutes on the counter or up to 12 hours in the fridge.'),
('Chicken_Stir_Fry',4,'Broccoli - Wash and separate broccoli into florets. Slice the stems into small pieces and keep them aside.  Tip - broccoli stems are tougher and take longer to cook so keep them on the side. We will add them to the pan earlier. '),
('Chicken_Stir_Fry',5,'Veggies - Slice the onions and separate the slices. Thinly slice the garlic and ginger. Roughly chop the parsley and scallions - set aside'),
('Chicken_Stir_Fry',6,'Sauce - Combine all the sauce ingredients in a bowl and set aside. Tip - cornstarch will settle to the bottom so make sure to stir it again before adding it to the pan'),
('Chicken_Stir_Fry',7,'Boil noodles as per package directions and set aside.'),
('Chicken_Stir_Fry',8,'Cashew nuts - add ½ tbsp oil in a wok or saute pan. Stir fry the cashew nuts until lightly toasted. Remove from the pan on a paper towel. '),
('Chicken_Stir_Fry',9,'Chicken - To the same wok or wide saute pan add another tablespoon of oil. Add the chicken pieces in a single layer. Cook for a minute then flip to the other side and cook another minute. Toss with a spatula and cook for 2 minutes more. Remove from the pan and keep warmTip - avoid tossing for the first two minutes this will give the chicken some color from the initial cooking.'),
('Chicken_Stir_Fry',10,'To the same wok or saute pan, add the remaining oil. Stir fry the onion, broccoli stems, and slices of ginger and garlic on medium-high for 2 minutes. '),
('Chicken_Stir_Fry',11,'Next, add the broccoli and 2 tbsp water. Cook on medium-high until broccoli is tenderTip - water creates steam and helps cook the broccoli quickly. '),
('Chicken_Stir_Fry',12,'Once the broccoli is almost tender return the chicken and cashews back to the pan. '),
('Chicken_Stir_Fry',13,'Season with salt and pepper. Then add the sauce and combine well. Tip - by this time both the chicken and broccoli should be cooked. The sauce will coat everything well and any juices in the pan will get thicken with the cornstarch. If necessary you can add a few tablespoons of water to help bring everything together.'),
('Chicken_Stir_Fry',14,'Taste and adjust for seasoning. Finally, add the parsley and scallions '),
('Chicken_Stir_Fry',15,'Serve hot over boiled noodles. '),
('Chicken_Wrap_with_Avocado',1,'Dressing - Combine all dressing ingredients in a bowl - set aside.'),
('Chicken_Wrap_with_Avocado',2,'Tortilla - Warm the tortilla on a skillet for 30 seconds on each side. Tip - warming the tortilla makes it softer but just 30 seconds. If you heat it too long it tends to get crisp quickly and break when you roll. '),
('Chicken_Wrap_with_Avocado',3,'Place the tortilla on a plate or sandwich wrapper. '),
('Chicken_Wrap_with_Avocado',4,'Spread a generous amount of dressing. followed by the shredded chicken, avocado, lettuce, cucumbers, and tomatoes.'),
('Chicken_Wrap_with_Avocado',5,'Season with salt and pepper. Add more dressing if you like a moist chicken wrap. '),
('Chicken_Wrap_with_Avocado',6,'Fold the wrap as shown in the video - First, fold the bottom over the ingredient firmly.- Then fold the sides over to close the filling in. - Continue to roll the wrap to the end.  '),
('Chicken_Wrap_with_Avocado',7,'You can wrap it in a sandwich wrap which keeps everything in place and makes it easier to eat. '),
('Chicken_Wrap_with_Avocado',8,'Enjoy!'),
